<node id="AIMBOM">
  <data key="d0">AIMBOM</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Model Bill of Materials (AIMBOM) is a component of the CoEvolution project intended to manage AI model descriptions and security compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;AIMBOM stands for AI Model Bill of Materials, a key concept in the CoEvolution project focusing on describing AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;AIMBOM, or AI Model Bill of Materials, is a pivotal concept introduced by CoEvolution to enhance the management of AI models within supply chains. It functions as a framework that characterizes AI models and ensures their compliance with essential standards pertaining to security, trust, and robustness. As part of the CoEvolution project, AIMBOM aims to effectively manage these models while addressing the critical needs for security and risk assessment. This innovative paradigm ultimately contributes to a more secure and compliant application of AI technologies in the supply chain ecosystem, reinforcing the importance of managing AI model descriptions and associated risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3cd6f072e1b8e8ae5414ff101a0d6b5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb9701b9fcb1c10b2c9b20f3e1b27700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb38bd592e74cfd0c261f9fdcdf9aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5704cabfb650f5e43d761190f9a6804e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a296b5c4f24ed1a5eae98b2e605e9835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-799b067a273693cb100c626ffac8631e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181669b03e4ddc55f13a32a92489775e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd182fd514d7984966c94b99cabf64e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbd9a2bb872299c973114830584e0f5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426314</data>
</node>
<node id="ICCS EREVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON">
  <data key="d0">ICCS EREVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ICCS is a research institution involved in the CoEvolution project, coordinating activities and managing contributions.&lt;SEP&gt;ICCS is the coordinator of the CoEvolution Project, responsible for overseeing the project activities as of July 2024.&lt;SEP&gt;ICCS is the coordinator of the project and is engaged in research and development in the field of systems and networks.</data>
