<node id="AI Cybersecurity Threats">
  <data key="d0">AI Cybersecurity Threats</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Cybersecurity Threats encompass the vulnerabilities and risks associated with artificial intelligence technology. These threats are characterized by their evolving nature and present significant challenges within the realm of AI, particularly regarding security vulnerabilities and risk assessment. The CoEvolution Project aims to address these AI Cybersecurity Threats through its comprehensive framework and assessment techniques, focusing on identifying and mitigating the associated risks effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9b4e4ed58eff7ae3d119d2cc4a4dc34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb9701b9fcb1c10b2c9b20f3e1b27700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a296b5c4f24ed1a5eae98b2e605e9835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de811e88e375a0427133f48114ab4084</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425823</data>
</node>
<node id="HORIZON Research and Innovation Actions">
  <data key="d0">HORIZON Research and Innovation Actions</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">HORIZON Research and Innovation Actions are European funding programs designed to support a wide range of research and innovation initiatives, including specific projects such as CoEvolution. These actions fall under the broader EU HORIZON framework, which aims to enhance research and innovation across various fields. Specifically, HORIZON Research and Innovation Actions categorizes projects like CoEvolution, which focuses on advancing research and innovation within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;HORIZON Research and Innovation Actions represents the program under which various projects, including those in AI and cybersecurity, are funded and managed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb9701b9fcb1c10b2c9b20f3e1b27700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa49b759b9aace6986ad6fa60df42057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181669b03e4ddc55f13a32a92489775e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d09c826db6cef6eb005a363f6b7421e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbd9a2bb872299c973114830584e0f5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422807</data>
</node>
<node id="HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01">
  <data key="d0">HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 is a dedicated funding initiative by the European Union (EU) aimed at fostering research and innovation projects in the realm of cybersecurity. This project is a vital part of the broader Horizon Europe initiative, focusing on addressing significant challenges associated with advancements in technology, particularly at the intersection of artificial intelligence (AI) and cybersecurity. 

As part of its objectives, HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 emphasizes innovation, technology development, validation, evaluation, and successful project outcomes. It aims to promote collaborative efforts among various stakeholders, including small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), to devise innovative solutions to contemporary cybersecurity threats.

One of the key projects funded under HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 is the CoEvolution project, officially designated as Project 101168560. CoEvolution focuses on enhancing security assurance for AI models and being proactive in creating strategies to address evolving cybersecurity challenges.

HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 is responsible for the management of financial resources, providing essential guidelines, and ensuring compliance with budget regulations critical for grant administration. Through this oversight, it facilitates successful collaboration and innovation aimed at ensuring robust cybersecurity measures in response to modern threats.

In summary, HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 is a pivotal component of the Horizon Europe framework, promoting innovative projects and cooperative research efforts centered on secure AI model development and strengthening cybersecurity preparedness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4d11e0e789971dbd47542c636e3dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46bfcb1e7800b6d1322402d2cc7c05f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee906c164033c38c47ee9b5abf0836f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-897fe30d76da92eef8ab39f6f37362da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-841013486b274ac183dbe85d18dd9731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6fbc1a3bfb993cb23f1ec5cd61622f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-955c93b159aa0cb5703c155f13b6c924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99b3cd45c7b1f82f0e5ceb4d19d8492e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03709ab50db69591a5a3696b455f47c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-672abb4b4d866c235db2385a6641554e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa3e6dafd736c20ef4b244c92ce1a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebde38c3cbda883291428373982665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b12294f744da8f2db1893e5324f5ccd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418889b13888444f1b331214c79d5c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca60b53f4fb08a71c2cabf42d2f6530&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7b908252804f7cc170638a174809eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e930d25a22cedceebd24b60e07cebcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c37b90adda874cb8932da7490275709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83c5cc0d6d218713cd2c6fd9873d16c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1087592f8aa348e94306c4850776be80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5cbf16cd814360775473b61c07db9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16ec89c88f17eab253fcbabae20f2eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a23b1d8ad6fd3128ebdb600d00c5bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7e190ff7826e647efd60e074ebf9f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fd8590e514e02237067258b84c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4490ece625d5431730795ad841da7ddd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ba5723f8c11853502f9c64b427fd38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f1982ab2664c79b22a447094fd7c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db15753633e13066899afb7067d1b475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d09c826db6cef6eb005a363f6b7421e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c94330a60dc34a0bfa60748253c8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a5bb32d295f690e6535a7cb23fa6baa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c84806ce6d96fb7e10ee2de2ef7fc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932f1546ff56a5a50a861aaa39f75771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbc421c0c6c9b08031c3d61a5013a3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-089ed2fed176c26ba2d2a44622231ee3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d11aa6e28f787c2ae7a7561e62d0a74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e115bd628f8fb0edc5eb2d730569997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909ff0598aa7c312fae851a154fae81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfb38bd592e74cfd0c261f9fdcdf9aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02286c7e1707a806f9e9959dada558a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3601f2df51a8a247b13dc91952cf725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449cdb7f2dbaf658674f7d17457a5b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81697e5e97b55f3fbdb3e229af635af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31116ac4e46d186dea94d94a7702584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7a7f20ec997cb53fbd114a846573bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc3ec14a8116e38b696429a7687340d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da85149284498fc139e8be382b981003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ae44e85d2d5dcfce82a1281830565f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0997e404b51fe3aa39a52767ed1caac5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb9701b9fcb1c10b2c9b20f3e1b27700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65321e5c497565cf717aab53e5aa7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cdadb910463745fc32934e593a1c6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4e2865d7233be2941bdb2500bc81cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8719a38bb7a9f42229f7fe81c9bf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cabeefd7ae48c25ad0cbe6631c0ecc22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5936cfdec252f012f8e0b69c534c24ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e311b0bf4e60d61a3a28a1b7cce6c4af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aed127c900f359169178e10d5facbb50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d65865b76581edf9ac1aac0de819fca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6067ea806d15eef91a8756966c65e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e809a3ce6da55906320f84dbd54cb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bbd9a2bb872299c973114830584e0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504206f0a7bf9dc2f99c1165d4800618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16332edc6609bf8b86a878abf63aec55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3431bd3a1c9c4041b4bc155e957326da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce012c5c7284b310263eb73817161dd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107384e3edcbe7422a87890a602648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c1513849fed8288aa7e5eef91460421&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8367c05350cd3e59ea1f7a290218e7e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e989c1f120fe4fad4e22404bc5b4449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-991c83168528be4a6f6d89078a6d75ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa49b759b9aace6986ad6fa60df42057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd293dc4bf55a53d90c2406f6a87c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-964065d9cfca78eacd342a9c89646e25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d40ee8239b5807a75857260b7afe44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef356bf47d4a7662b1eebd219b6efecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0299893c12de3ee2631ab3f6cf4ec2e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1079c5a2020c1fa8f7ce2c209e6097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d59b8f25e569d0889a7d7bf44bb2ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e9aa7ab49a00972f3d46c56705b630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-156a8e85a6eb2d84a8dc90300df66a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ddd092d2b8685079c5b87c6675e59f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1e6845be0998259ad41a50c2e648ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c733bc2ac52924fad86b0ae9233921f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66775d2ca4e61f236e59e3423f42a76e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426336</data>
</node>
<node id="HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01-03">
  <data key="d0">HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01-03</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01-03 is a call aimed at funding projects that contribute to enhancing security and trust in AI models and systems.&lt;SEP&gt;HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01-03 is the specific topic within the HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 call that the CoEvolution Project addresses.&lt;SEP&gt;HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01-03 is a call for proposals related to security and resilience in artificial intelligence projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ddb9ddb0c5f55caea9f52e4feaa7073c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb9701b9fcb1c10b2c9b20f3e1b27700&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3d753a5ba3bfc0d8c4ec414093b1cf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422771</data>
</node>
<node id="REVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON (ICCS)">
  <data key="d0">REVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON (ICCS)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ICCS is an organization involved in funding activities and grants, as indicated by its association with grant amounts and budgetary details.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419056</data>
</node>
<node id="Grant">
  <data key="d0">Grant</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A grant is a form of financial support provided to beneficiaries under specific conditions and guidelines, aimed at funding particular actions or projects. This support is governed by a Grant Agreement, which outlines the eligible costs and contributions required for the funding. Grants are offered by a granting authority and may be subject to recovery if the beneficiaries fail to comply with the set conditions. Additionally, in the context of the European Union, grants are often provided under framework agreements to support designated projects or actions undertaken by the beneficiaries. Non-compliance with the terms of the grant can lead to a reduction or complete revocation of the financial support.&lt;SEP&gt;The Grant refers to a financial support mechanism indicated as budget-based, with specific maximum amounts and cost eligibility options discussed in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The Grant refers to financial support being provided under specific conditions, including maximum amounts and eligible costs associated with the funding process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4d11e0e789971dbd47542c636e3dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7998d7f556fa82a3f85973da5a1f2d77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e44d77d456cfa0de0a4ae0ee65c3ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7b908252804f7cc170638a174809eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-315481829958213fce3674f0a85f2bf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0997e404b51fe3aa39a52767ed1caac5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cabeefd7ae48c25ad0cbe6631c0ecc22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424983</data>
</node>
<node id="Belgium">
  <data key="d0">Belgium</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Belgium is a country situated in Western Europe, recognized for its significant role as a legal jurisdiction, particularly regarding organizational operations and disputes. The country hosts the jurisdiction of the Courts of Brussels, which adjudicate various legal matters, especially those involving specific agreements. Belgium's legal framework is especially relevant for non-EU beneficiaries and is pivotal in the governance of agreements like the Consortium Agreement. The laws of Belgium complement European Union legislation, providing a coherent regulatory environment for addressing legal issues and disputes related to grants and financial responsibilities. This authoritative legal framework positions Belgian law as crucial for the interpretation and enforcement of agreements, ensuring clarity and support for beneficiaries of EU funding. Thus, Belgium serves both as a geographical location and a key legal jurisdiction that governs agreements and disputes within its legal environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Belgium is a country within the European Union and is mentioned in the context of legal jurisdiction for dispute settlement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9914231eecde0fb46ee3d4c21bb3e505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-884efa32a7364a4e3afb2c062c3914da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9af1226bfbc3ea69059eb3576fcaf4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8daee7887465a1bbc64f6da189934ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e9aa7ab49a00972f3d46c56705b630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b33dd17c4669f5a8bcc3fc405a6a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418889b13888444f1b331214c79d5c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e61a5cae6fe4c2cb8e2ff9868086dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c811c5c2da7facca7b18e0019c9ea9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2800fd1db09254940cc4a13a8d3cb57c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395405bf739ba7ab815c034dae49720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca56f67073468dac14fea47e10463965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425824</data>
</node>
<node id="EU General Court">
  <data key="d0">EU General Court</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The EU General Court is a judicial body operating under the jurisdiction of the European Union, primarily tasked with resolving legal disputes related to the interpretation and application of EU agreements and laws. It serves as a fundamental forum for adjudicating grievances and legal challenges brought by beneficiaries of the EU, ensuring a structured and consistent platform for dispute settlement. The court plays a critical role in effectively handling cases concerning compliance and the enforcement of EU law, thereby reinforcing its significance within the EU's judicial system.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU General Court is a judicial body that handles legal disputes involving the European Union and its beneficiaries, particularly for disputes arising under EU law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9914231eecde0fb46ee3d4c21bb3e505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-884efa32a7364a4e3afb2c062c3914da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e9aa7ab49a00972f3d46c56705b630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b33dd17c4669f5a8bcc3fc405a6a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418889b13888444f1b331214c79d5c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2800fd1db09254940cc4a13a8d3cb57c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395405bf739ba7ab815c034dae49720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e61a5cae6fe4c2cb8e2ff9868086dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425824</data>
</node>
<node id="EU Court of Justice">
  <data key="d0">EU Court of Justice</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The EU Court of Justice is the highest court in the European Union, responsible for ensuring that EU law is interpreted and applied uniformly across all member states. It serves as an appellate court that handles appeals related to decisions made by the EU General Court, particularly concerning disputes involving EU beneficiaries. The court's jurisdiction includes adjudicating appeals that arise under the EU legal framework, which is crucial for maintaining legal consistency throughout the union. By overseeing these legal processes, the EU Court of Justice upholds the integrity of EU law and plays a vital role in its enforcement within the member states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9914231eecde0fb46ee3d4c21bb3e505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-884efa32a7364a4e3afb2c062c3914da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e9aa7ab49a00972f3d46c56705b630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b33dd17c4669f5a8bcc3fc405a6a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-418889b13888444f1b331214c79d5c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2800fd1db09254940cc4a13a8d3cb57c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e61a5cae6fe4c2cb8e2ff9868086dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425826</data>
</node>
<node id="Budget Categories">
  <data key="d0">Budget Categories</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Budget Categories refer to the specific types of expenses outlined for the grant, including personnel costs, subcontracting, purchase costs, and other cost categories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419056</data>
</node>
<node id="Personnel Costs">
  <data key="d0">Personnel Costs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Personnel Costs include the expenses related to employees or equivalent/direct contracted natural persons involved in the project.&lt;SEP&gt;Personnel Costs refer to the salaries and related expenses incurred for employees, contractors, and natural persons involved in a grant project. This includes the salaries and wages of all personnel assigned to the action, subject to specific eligibility conditions. Personnel Costs also encompass all financial obligations related to those working on the project, ensuring compliance with general eligibility requirements. Furthermore, this category includes SME owners and individuals who may not receive a regular salary but fulfill the necessary eligibility criteria, as well as expenses related to direct contracts and seconded personnel. Overall, Personnel Costs represent a comprehensive overview of the costs associated with human resources engaged in the organization's activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Personnel costs refer to the portion of the project's budget allocated to staff, comprising 74% of total costs, closely tied to project activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-167b08e854bdbecae98ac74e0774cabf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a849a6c0719d6015ef6c319e7b3a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa3e6dafd736c20ef4b244c92ce1a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777c5064b9d91d9fead9d42c14884581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ae92172040335a85ccb27a77e2cf717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9722302d2df0ff82bdb9f924fc7dbf39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbc421c0c6c9b08031c3d61a5013a3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424967</data>
</node>
<node id="Subcontracting Costs">
  <data key="d0">Subcontracting Costs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Subcontracting Costs are expenses incurred by an organization when it contracts out services to third-party providers. These costs encompass the fees and expenses associated with outsourcing work that is essential for fulfilling project requirements, particularly under grants. Subcontracting Costs must comply with specific eligibility conditions and should be based on actual costs. They relate to the hiring of external parties to perform specific tasks necessary for the successful execution of projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Subcontracting Costs are expenses related to engaging third parties for services under the project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-167b08e854bdbecae98ac74e0774cabf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777c5064b9d91d9fead9d42c14884581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa3e6dafd736c20ef4b244c92ce1a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9722302d2df0ff82bdb9f924fc7dbf39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbc421c0c6c9b08031c3d61a5013a3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423139</data>
</node>
<node id="Purchase Costs">
  <data key="d0">Purchase Costs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Purchase Costs encompass the expenses associated with acquiring items, services, and works necessary for various activities within the organization. These costs are categorized under specific headings, including travel, equipment, and other essential goods. They involve expenditures aimed at fulfilling the requirements of grant activities and are crucial for the operational effectiveness of the organization. Overall, Purchase Costs represent the financial outlay for obtaining the goods and services that support the organization's projects and activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Purchase Costs refers to a category that encompasses the expenses incurred for acquiring goods and services in a project context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa3e6dafd736c20ef4b244c92ce1a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b33dd17c4669f5a8bcc3fc405a6a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425825</data>
</node>
<node id="Indirect Costs">
  <data key="d0">Indirect Costs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Indirect Costs are expenses that are essential for the overall functioning of an organization but are not directly linked to specific projects. These costs encompass overhead expenses critical for supporting the administrative infrastructure necessary for project execution while maintaining compliance with funding regulations. Indirect Costs are typically calculated as a percentage or a flat rate based on eligible direct costs, with common reimbursement structured at a flat rate of 25% of those direct costs, excluding specific costs as defined in grant terms. It is important to note that these costs are generally considered ineligible for reimbursement if they are covered by an operating grant, illustrating their unique role within the financial framework of project funding and organizational budgeting. Overall, Indirect Costs are indispensable for the organization, as they cannot be directly attributed to particular project activities, yet are necessary for the overall operation and successful execution of projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b72b3e7ba1aaeb63a98bb04479fd99ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-167b08e854bdbecae98ac74e0774cabf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9941c6cbac26f2073168a5b30c17afcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-777c5064b9d91d9fead9d42c14884581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa3e6dafd736c20ef4b244c92ce1a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ae92172040335a85ccb27a77e2cf717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0299893c12de3ee2631ab3f6cf4ec2e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f216fc14ce08511b03292fca3d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b33dd17c4669f5a8bcc3fc405a6a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4e4ed58eff7ae3d119d2cc4a4dc34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425824</data>
</node>
<node id="Mutual Insurance Mechanism (MIM)">
  <data key="d0">Mutual Insurance Mechanism (MIM)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutual Insurance Mechanism (MIM) refers to the financial system in place to support grant funding, which includes a contribution retained from the initial prefinancing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mutual Insurance Mechanism (MIM) is a financial mechanism designed to manage and mitigate financial risks associated with grant disbursement. It functions as a funding tool that retains 5% of the maximum grant amount, providing a financial buffer against potential issues that may arise during the grant process. This retention of funds is aimed at safeguarding the financial resources allocated through grants, ensuring adequate support is available if problems occur. Furthermore, the MIM plays a crucial role in the recovery processes related to grants, as it allows the granting authority to intervene when necessary. It is structured as an organizational framework that contributes a percentage of the maximum grant amounts to effectively handle financial risks, thereby reinforcing the integrity and sustainability of grant funding.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mutual Insurance Mechanism (MIM) is an organization or mechanism related to the financial management of grants, providing mutual coverage among beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ee3eb87a546ba8ada176f900494902b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b33dd17c4669f5a8bcc3fc405a6a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e44d77d456cfa0de0a4ae0ee65c3ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-315481829958213fce3674f0a85f2bf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2800fd1db09254940cc4a13a8d3cb57c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395405bf739ba7ab815c034dae49720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0796cf55497f532b00e0a5347e46781a</data>
