70cd2d0de2fb4466e3c766fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce96797e723874f84f3ba02a22d09d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc0f669cc4e2bfef891820395ef55650&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d976f2ffb8ad5255bb083a125919929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d36e00d6638001bed983791ad13038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1bbb9e746eec802a40ceda441e1c95e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daedd8cfb8dad5cd7a0132b3057fb6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef356bf47d4a7662b1eebd219b6efecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a23b1d8ad6fd3128ebdb600d00c5bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0362c884f52f6e88e18946d6287d4495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-841013486b274ac183dbe85d18dd9731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504206f0a7bf9dc2f99c1165d4800618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe06437e382ce0fa404ec6b5b10ceaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beda666afc02f488950a3cdbad5279e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107384e3edcbe7422a87890a602648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-017e7c3267b01fc259f8929e89a0b812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c94330a60dc34a0bfa60748253c8dd</data>
  <data key="d2">ICCS is a partner in the CoEvolution project with responsibilities regarding dissemination and communication.&lt;SEP&gt;The Institute of Computer Science (ICCS), officially known in Greek as EREVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON, is a prominent Greek research institution that plays a critical role in the CoEvolution project. ICCS is actively engaged in various aspects of this initiative, primarily focusing on AI security and privacy. As a participant organization, ICCS is involved in multiple tasks including architecture and adversarial attack security assessment, and it significantly contributes to the research and development of cybersecurity methodologies. 

ICCS holds a leading position in the CoEvolution project, acting as the lead beneficiary for deliverables and project management work packages, specifically WP1. They are responsible for the codification of project scope, managing deliverables, and producing essential documentation such as the Project Manual and scientific reports. Additionally, ICCS has committed an impressive 82 person-months to ensure effective security monitoring, vulnerability assessments, and risk management relative to AI systems, engaging in tasks such as AI model security, simulator development, and dataset creation.

The organization emphasizes collaborative methods by contributing its expertise to open-source projects and publications, thereby reinforcing its role within the CoEvolution consortium. ICCS's adherence to ethical standards and rigorous compliance in cybersecurity enhances its contributions to the project and facilitates effective coordination among multiple partners.

Overall, ICCS's integral position within the CoEvolution project underscores its expertise and significant involvement in advancing AI technologies and security assessments, assuring robust project implementation and management since July 6, 2024.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756144346</data>
</node>
