<node id="EREVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON">
  <data key="d0">EREVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">EREVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON is a Greek institution involved in the CoEvolution project.&lt;SEP&gt;The EREVNITIKO PANEPISTIMIAKO INSTITOUTO SYSTIMATON EPIKOINONION KAI YPOLOGISTON, commonly known as ICCS, is an academic and research institution located in Athens, Greece. It is recognized for its involvement in the fields of communication systems and computing technologies. As a significant player in the Horizon Europe project, ICCS acts as the coordinator for the CoEvolution project, demonstrating its leadership and expertise in advanced research. The institution not only contributes to but also benefits from the CoEvolution initiative, reflecting its dedication to promoting knowledge and innovation in its specialized areas of study. Furthermore, ICCS is noted as a coordinating body for grants starting from July 6, 2024, emphasizing its role in facilitating research funding and collaboration within the academic and research community.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9e989c1f120fe4fad4e22404bc5b4449&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d16a55d1d3dc5f1ef6966990760ab1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0595846d444fbd08dfeeed4f13a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf164c706b7b264b8973737a16cc2a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c996e92a321a548b9762f96a234cf48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc2a026cf3ae3a1dbeb730bf3d668f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ceb7cbd40f9a45f01986a8223d768e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667986d4a34f30cf5bfa22415edc5c10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e44d77d456cfa0de0a4ae0ee65c3ebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd16c3e5393576d245d512c360865185&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fd8590e514e02237067258b84c6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf2425f890b3ae59f4929d1cd4a0994</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426201</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CoEvolution is a collaborative research initiative and consortium dedicated to enhancing the security, trust, and robustness of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies. It operates under the HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 program, with grant agreement number 101168560. The primary mission of CoEvolution is to develop effective methods and tools for assessing and strengthening the safety and resilience of AI models against adversarial threats, such as data poisoning and adversarial attacks, while ensuring compliance with essential European Union regulations, including the EU Artificial Intelligence Act and the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

The initiative aims to create a comprehensive framework for secure, interconnected AI solutions by integrating security, trust, and robustness assessments, and focuses on developing security assessment tools for AI to address critical issues such as data bias and adversarial attacks on datasets. To foster innovation, CoEvolution emphasizes collaboration among experts in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM), and establishes partnerships among industry leaders, researchers, and policymakers to drive communal learning and ethical standards in AI development.

CoEvolution employs a Bills-of-Materials (BOM) approach to provide detailed security-related information, enhancing the resilience and lifecycle management of AI systems, with a focus on context awareness for improved adaptive security. Additionally, it engages in peer-to-peer learning through a system called P4L (Peer for Learning) to address privacy and collective learning challenges. The project also incorporates gender-specific considerations to enhance innovation, equality, and compliance with European regulations.

Key activities of CoEvolution include organizing industrial exhibitions and workshops aimed at raising awareness and promoting synergy within the AI community. The consortium is committed to establishing a comprehensive risk analysis and security assessment framework, standardizing threat models and protection profiles to tackle critical AI security risks. Moreover, CoEvolution focuses on promoting sustainable strategies for exploiting research results while enhancing network systems through context-aware learning frameworks.

In summary, CoEvolution is dedicated to developing innovative solutions for a secure and trusted AI environment by engaging various stakeholders through events, pilot studies, and feedback mechanisms. The initiative targets adversarial threats and vulnerabilities across multiple applications, particularly in the industrial and automotive sectors. By emphasizing compliance with regulatory frameworks and the integration of principled models with data-driven techniques, CoEvolution aims to significantly enhance the security, privacy, and robustness of AI models throughout their lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;CoEvolution is a project focused on communication and dissemination strategies to maximize its relevance and impact throughout its lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;CoEvolution is a project focused on enhancing adversarial robustness and security in AI systems, aiming to improve the trustworthiness of AI technologies.</data>
