<node id="Mutual Insurance Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Mutual Insurance Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Mutual Insurance Mechanism is a financial arrangement and instrument utilized by the European Union to manage funding distributions according to the Consortium Agreement. Its primary purpose is to oversee payments and offsets owed to beneficiaries while safeguarding against financial risks associated with project funding. This mechanism serves as a financial safety net aimed at mitigating risks for beneficiaries involved in EU-funded projects.

In addition to its role in financial management, the Mutual Insurance Mechanism retains certain funds for specific regulatory purposes and plays a crucial part in the recovery process by intervening to support beneficiaries in cases of debts, provided certain conditions are met. It is also referenced in the context of interventions by the granting authority for recovery purposes. Overall, the Mutual Insurance Mechanism contributes to the overall financing related to grant payments, ensuring effective financial management and assistance for those involved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e00a4e19d0d0ff1473ebdef441a1463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-897fe30d76da92eef8ab39f6f37362da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153d0d25b1dc6cfa0bcf7a7947b40d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6587c0a38b949dea5de8a236e80407fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83c5cc0d6d218713cd2c6fd9873d16c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-340cab0aeae7a8a4e864f5fb97fb2b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e1fb202d9cabb7b747aef687ac4527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd16c3e5393576d245d512c360865185&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cabeefd7ae48c25ad0cbe6631c0ecc22</data>
