<node id="Defaulting Party">
  <data key="d0">Defaulting Party</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Defaulting Party is defined as a member of a consortium who has been identified as failing to meet its obligations under either the Consortium Agreement or the Grant Agreement. This designation is typically conferred by the General Assembly, and it applies to any party that breaches its commitments. The consequences of being labeled a Defaulting Party include restrictions on voting rights, penalties, or even removal from the consortium. 

The breach of obligations by a Defaulting Party not only affects their own rights but can also lead to the cessation of Access Rights, which has significant financial implications, potentially impacting payment entitlements. In summary, a Defaulting Party is any participant within the consortium that has been declared in breach, resulting in various repercussions, including additional costs for other consortium members and the immediate termination of access rights upon notification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27907e0f1cca34615e2743e211e3915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc042244536a2c477c732ec854a8e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f271cb21c3e352192b6e5d9f263eec2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876d5a07d8e572ddca68ea75a19f396f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-163e8dfb11222dec22dc86de3c28a3b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2804b4b4d78b4e8ad4bf46a4086bc654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f737a86267a87605168fd1ae879e6180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87403324e3568e1b98a5a74b67704968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2e8770375019a8ec84b226fe246ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561ef15ef8c11dbe41ee0269571778b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad85c72a1fdaf22b42cfab6d99532ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924177c0e0f362a235f652bd1017e028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419437</data>
</node>
<node id="Obligation to Implement Action Tasks">
  <data key="d0">Obligation to Implement Action Tasks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Obligation to Implement Action Tasks refers to the requirement for all parties to execute their designated roles and responsibilities within the Project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8c12a8ce9dbccebc341927add84979a3</data>
