  <data key="d5">1755422087</data>
</node>
<node id="Extraordinary Meeting">
  <data key="d0">Extraordinary Meeting</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">An Extraordinary Meeting refers to a special convening of the General Assembly that allows for discussions and decisions outside the regular meeting schedule, typically called for urgent matters.&lt;SEP&gt;An Extraordinary Meeting refers to a special meeting convened by the General Assembly to discuss urgent matters not covered in ordinary meetings.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-876d5a07d8e572ddca68ea75a19f396f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1fd5d76650ba686326c9347bd47e69a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419435</data>
</node>
<node id="Voting Rules">
  <data key="d0">Voting Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Voting Rules define the procedures by which decisions are made during meetings, including quorum requirements and the process for voting on agenda items.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-876d5a07d8e572ddca68ea75a19f396f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419175</data>
</node>
<node id="Veto Rights">
  <data key="d0">Veto Rights</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Veto Rights refers to the authority of a Party to oppose decisions that may negatively impact its legitimate interests as defined in the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-876d5a07d8e572ddca68ea75a19f396f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419175</data>
</node>
<node id="Teleconference">
  <data key="d0">Teleconference</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Teleconference refers to meetings that are conducted using telecommunications technology, allowing members to participate remotely.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-876d5a07d8e572ddca68ea75a19f396f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419175</data>
</node>
<node id="Access Rights">
  <data key="d0">Access Rights</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Access Rights define the conditions under which results or background information can be utilized by various parties involved in a project. These rights encompass the permissions granted for the exploitation of results, including specific provisions for research and sublicensing. Access Rights are crucial for implementing the project, as they delineate the entitlements regarding the use and exploitation of project results and background data, as specified in both the Grant Agreement and the Consortium Agreement.

Access Rights specify the permissions for utilizing each other's results or background knowledge, regulating the usage and distribution of information and resources among the parties involved in the consortium framework. They cover the permissions concerning the use of data, know-how, and information essential for effective project execution. Consequently, Access Rights serve as a foundational element governing the collaborative efforts and resource utilization among the participating entities, significantly impacting their collaboration and overall project dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f27907e0f1cca34615e2743e211e3915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2e8770375019a8ec84b226fe246ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364ff6bf933fe0af2f8dba4b5fab5748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f4d0db61ea04c6dd99be408590bb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24642f1f9525ded7b8b36983c7df32bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9958663eec02e383c065626a74bfdabd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc736562ef02e369a2653a250fd668b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad85c72a1fdaf22b42cfab6d99532ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-496ff2c08e0ff26b59002ce18b9a5411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445008e17e64c0438134e1fefbcf5dfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87403324e3568e1b98a5a74b67704968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c12a8ce9dbccebc341927add84979a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cbcc5a33a538807285883f44a32ffd6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420827</data>
</node>
<node id="Written Notice">
  <data key="d0">Written Notice</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Written Notice refers to the formal communication required to provide information or notification among members regarding decisions and agenda items.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-876d5a07d8e572ddca68ea75a19f396f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419175</data>
</node>
<node id="Members">
  <data key="d0">Members</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Members are parties involved in the Consortium Agreement, responsible for decisions and actions during meetings.&lt;SEP&gt;Members are the participants of the consortium who attend meetings, vote on decisions, and have a role in the governance of the organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Members refer to parties involved in the General Assembly and project, responsible for contributing to the decision-making process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-163e8dfb11222dec22dc86de3c28a3b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561ef15ef8c11dbe41ee0269571778b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53de78ee256314f49b2496da2bf2ac29</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419435</data>
</node>
<node id="Background in Attachment 1">
  <data key="d0">Background in Attachment 1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Background in Attachment 1 refers to the foundational information and context related to the project outlined in the Consortium Agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-561ef15ef8c11dbe41ee0269571778b5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419175</data>
</node>
<node id="Attachment 3">
  <data key="d0">Attachment 3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Attachment 3 is a component of the Consortium Agreement that contains a comprehensive list of third parties involved in the simplified transfer of project outputs. This list is aligned with specific provisions outlined in the agreement, specifically regarding the potential ownership transfer of project Results. The document is structured to facilitate the identification of these third parties, as referenced in Section 8.3.2 of the Consortium Agreement. Overall, Attachment 3 plays a crucial role in streamlining the process of transferring project outputs to the identified third parties as per the established guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Attachment 3 lists Third Parties for simplified transfer according to the Grant Agreement, which is part of the project's operational framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Attachment 3 refers to a specific section in the Consortium Agreement where parties can identify third parties for transferring ownership of results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9af1226bfbc3ea69059eb3576fcaf4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53de78ee256314f49b2496da2bf2ac29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45c41aa4c4e38dda43fae0f22b2c010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87403324e3568e1b98a5a74b67704968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2e8770375019a8ec84b226fe246ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561ef15ef8c11dbe41ee0269571778b5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419436</data>
</node>
<node id="Granting Authority's Financial Contribution">
  <data key="d0">Granting Authority's Financial Contribution</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Granting Authority's Financial Contribution pertains to the funding provided for the Project as outlined in the Consortium Plan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d70be6cc96049933abcbd5d9cfc8374</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419175</data>
</node>
<node id="Affiliated Entities">
  <data key="d0">Affiliated Entities</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Affiliated Entities refer to organizations or individuals that have a connection to a main entity involved in a project. These entities are often related to beneficiaries and may be held liable for repaying debts if required by the granting authority. They participate in the project alongside the main entity and share financial responsibilities as detailed in the Consortium Agreement. Affiliated Entities play specific roles and may include third parties or organizations that maintain obligations related to the project. Additionally, they may incur costs that are justified under the Consortium Plan, reflecting their active involvement and association with the primary entity in the context of the project. Overall, Affiliated Entities are essential participants in the implementation of the action as defined in the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e293777d71c3ca9709a65d86e40e18b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc042244536a2c477c732ec854a8e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e00a4e19d0d0ff1473ebdef441a1463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46bfcb1e7800b6d1322402d2cc7c05f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d70be6cc96049933abcbd5d9cfc8374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e1fb202d9cabb7b747aef687ac4527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2804b4b4d78b4e8ad4bf46a4086bc654</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422072</data>
</node>
<node id="Payment Schedule">
  <data key="d0">Payment Schedule</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Payment Schedule outlines the timeline and procedures for transferring funds to the Parties involved in the Project according to the Grant Agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d70be6cc96049933abcbd5d9cfc8374</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419175</data>
</node>
<node id="Coordinator">
  <data key="d0">Coordinator</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Coordinator is a crucial individual or entity tasked with overseeing and managing grant activities and submissions on behalf of the beneficiaries involved in a project. This role encompasses several key responsibilities, primarily serving as the representative responsible for submitting requests related to the assignment of claims and ensuring effective communication between the beneficiaries and the granting authority.

As the vital intermediary between the parties within a consortium and the Granting Authority, the Coordinator plays a multifaceted role essential for the project's success. This includes monitoring compliance with both the Consortium Agreement and the Grant Agreement, which entails ensuring all parties fulfill their obligations. The Coordinator prepares meetings, manages financial contributions, and oversees payments to the involved parties while maintaining strict adherence to the agreed-upon terms.

In addition to administrative tasks, the Coordinator facilitates communication and decision-making processes among consortium members, which includes circulating proposed decisions, updating members on voting outcomes, and managing the overarching administrative and financial components of the project in alignment with the Consortium Plan. The Coordinator is authorized to withhold payments if obligations under the agreements are not met, reinforcing accountability among all parties involved.

In summary, the Coordinator is integral to the smooth operation and oversight of the project, ensuring effective interactions between project partners and the Granting Authority while maintaining compliance with all established agreements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e00a4e19d0d0ff1473ebdef441a1463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-884efa32a7364a4e3afb2c062c3914da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-163e8dfb11222dec22dc86de3c28a3b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0997e404b51fe3aa39a52767ed1caac5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561ef15ef8c11dbe41ee0269571778b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2804b4b4d78b4e8ad4bf46a4086bc654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87403324e3568e1b98a5a74b67704968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8eaae213c278ba06a759f0d91e6d71c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2e8770375019a8ec84b226fe246ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc042244536a2c477c732ec854a8e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925b1f5a2133d1fdc125c610bbbae027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d70be6cc96049933abcbd5d9cfc8374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db0d8aa15d17a4b672a2dd3371a4ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1fd5d76650ba686326c9347bd47e69a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53de78ee256314f49b2496da2bf2ac29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45c41aa4c4e38dda43fae0f22b2c010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876d5a07d8e572ddca68ea75a19f396f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924177c0e0f362a235f652bd1017e028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422097</data>
</node>
<node id="Beneficiary">
  <data key="d0">Beneficiary</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Beneficiary is defined as either an individual or an entity that is entitled to receive payments under a Grant Agreement. To be eligible for funding from the Granting Authority, a Beneficiary must sign the Consortium Agreement and comply with various obligations outlined in both the Consortium and Grant Agreements. Beneficiaries engage in diverse capacities, primarily receiving financial contributions from the European Union (EU) for their project activities.

These entities are obligated to adhere to several regulations regarding their financial and operational conduct, as specified in the agreements. Importantly, Beneficiaries are responsible for the potential repayment of funds if required and must notify the granting authority of any changes involving transfers of ownership or licensing related to the grant.

In summary, the term Beneficiary encapsulates those who receive financial support, with the understanding that they must implement the project according to the grant's conditions and fulfill their designated responsibilities. Overall, Beneficiaries are mandated to maintain compliance with specific financial reporting requirements as set forth by the granting authority while actively participating in executing the approved actions of their respective projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0997e404b51fe3aa39a52767ed1caac5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f209ba7faab244fa0ec2f617b5183fda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925b1f5a2133d1fdc125c610bbbae027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d3c3eaedec46daebd343527b0c0d92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2e8770375019a8ec84b226fe246ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8719a38bb7a9f42229f7fe81c9bf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee906c164033c38c47ee9b5abf0836f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e901df4ec4c380c4f63b0cd3f4cc859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e1fb202d9cabb7b747aef687ac4527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-340cab0aeae7a8a4e864f5fb97fb2b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce05917392d14a6ff1f6d80ad2f3e51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87403324e3568e1b98a5a74b67704968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddc1f667d5d7b593ff074f4172cecd6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cabeefd7ae48c25ad0cbe6631c0ecc22</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422094</data>
</node>
<node id="Ownership of Results">
  <data key="d0">Ownership of Results</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ownership of Results refers to the rights and management related to the outputs generated by the project, as specified in the agreements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419176</data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Ownership">
  <data key="d0">Joint Ownership</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint Ownership is a category describing the situation where two or more parties share ownership of results that have been generated collectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419176</data>
</node>
<node id="Transfer of Results">
  <data key="d0">Transfer of Results</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfer of Results details the procedures by which ownership of results can be passed from one party to another, following specific guidelines in the agreements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419176</data>
</node>
<node id="Attachment (3)">
  <data key="d0">Attachment (3)</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">Attachment (3) refers to a section of the Consortium Agreement where parties can identify third parties for potential transfer of ownership.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419176</data>
</node>
<node id="Parties">
  <data key="d0">Parties</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The term "Parties" refers to the entities or organizations that are involved in the Consortium Agreement of the CoEvolution project. These Parties contribute to the project by participating in specific tasks and justifying associated costs. They are collectively responsible for adhering to the terms outlined in the agreement, which details their rights and obligations. The Parties consist of both individuals and organizations that have entered into this consortium agreement, each having defined roles within the collaboration. Additionally, the Parties are bound by the terms of a Grant Agreement and are involved in provisions related to dissemination and confidentiality concerning their results or background knowledge. Overall, the Parties represent the diverse organizations and entities that engage in agreements pertinent to the project's objectives and goals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6599f093b4ec88ee5238eadeb9162efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b31cd9f391e84711dd5b3744b4d008a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e00a4e19d0d0ff1473ebdef441a1463&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c19c865a25591ddde6bd157a82d4494a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364ff6bf933fe0af2f8dba4b5fab5748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aeb98f7220f8ac33b9ea96243f02f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a48cfc1f38ba5b30413053bbdefda5ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-496ff2c08e0ff26b59002ce18b9a5411</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419439</data>
</node>
<node id="Results">
  <data key="d0">Results</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Results refer to the outcomes of the action, which include any data, knowledge, or information generated as part of the Agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Results refer to the outcomes or deliverables produced from collaborative projects undertaken by the parties involved, typically governed by a consortium agreement and a Grant Agreement. These results encompass the findings and outputs generated through various project activities and are subject to specific access rights and exploitation conditions as detailed in the relevant agreements. Access rights dictate how these results can be utilized, ensuring that they are made available to project partners according to predefined conditions. Additionally, the ownership and management of the results are clearly specified in these agreements, promoting clarity regarding the distribution and utilization of the generated outputs. Overall, the results reflect the collaborative efforts and technological advancements achieved throughout the project's duration, highlighting the importance of the collective contributions of all parties involved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f27907e0f1cca34615e2743e211e3915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b31cd9f391e84711dd5b3744b4d008a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2e8770375019a8ec84b226fe246ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364ff6bf933fe0af2f8dba4b5fab5748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72b68418a8ead942187d57bc3764f34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f4d0db61ea04c6dd99be408590bb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22cbe105bf419f163813e1e4122e6db8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a48cfc1f38ba5b30413053bbdefda5ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23bb168a6eb96b8932c2abd02b87a7b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-496ff2c08e0ff26b59002ce18b9a5411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87403324e3568e1b98a5a74b67704968&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420997</data>
</node>
<node id="Confidential Information">
  <data key="d0">Confidential Information</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Confidential Information encompasses any data that is disclosed between parties in the consortium, requiring careful handling and protection under the agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential Information encompasses any sensitive information shared during the project that is explicitly marked as confidential or sensitive. This includes sensitive data belonging to the objecting Party, which cannot be disseminated without prior approval. Furthermore, Confidential Information refers to any information designated as confidential or sensitive during collaboration and is protected under specific obligations outlined in the agreement. It is essential that this sensitive data is handled with care and only disclosed with the necessary consent, as specified in the Consortium Agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidential Information includes any sensitive data disclosed during the project, marked as confidential by the parties involved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6599f093b4ec88ee5238eadeb9162efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8daee7887465a1bbc64f6da189934ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364ff6bf933fe0af2f8dba4b5fab5748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aeb98f7220f8ac33b9ea96243f02f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a48cfc1f38ba5b30413053bbdefda5ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-496ff2c08e0ff26b59002ce18b9a5411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c811c5c2da7facca7b18e0019c9ea9e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419438</data>
</node>
<node id="Attachment 1">
  <data key="d0">Attachment 1</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">Attachment 1 serves as a crucial document within the framework of the Consortium Agreement, providing comprehensive background information pertinent to the Project. It outlines the agreed-upon Access Rights associated with the Background relevant to the consortium's obligations as stipulated in the Grant Agreement. Furthermore, Attachment 1 specifically identifies a section of the document where the involved parties have collaboratively recognized and consented to the Background necessary for advancing the Project. This consolidated information underscores the foundational aspects crucial for the consortium's operations and responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9af1226bfbc3ea69059eb3576fcaf4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-364ff6bf933fe0af2f8dba4b5fab5748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b31cd9f391e84711dd5b3744b4d008a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53de78ee256314f49b2496da2bf2ac29</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419438</data>
</node>
<node id="Entities under the same control">
  <data key="d0">Entities under the same control</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Entities under the same control refer to organizations or parties that share control and governance, allowing them to share Access Rights as defined in the agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Entities under the same control refers to organizations or individuals that operate under common governance and are involved in the project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9aeb98f7220f8ac33b9ea96243f02f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad85c72a1fdaf22b42cfab6d99532ee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419438</data>
</node>
<node id="Non-defaulting Party">
  <data key="d0">Non-defaulting Party</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Non-defaulting Party is a consortium member who voluntarily leaves the project with the consent of other parties and retains certain access rights until termination.&lt;SEP&gt;The Non-defaulting Party refers to a consortium member that continues to fulfill its obligations while another party defaults.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f27907e0f1cca34615e2743e211e3915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad85c72a1fdaf22b42cfab6d99532ee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419437</data>
</node>
<node id="Controlled Licence Terms">
  <data key="d0">Controlled Licence Terms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Controlled Licence Terms are provisions that govern the access and use of software and other project results.&lt;SEP&gt;Controlled Licence Terms refer to the specific conditions under which software and other intellectual properties can be accessed, used, and shared among parties within the context of the project.&lt;SEP&gt;Controlled Licence Terms define specific legal conditions under which software and results are accessed and used within the project context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9aeb98f7220f8ac33b9ea96243f02f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6599f093b4ec88ee5238eadeb9162efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a48cfc1f38ba5b30413053bbdefda5ec</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419438</data>
</node>
<node id="Courts of Brussels">
  <data key="d0">Courts of Brussels</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Courts of Brussels are judicial institutions located in Belgium that serve as the designated forum for resolving disputes arising from the Consortium Agreement, particularly when such disputes cannot be settled amicably. They specifically cater to non-EU beneficiaries involved in the agreement and may handle cases tied to EU court judgments relevant to these beneficiaries. As local courts, the Courts of Brussels play a significant role within the legal framework established for non-EU beneficiaries, ensuring that their disputes are addressed within the context of Belgian law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9af1226bfbc3ea69059eb3576fcaf4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395405bf739ba7ab815c034dae49720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9914231eecde0fb46ee3d4c21bb3e505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e61a5cae6fe4c2cb8e2ff9868086dc8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424987</data>
</node>
<node id="Recipient">
  <data key="d0">Recipient</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Recipient is a party involved in the CoEvolution Consortium Agreement, responsible for handling confidential information according to the terms of the agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Recipient is a party required to handle Confidential Information in accordance with the terms outlined in the Consortium Agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Recipient refers to individuals or entities receiving Confidential Information and is obligated to protect it according to the Consortium Agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9af1226bfbc3ea69059eb3576fcaf4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8daee7887465a1bbc64f6da189934ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c811c5c2da7facca7b18e0019c9ea9e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419439</data>
</node>
<node id="Disclosing Party">
  <data key="d0">Disclosing Party</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Disclosing Party is an entity that shares Confidential Information with the Recipient and is involved in protecting the confidentiality of that information.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disclosing Party is the individual or entity that provides Confidential Information to the Recipient under the terms set out in the Consortium Agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disclosing Party refers to any party that shares confidential information within the context of the CoEvolution Consortium Agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9af1226bfbc3ea69059eb3576fcaf4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8daee7887465a1bbc64f6da189934ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c811c5c2da7facca7b18e0019c9ea9e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419439</data>
</node>
<node id="Attachment 2">
  <data key="d0">Attachment 2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Attachment 2 includes terms and conditions agreed upon by the parties involved in the Grant Agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Attachment 2 is the document related to the accession of new parties to the Consortium Agreement, stipulating the conditions for their participation.&lt;SEP&gt;Attachment 2 of the Consortium Agreement is referred to as the Accession document that outlines terms for adding parties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb5e441f8c44c114214f8184f4a2b10a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9af1226bfbc3ea69059eb3576fcaf4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53de78ee256314f49b2496da2bf2ac29</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419436</data>
</node>
<node id="ATHINA-EREVNITIKO KENTRO KAINOTOMIAS STIS TECHNOLOGIES TIS PLIROFORIAS, TON EPIKOINONION KAI TIS GNOSIS">
  <data key="d0">ATHINA-EREVNITIKO KENTRO KAINOTOMIAS STIS TECHNOLOGIES TIS PLIROFORIAS, TON EPIKOINONION KAI TIS GNOSIS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The ATHINA-EREVNITIKO KENTRO KAINOTOMIAS STIS TECHNOLOGIES TIS PLIROFORIAS, TON EPIKOINONION KAI TIS GNOSIS, commonly known as ISI, is an organization situated in Maroussi, Greece, dedicated to innovation in the fields of information technology and communications. It engages in cutting-edge research and development, focusing on the advancement of knowledge and innovative technologies. As a participant in the CoEvolution project, ISI contributes to collaborative efforts aimed at enhancing technology research and implementation. Through its initiatives, ISI plays a significant role in the evolution of information technologies, positioning itself as a key player in the innovation landscape.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb0595846d444fbd08dfeeed4f13a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c996e92a321a548b9762f96a234cf48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf2425f890b3ae59f4929d1cd4a0994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667986d4a34f30cf5bfa22415edc5c10</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419442</data>
</node>
<node id="Antonio Guzmán Sacristán">
  <data key="d0">Antonio Guzmán Sacristán</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Antonio Guzmán Sacristán is a legal representative for TELEFONICA INNOVACION DIGITAL SL, involved in the signing of the CoEvolution Consortium Agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Antonio Guzmán Sacristán is identified as a legal representative associated with Telefonica Innovacion Digital SL.&lt;SEP&gt;Antonio Guzmán Sacristán is noted as a legal representative for TELEFONICA INNOVACION DIGITAL SL.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5eb0595846d444fbd08dfeeed4f13a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c996e92a321a548b9762f96a234cf48a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-667986d4a34f30cf5bfa22415edc5c10</data>
