<node id="IMT">
  <data key="d0">IMT</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">IMT (Institut Mines-Télécom) is a distinguished French higher education institution that focuses on technology and telecommunications. Originally, IMT played a crucial role as a research partner in the CoEvolution project, significantly contributing to areas such as artificial intelligence (AI) and the development, evaluation, and implementation of security techniques. IMT's expertise was instrumental in supporting the PlanIoT framework and effectively managing sensor data. The organization was involved in various project tasks, particularly in architecture definition, collaborative research, and the development of context-aware AI resilience technologies.

However, due to changes in leadership, IMT withdrew from the CoEvolution project consortium. This decision led to the reassignment of its responsibilities, including deliverable D6.2, to the University of Patras (UPatras). The withdrawal was characterized as a strategic adaptation among project partners rather than a sign of failure, and IMT continued to be acknowledged as a beneficiary despite its formal exit. Its foundational contributions remain influential within the project, especially impacting the work of UPatras.

While IMT was responsible for overseeing project management tasks, including budget oversight and the development of a minimum viable product (MVP) for the integrated framework, specific financial disclosures about its activities were not provided in detail. Nevertheless, IMT has been listed in the financial reports of the CoEvolution project, signaling its status as a lead beneficiary.

In summary, IMT was a vital participant in the CoEvolution project, engaging in various capacities related to cybersecurity, architecture, and deliverable management. Even after its departure, IMT's contributions continue to uphold the project's integrity and operational framework, leaving a lasting legacy in the field of sensor data management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16332edc6609bf8b86a878abf63aec55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a849a6c0719d6015ef6c319e7b3a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6a0f23e95fea1a56df838e0e512fb24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc2a026cf3ae3a1dbeb730bf3d668f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16ec89c88f17eab253fcbabae20f2eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd182fd514d7984966c94b99cabf64e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9439f586c1b31de13fd7c269ff9fb63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4810c9b22b0ce26c963075600f4dbd84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c090092136e198b11011668061264f99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932990ed344e37eccd1a99284c64597c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0362c884f52f6e88e18946d6287d4495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fb0f79a7142225a7d2dfaedc44c958&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f1982ab2664c79b22a447094fd7c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd293dc4bf55a53d90c2406f6a87c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe06437e382ce0fa404ec6b5b10ceaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d40ee8239b5807a75857260b7afe44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc736562ef02e369a2653a250fd668b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf2425f890b3ae59f4929d1cd4a0994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c8a90d0356b7b59238f88457856e99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-672abb4b4d866c235db2385a6641554e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d2ff0e7582f72b15822c3c3392a6345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1840a2aa861c08b15185d927867134a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa3e6dafd736c20ef4b244c92ce1a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9958663eec02e383c065626a74bfdabd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d976f2ffb8ad5255bb083a125919929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91306f86deee226d4e904fb6737b7337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e930d25a22cedceebd24b60e07cebcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2c4aae27b4457d3ffe0ecb38813ebd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3b7d48470cd2d0de2fb4466e3c766fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8bb95ba3048fe4ba1a028477aaf2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827c0e1b05bc9eac5d2bbfb266ef6562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6067ea806d15eef91a8756966c65e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f2e8aebdfb355f313ea068cac55423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-017e7c3267b01fc259f8929e89a0b812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8830be99a56abf88963043f2ab9507b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daedd8cfb8dad5cd7a0132b3057fb6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f0e52ffd2cfc0cefb2f4e79d13f201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e809a3ce6da55906320f84dbd54cb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad8c45296704b976d9974fb6ccbcc41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c85ec84436942dd8fc56f3409a58ac9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911f0045819caa0ee2d858aae2c793ce</data>
