<node id="Unica">
  <data key="d0">Unica</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Unica is the legal abbreviation for the UNIVERSITA DEGLI STUDI DI CAGLIARI, participating in the CoEvolution project as a beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdf2425f890b3ae59f4929d1cd4a0994</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419291</data>
</node>
<node id="SIE">
  <data key="d0">SIE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SIE is one of the organizations contributing to the CoEvolution project, participating in dissemination efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;SIE, formally known as Siemens Aktiengesellschaft, is a significant industrial partner participating in the CoEvolution project, where it plays a crucial role in advancing artificial intelligence (AI) and cybersecurity initiatives. Within the CoEvolution consortium, SIE is actively involved in developing strategies for AI security and robustness, revealing its commitment to addressing vulnerabilities and creating essential security measures for AI systems. 

As the lead beneficiary for deliverable D6.3, SIE focuses on the final integrated framework and prototypes and is responsible for task 6.3, which entails pilot deployment, testing, and demonstration of these prototypes. In addition to its leadership role in deliverables, SIE contributes to various work packages, engages in exploitation activities, and organizes training sessions for internal stakeholders, ensuring the uptake of project findings throughout the larger organization and among partners involved in CoEvolution.

SIE's multifaceted involvement in the project includes gathering technological and industrial requirements for various use cases and participating in training activities to enhance knowledge and skills related to project outcomes. The organization is also engaged in the Continuous Post-Deployment Defence project, solidifying its commitment to continuous improvements in AI security.

Further showcasing its dedication to innovation, SIE is involved in patent filing practices to protect new inventions and effectively manage project resources. The organization has committed a substantial 38 person-months in developing demonstrator deliverables, highlighting its significant contributions to project management and resource allocation. Overall, SIE’s extensive participation underscores its leadership position within the CoEvolution project and its unwavering dedication to enhancing security and resilience within the AI landscape.</data>
