<node id="AEGIS">
  <data key="d0">AEGIS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">AEGIS IT Research GmbH is a prominent German research and consultancy firm that plays a vital role as the lead beneficiary in the CoEvolution project. The organization is instrumental in the project's initiation, taking charge of Milestone 1 and overseeing critical deliverables focused on innovation management, ethical oversight, and essential data management reports that are crucial for the project's success.

Within the CoEvolution project, AEGIS leads Task 6.1, which is dedicated to the integration and implementation of the CoEvolution hub. The firm adopts a proactive approach to outreach planning, communication, and dissemination efforts, striving to raise awareness among diverse stakeholders about the project's results. Furthermore, AEGIS is committed to upholding high European standards and contributes to innovation tracking and ensuring ethical compliance, particularly concerning the development and application of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies.

In addition to leading Task 6.1, AEGIS is actively engaged in other project tasks, including Tasks 3.4 and 5.1, where it focuses on defining, designing, and managing AI model bills of materials (MBOM) and security frameworks. The organization has dedicated a total of 68 person-months across its work packages, reflecting its strong commitment to effective resource management. AEGIS receives substantial support from SAP, which includes the assignment of 12 project managers and additional resources to enhance its capacity within the CoEvolution framework.

AEGIS is also involved in conducting security and risk assessments for AI models and engaging in cybersecurity research to advance AI security standards and resilience. As one of the seven small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) in the CoEvolution consortium, AEGIS takes on leadership roles in various project tasks while collaborating with consortium partners to disseminate findings and provide training activities.

In summary, AEGIS IT Research GmbH is recognized for its collaborative leadership and significant contributions to AI research initiatives within the CoEvolution project. The organization is responsible for providing tools, content, and structure for project documentation, as well as managing dissemination activities, communication strategies, and key performance indicators, while actively participating in and supporting multiple aspects of the project's overall mission to facilitate technological advancements in AI.</data>
