<node id="UNIPI">
  <data key="d0">UNIPI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">UNIPI is a contributing partner in the CoEvolution project, responsible for certain tasks and activities.&lt;SEP&gt;UNIPI, officially known as Università di Pisa, is a prominent Italian university that plays a significant role in advancing cybersecurity and the robustness of artificial intelligence (AI) models. As a key beneficiary organization in the CoEvolution project, UNIPI contributes to various aspects of the initiative, including research focused on developing novel training techniques aimed at enhancing the security and robustness of AI models. It participates actively across multiple work packages and specific tasks, notably leading Task 4.5, which is dedicated to incrementally training AI models to strengthen their security.

Within the framework of the CoEvolution project, UNIPI's contributions include analyzing threat models, creating effective security engines for risk management, and implementing context-aware adaptation strategies. The university is also engaged in establishing continuous post-deployment defense strategies and exploring innovative learning techniques to improve security measures.

In addition to its technical endeavors, UNIPI is recognized for its strong commitment to open-source practices, which strengthens its influence within the CoEvolution consortium and the wider research community. The university is responsible for resource management and project cost estimation, showcasing its dedication to the financial and operational success of the project.

Furthermore, UNIPI leads several initiatives beyond CoEvolution, such as Avalanche, HEU-EMERGE, and AI-Toolkit, all designed to propel advancements in cybersecurity and AI learning. Through these extensive efforts, UNIPI not only drives the objectives of the CoEvolution project forward but also establishes itself as a pivotal entity in the field of AI security research.</data>
