<node id="AVI">
  <data key="d0">AVI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">AVI is a partner organization in the CoEvolution project, assisting with dissemination and communication tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;AVI, also known as AviSense.AI Technovlastos IKE, is a pivotal organization in the CoEvolution project, where it serves as a lead beneficiary. AVI plays a central role in various tasks and is responsible for key deliverables, notably D6.1 and D6.2, which involve the development of simulators and datasets crucial for enhancing the perception capabilities of autonomous vehicles. As the leader of Work Package 6 (WP6), AVI focuses on integration, evaluation, and project outcomes, demonstrating its commitment to the project's objectives with a substantial allocation of resources amounting to 58 person-months.

Within the CoEvolution framework, one of AVI's significant responsibilities includes leading Task 4.1, which centers on adversarial attack security assessment techniques aimed at strengthening AI security for connected and autonomous vehicles (CAV). This role underscores AVI's important contribution to establishing a sophisticated testing infrastructure, particularly through collaborations with other partners, including AVL.

AVI specializes in perception-oriented solutions for autonomous vehicles, dedicated to enhancing sensor quality and developing AI models specific to this sector. Its initiatives also include creating necessary simulators and datasets that advance technologies essential for functionalities such as parking assistance and path planning. AVI has achieved notable milestones in the project, including the successful release of a Minimum Viable Product (MVP) as part of Milestone 4.

Furthermore, AVI is committed to ethical AI practices, underscored by a financial investment of 319,000.00 EUR, which reinforces its critical role in the broader objectives of the CoEvolution Consortium. Additionally, the organization engages in supplementary work related to tasks outside the scope of PAN, enhancing its collaborative efforts within the consortium and contributing significantly to research and development. Overall, AVI's active participation and leadership in the CoEvolution project facilitate cutting-edge advancements in AI security and autonomous vehicle technology.</data>
