<node id="CBRL">
  <data key="d0">CBRL</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CBRL is a partner organization that contributes to the CoEvolution project, focusing on dissemination strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;CBRL, also known as CYBERALYTICS LIMITED, is a small to medium-sized enterprise (SME) and a participant organization in the CoEvolution project. It plays a multifaceted role within the project, leading efforts in impact analysis and reporting, while also contributing to various research activities related to artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML). 

As a lead beneficiary, CBRL is responsible for Work Package WP2, which focuses on dissemination, exploitation, and sustainability strategies. This involves developing effective communication strategies to share project results and ensure alignment with established project milestones, including Milestone 6. CBRL has committed significant resources to the project, dedicating 35 person-months of effort and contributing 297,500.00 EUR to the overall project budget.

In addition to its dissemination efforts, CBRL leads Task 5.4, which is central to the CoEvolution project’s impact analysis reporting. Throughout the project’s duration, CBRL is tasked with producing impact analysis reports to detail the implications of the project’s activities. Furthermore, the organization actively engages in the project’s standardization efforts, contributing to existing standards related to AI security and cybersecurity.

CBRL is also at the forefront of developing the CoEvolution Security Assurance Engine, where it conducts critical risk analysis and security assurance tasks, underscoring its commitment to enhancing security assurance, ethical AI practices, and cybersecurity.

Overall, CBRL's expertise and extensive contributions are crucial to the CoEvolution project’s goals, significantly influencing AI and cybersecurity research while ensuring the project’s long-term success and sustainability.</data>
