614b1182e2be9469625326eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b26ea5c9fd025a1c37710d2d39cf836d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84670dae929f0474fd75c1904113c7d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d65865b76581edf9ac1aac0de819fca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3b7d48470cd2d0de2fb4466e3c766fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce96797e723874f84f3ba02a22d09d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f26601f4c4959a5a23ecaace643d0bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc0f669cc4e2bfef891820395ef55650&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d36e00d6638001bed983791ad13038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e115bd628f8fb0edc5eb2d730569997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1bbb9e746eec802a40ceda441e1c95e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef356bf47d4a7662b1eebd219b6efecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a23b1d8ad6fd3128ebdb600d00c5bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504206f0a7bf9dc2f99c1165d4800618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc12431b623f53cd11ca16b1437d498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f7b898ba71a7016ad21ff4ed438387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fe06437e382ce0fa404ec6b5b10ceaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107384e3edcbe7422a87890a602648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-017e7c3267b01fc259f8929e89a0b812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edc6612637391d476f24729c8ff8104e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c94330a60dc34a0bfa60748253c8dd</data>
  <data key="d2">ISI is among the partners collaborating in the CoEvolution project, outlined to manage outreach to other projects and initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;ISI, officially known as ATHINA-EREVNITIKO KENTRO KAINOTOMIAS STIS TECHNOLOGIAS TIS PLIROFORIAS, is a prominent Greek research center substantially involved in the CoEvolution project. This project aims to advance artificial intelligence (AI) systems and bolster cybersecurity. As a lead beneficiary, ISI is responsible for various tasks including the preparation and delivery of reports, technical specifications, and scientific coordination.

Within the framework of the CoEvolution project, ISI leads Work Package 3 (WP3), which emphasizes specifications, architecture, and security assurance management. Additionally, ISI heads Task 3.3, focusing specifically on the architecture of the CoEvolution framework. The organization is also involved in leading Task 1.2 in Work Package 1 and Task 5.1, where it defines and manages AI model bills-of-material, and is a participant in Task 5.4.

Contributing to multiple work packages and tasks, ISI plays a vital role in the design and evaluation of AI models and the establishment of security measures. It has delivered critical reports, including deliverable D5.1, which focuses on security assurance and monitoring techniques. ISI's expertise encompasses the development of AI safety technologies, emphasizing resilience, security, and the identification of vulnerabilities, which contribute to enhancing overall safety in AI systems.

To support its project endeavors, ISI has a total resource allocation of 84 person-months, with 19 project months allocated specifically from SAP. The organization is deeply engaged in scientific and technical coordination, managing technical discussions, and formulating a comprehensive roadmap for project activities. It actively participates in standardization efforts and coordinates with other EU-funded projects to meet data requirements and address protections against adversarial attacks.

In addition, ISI is working on the development of a security assurance engine to promote ethical and legal oversight of AI systems, ensuring that safety and security measures are integrated throughout the CoEvolution project. With its specialization in innovative technologies and machine learning techniques, ISI is committed to enhancing privacy and security assessments, particularly in mitigating side-channel attacks, underscoring its essential role in advancing research in AI and strengthening cybersecurity within the project's objectives.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756144344</data>
</node>
