ba71a7016ad21ff4ed438387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beda666afc02f488950a3cdbad5279e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107384e3edcbe7422a87890a602648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-017e7c3267b01fc259f8929e89a0b812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c94330a60dc34a0bfa60748253c8dd</data>
  <data key="d2">UNICA is a partner in the CoEvolution project, involved in dissemination and project activities.&lt;SEP&gt;UNICA, formally known as Università Degli Studi di Cagliari, is a prominent academic institution and a key participant in the CoEvolution project, which aims to enhance the security and robustness of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. As a lead organization within the CoEvolution consortium, UNICA plays a vital role in a multitude of tasks, particularly focusing on AI security developments, data privacy, and security enhancements.

In its contributions to the CoEvolution project, UNICA is actively involved in various tasks, notably Task 4.2, which concentrates on designing and implementing security assessment tools for AI models, and Task 5.5, centered on context-aware AI adaptation techniques. The institution is also a participant in the assessment of AI models and contributes significantly to the analysis of technological and industrial requirements necessary for the project's progress. UNICA allocates substantial resources to this initiative, dedicating a total of 52 person-months to various work packages, reflecting its commitment to project deliverables, which include crucial scientific and technical reports.

UNICA is recognized for its expertise in open-source projects, contributing tools like the SecML library, a Python library aimed at enhancing adversarial robustness in AI testing methodologies. This library serves as an essential resource for improving AI applications across diverse sectors.

In terms of project management and organization, UNICA focuses on defining project requirements and specifications, participates in budget allocation for the CoEvolution project, and endorses the CoEvolution Consortium Agreement, demonstrating both organizational and financial commitment. Furthermore, the institution incorporates considerations of gender equality into its work, ensuring a comprehensive approach to achieving project objectives.

Additionally, UNICA is the lead beneficiary for deliverable D4.1, focusing on enablers development and technological reporting in the HORIZON-CL3-2023-CS-01 project. Through its multifaceted involvement, UNICA is essential for advancing secure AI technologies and achieving the goals of the CoEvolution Project, showcasing its research capabilities and dedication to innovation in AI security.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756144346</data>
</node>
