<node id="CoEvolution Framework">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution Framework is a comprehensive open-source initiative designed to enhance security, trust, and robustness assurance across the entire lifecycle of artificial intelligence (AI) models within the AI supply chain. As a key component of the CoEvolution Project, the framework emphasizes the integration, evaluation, and continual adaptation of networked AI systems, particularly in dynamic industries such as automotive and logistics.

This framework is dedicated to reinforcing the trustworthiness of AI components by establishing rigorous architectural design standards. These standards align with European Union regulations on AI security, focusing on collaboration, effective resource management, and the development of innovative techniques aimed at detecting and mitigating adversarial attacks.

The CoEvolution Framework provides a broad spectrum of support services, including training, consulting, and technological extensions, to facilitate the growth and advancement of AI technologies. Its design is especially geared towards addressing critical use cases in logistics and autonomous vehicles, promoting sustainable business practices and adaptive financing models within the AI community. By offering a structured approach for the development and validation of AI-based solutions, the CoEvolution Framework highlights the vital necessity for reliable and secure AI technologies amid today’s intricate and evolving digital landscape.

Additionally, the framework's architecture plays a central role in the CoEvolution Project, serving as a reference standard for implementation. It is focused on security, trust, and context awareness throughout its operations and lifecycle, and is also involved in the creation and deployment of AI-driven localization and edge/resource management solutions that enhance productivity in industrial logistics and autonomous vehicle domains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1085773cd43df1afe7247dd49f7475fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6a0f23e95fea1a56df838e0e512fb24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81418f280483fb994ba74151f8e56fb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577bd3edffb92fe21986d68a6eb2cc22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0445a20d7ba0635033f2f217666f7e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c45633c6b079b86215891c3f1d283a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6c9cfb6e7abe8b52771b95508dd1919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c47283aa17272462fab245e43ac76b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75554414522e9656908eb2a8c6a7c1b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-672abb4b4d866c235db2385a6641554e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cafddfb6023f95166fd0911d6de46cf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d188b520ae593ffa16184991a28ba19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ee7f9cc09dacb04da20b5e541d35880&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5611f1258fe52c0e8568e9fe484f3f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cc533b2db505c23b211fa8248d014e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51db1d0ebfb384f2340004d2031fd42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c79851ac919cf8bc22fc5597de36064b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9510fe2b92ae882d551007b5ee87df2e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426353</data>
</node>
<node id="WP3">
  <data key="d0">WP3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">WP3, or Work Package 3, is a critical component of the CoEvolution Project, designated for specific activities and objectives within the initiative. It plays an essential role in the overall research and development efforts by focusing on the specification, requirements, and architecture pertinent to the project's framework. WP3 provides comprehensive technical oversight, engaging in technology analysis, requirement elicitation, and the specification of threat models particularly regarding networked AI systems. 

As part of the project's evolution, responsibilities initially held by SAP have been redistributed, primarily to ICCS and AEGIS, reflecting a shift in workload management among project partners. This redistribution has impacted resource allocation and project dynamics. WP3 is responsible for influencing the activities of other technical work packages, specifically WP4 through WP6, ensuring successful implementation of the CoEvolution framework. Thus, WP3 is pivotal in defining project specifications, architecture, and requirements, as well as driving the technological developments associated with the CoEvolution Project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5936cfdec252f012f8e0b69c534c24ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9a196fd79cf2ad7253020f3005f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fb0f79a7142225a7d2dfaedc44c958&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f2e8aebdfb355f313ea068cac55423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5954618a5ba5f9a63e629b838f5a752e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84670dae929f0474fd75c1904113c7d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5cbf16cd814360775473b61c07db9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9101312bae5650dad5c9bc39d26c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab48b662719cb842a1786a0c13a6d2cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-841013486b274ac183dbe85d18dd9731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909ff0598aa7c312fae851a154fae81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad8c45296704b976d9974fb6ccbcc41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd2acaeb0d9437c3f09baa7c94ddf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-672abb4b4d866c235db2385a6641554e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425668</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 2.5">
  <data key="d0">Task 2.5</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 2.5 is a pivotal element of the CoEvolution project, concentrating on end-user internal organization training activities aimed at enhancing capacity among the project's partner organizations. Its primary objective is to ensure the effective uptake of project findings within the large organizations involved in the initiative. This entails conducting targeted training activities that facilitate the dissemination of the project's outcomes across different departments within these organizations. By doing so, Task 2.5 plays a critical role in supporting the successful implementation and integration of the CoEvolution project's results, thereby maximizing the benefits for all participating entities. Overall, Task 2.5 is dedicated to fostering a thorough understanding of project findings through organized training initiatives, ensuring that all stakeholders are well-equipped to apply the knowledge gained.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1079c5a2020c1fa8f7ce2c209e6097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449cdb7f2dbaf658674f7d17457a5b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e809a3ce6da55906320f84dbd54cb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfaacf3af6603ac9cb26af5c77f318ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc12431b623f53cd11ca16b1437d498</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426345</data>
</node>
<node id="UPatras">
  <data key="d0">UPatras</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The University of Patras (UPatras) stands out as a prominent academic and research institution, actively engaged in several influential initiatives, most notably the CoEvolution project and the H2020 HEIR project. Within the CoEvolution project, UPatras has taken on the role of lead beneficiary and research partner, succeeding IMT in the consortium and significantly amplifying its contributions.

UPatras's involvement in the CoEvolution project encompasses a wide range of responsibilities. The university is deeply engaged in adversarial attack security testing, as well as the design of technical specifications and project architecture. A key aspect of its role is leading the development of deliverable D6.2, which is focused on creating a minimum viable product (MVP) for the integrated framework established by the project. The institution is well-regarded for its specialized expertise in artificial intelligence technologies, which supports its significant contributions to simulation tasks related to AI model assessment and technological analysis, particularly concerning security facets.

Additionally, UPatras is contributing to the development of the ComDeX architecture to enhance efficient data exchange within Internet of Things (IoT) ecosystems while improving context-awareness in Federated Learning. Its participation in the H2020 HEIR project further emphasizes UPatras's commitment to enhancing AI security and elevating data quality assessment through innovative tools designed to analyze and aggregate sources of vulnerability.

Financially, UPatras has demonstrated its commitment to the CoEvolution project by contributing €220,000.00 and dedicating 44 person-months to Project 101168560, underscoring its dedication to impactful research and collaboration. The institution's comprehensive engagement spans various dimensions, including AI security, privacy efforts, and data quality assessment, thereby solidifying its reputation as a leading organization in the development of networked AI systems and context-aware collaborative AI. 

In summary, UPatras is an integral participant in the CoEvolution project with well-defined roles across multiple tasks and deliverables, actively contributing to collaborative research efforts, adversarial attack assessments, and frameworks aimed at ensuring AI resilience and robustness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81b5e09ae3d0f914dccc0db6a5f91e22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63daf77ed4db04707c5e7f33947f8edf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6fbf5dd7af05fd0e193c115784651e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adc3d9c69d7abcc740f761a0cbbf43e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f80aa6caf939e06fbb5e4bab717d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce012c5c7284b310263eb73817161dd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6205dbd68fc8bd585195fe14e81b0d57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edc6612637391d476f24729c8ff8104e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-841013486b274ac183dbe85d18dd9731&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577bd3edffb92fe21986d68a6eb2cc22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd182fd514d7984966c94b99cabf64e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d6fba577b81094056c9337ad52c3ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20c0cc0a37ebaa1bdc18241b7b7a42f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0445a20d7ba0635033f2f217666f7e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fb0f79a7142225a7d2dfaedc44c958&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5bd329614b1182e2be9469625326eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecef4657b9eaa07737a23410c0933ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51eaae3a3d54576dbf82c1b062f1bf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfaacf3af6603ac9cb26af5c77f318ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-853e3c305e010114288cc805df7be8a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c84806ce6d96fb7e10ee2de2ef7fc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7086ddfd2becc56c4a5d794fb4aa63db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec24c7171d1f9190641a3a8d0adbdf96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca4e2865d7233be2941bdb2500bc81cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d2ff0e7582f72b15822c3c3392a6345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80dbc2c57631e342a48a24b95f6e1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1840a2aa861c08b15185d927867134a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce96797e723874f84f3ba02a22d09d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75efa432cb6a9347528127bab93b2e22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8bee6728a0eb29b6a3c4f9a4ccf3996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c733bc2ac52924fad86b0ae9233921f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9925c33404cf10a29a2c57f9e6874c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e00a0c381689061b9602b16e3966e85a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f7b898ba71a7016ad21ff4ed438387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827c0e1b05bc9eac5d2bbfb266ef6562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6047665c4bd29f334a06022d100213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d798311ba09f5fcfd