<node id="Work Package WP3">
  <data key="d0">Work Package WP3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Work Package WP3 is a critical segment of the CoEvolution project that focuses on the specification, requirements, and architecture of the overall initiative. It encompasses various tasks related to these areas from the project's commencement in month 1 to its conclusion in month 12. Additionally, Work Package WP3 is specifically concerned with the architecture of the CoEvolution project and is led by ISI. This work package plays a vital role in codifying the project scope and managing related tasks, ensuring a comprehensive approach to the development and implementation of the project's foundational elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfaacf3af6603ac9cb26af5c77f318ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edc6612637391d476f24729c8ff8104e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de811e88e375a0427133f48114ab4084</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425682</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 3.1">
  <data key="d0">Task 3.1</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 3.1 deals with analyzing the state-of-the-art in AI, security, and cybersecurity within the CoEvolution project.&lt;SEP&gt;Task 3.1 is a collaborative initiative within the CoEvolution Project that focuses on conducting a comprehensive analysis of the state-of-the-art in artificial intelligence (AI), security, and cybersecurity. This task aims to characterize potential threats against networked AI systems, thereby enhancing the understanding of AI security trends. Additionally, Task 3.1 is responsible for providing functional specifications that will inform the architectural development within the CoEvolution framework. Through this detailed investigation, Task 3.1 seeks to develop effective threat models that will contribute to the overall objectives of the CoEvolution Project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f8bb95ba3048fe4ba1a028477aaf2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e809a3ce6da55906320f84dbd54cb6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426337</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 3.2">
  <data key="d0">Task 3.2</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 3.2 is a critical phase within the CoEvolution project that focuses on establishing use-case specifications and requirements intended for integration within the AI supply chain and automotive sector. The task is dedicated to the comprehensive collection of both technological and industrial requirements for proposed use cases. By defining these specifications and requirements, Task 3.2 plays a pivotal role in aligning the project's objectives with the necessary criteria derived from various use cases. This effort is essential for providing crucial information that enhances the understanding of the overall requirements related to the CoEvolution project, particularly in terms of networked AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d2ff0e7582f72b15822c3c3392a6345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8bb95ba3048fe4ba1a028477aaf2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1079c5a2020c1fa8f7ce2c209e6097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9925c33404cf10a29a2c57f9e6874c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e809a3ce6da55906320f84dbd54cb6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426345</data>
</node>
<node id="STS">
  <data key="d0">STS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">STS is a partner organization in the CoEvolution project, contributing to project goals and dissemination.&lt;SEP&gt;Sphynx Technology Solutions AG (STS) is a small to medium-sized enterprise (SME) that plays a pivotal role in the CoEvolution project, which is dedicated to advancing artificial intelligence (AI) technologies while ensuring ethical practices in AI systems. As a contributing organization, STS is involved in several tasks related to AI model training and security assurance, specifically participating in Task 5.4 and contributing to important activities outlined in the project.

STS is actively engaged in various work packages within the CoEvolution initiative, focusing particularly on Task 5.1, which involves defining, designing, and managing the AI Model Bill of Materials (MBOM) structure. Additionally, STS contributes to Task 6.4, where it is involved in validation efforts and reporting outcomes related to the project. Throughout its participation, STS has allocated a total of 26 person-months to research and development to enhance AI security by developing security components and engaging in security assurance tasks.

Furthermore, STS serves as a liaison with the European Union, facilitating effective communication regarding the project's goals and achievements. Although some financial data concerning STS's involvement has been acknowledged in project documents, specific figures remain undisclosed. Overall, STS demonstrates a significant commitment to the advancement of practical AI applications, emphasizing the importance of standardizing safe and ethical uses of AI technologies through its comprehensive engagement in the CoEvolution initiative.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b81697e5e97b55f3fbdb3e229af635af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f26601f4c4959a5a23ecaace643d0bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d798311ba09f5fcfd50eafd690ade83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75efa432cb6a9347528127bab93b2e22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6fbc1a3bfb993cb23f1ec5cd61622f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80dbc2c57631e342a48a24b95f6e1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c01a4f4fce25ef615aa8d96cea16200a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3601f2df51a8a247b13dc91952cf725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d976f2ffb8ad5255bb083a125919929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577bd3edffb92fe21986d68a6eb2cc22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6379cdca686a83d4dcc68c446a27b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b72b3e7ba1aaeb63a98bb04479fd99ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29a64033d909953d984427106205f924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa547865cf460d6e73617a01a0b88537&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a849a6c0719d6015ef6c319e7b3a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041a92c5d6ba00b1fe79852f2d1bcf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d6fba577b81094056c9337ad52c3ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd182fd514d7984966c94b99cabf64e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd021e77c6a98f8d589a96e248297baf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72e3d6c0adc259c792912cb22e5365cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f80aa6caf939e06fbb5e4bab717d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0445a20d7ba0635033f2f217666f7e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0362c884f52f6e88e18946d6287d4495&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e00a0c381689061b9602b16e3966e85a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4810c9b22b0ce26c963075600f4dbd84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-504206f0a7bf9dc2f99c1165d4800618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c84806ce6d96fb7e10ee2de2ef7fc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc12431b623f53cd11ca16b1437d498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c733bc2ac52924fad86b0ae9233921f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce012c5c7284b310263eb73817161dd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-156a8e85a6eb2d84a8dc90300df66a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce96797e723874f84f3ba02a22d09d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-613f6432243d121b9ba6b6dbfd90ee39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88921885a26ccc1c5504cb6fb467c4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f0e52ffd2cfc0cefb2f4e79d13f201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16ec89c88f17eab253fcbabae20f2eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5bd329614b1182e2be9469625326eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107384e3edcbe7422a87890a602648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-991c83168528be4a6f6d89078a6d75ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecef4657b9eaa07737a23410c0933ea8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756144347</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 3.3">
  <data key="d0">Task 3.3</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 3.3 is a crucial aspect of the CoEvolution Project, focused on defining the architecture of the CoEvolution framework and its components. This task establishes a reference architecture that is foundational for subsequent implementation efforts. It involves collaboration among various organizations working towards the development of the CoEvolution Reference Architecture, which is intended to serve as a comprehensive guide for future implementation activities. Task 3.3 encompasses not only the definition of the framework's structure and components but also the development of associated technical requirements, ensuring a well-rounded approach to support the goals of the CoEvolution Project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f8bb95ba3048fe4ba1a028477aaf2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6a0f23e95fea1a56df838e0e512fb24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7e6360e26602def4ba1d660311269&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d40ee8239b5807a75857260b7afe44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e809a3ce6da55906320f84dbd54cb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-853e3c305e010114288cc805df7be8a4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426346</data>
</node>
<node id="WP4">
  <data key="d0">WP4</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">WP4, or Work Package 4, is a crucial component of the CoEvolution project that focuses on the organization of tasks and contributions from various partners. Its primary aim is to enhance the security and resilience of AI models throughout their lifecycle. The work package undertakes distinct tasks that are integral to the CoEvolution initiative, particularly exploring the correlation between various parameters and associated security and privacy risks, and developing tools and strategies to mitigate these risks.

WP4 operates within a dynamic management structure that involves collaboration among partners such as ICCS, ISI, and AEGIS, while also incorporating responsibilities previously managed by SAP. The core activities of WP4 include conducting analyses to improve the security and resilience of AI models, addressing critical challenges such as adversarial attacks. Furthermore, WP4 is tasked with developing machine learning components and producing reports that contribute to the overall success of the CoEvolution project.

In summary, WP4 is instrumental in advancing AI technology development within the CoEvolution project, underscoring its significance in achieving objectives related to AI model security, enhancement, and the integration of contextual technology enablers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5cbf16cd814360775473b61c07db9e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84670dae929f0474fd75c1904113c7d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd2acaeb0d9437c3f09baa7c94ddf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9a196fd79cf2ad7253020f3005f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fb0f79a7142225a7d2dfaedc44c958&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b9101312bae5650dad5c9bc39d26c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d40ee8239b5807a75857260b7afe44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab48b662719cb842a1786a0c13a6d2cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51eaae3a3d54576dbf82c1b062f1bf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec24c7171d1f9190641a3a8d0adbdf96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-672abb4b4d866c235db2385a6641554e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5954618a5ba5f9a63e629b838f5a752e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-909ff0598aa7c312fae851a154fae81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8bb95ba3048fe4ba1a028477aaf2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5936cfdec252f012f8e0b69c534c24ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f2e8aebdfb355f313ea068cac55423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d36e00d6638001bed983791ad13038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad8c45296704b976d9974fb6ccbcc41</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425669</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Models">
  <data key="d0">AI Models</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Models are advanced computational systems engineered to perform a variety of tasks such as inference, classification, and regression. These models leverage data processing capabilities to make decisions based on learned patterns, allowing them to adapt to diverse scenarios effectively. Within the context of the CoEvolution project, AI Models are specifically designed to enhance performance while prioritizing improvements in security, robustness, and trustworthiness. This focus aims to defend against adversarial attacks and address potential vulnerabilities that may arise throughout their operational lifecycle.

The CoEvolution framework emphasizes the development of AI Models that can adapt to various network conditions and respond effectively to threats, thereby optimizing their defensive capabilities. These models encompass a broad range of machine learning and deep learning algorithms, which are crucial to the project’s objectives of enhancing both the security and operational reliability of AI systems.

AI Models are equipped with CoEvolution gadgets and security self-awareness mechanisms that bolster their ability to efficiently detect adversarial attacks. They represent various artificial intelligence systems utilized within the AI supply chain, showcasing a strong commitment to security and reliability. Furthermore, these models are designed to possess context-awareness and are fortified through a series of defensive strategies aimed at effective vulnerability assessments and lifecycle management against adversarial threats.

Additionally, AI Models are structured systems created for processing data that must be resilient and compliant with regulatory frameworks, such as the EU AI Act. They can be classified as either white boxes or black boxes based on their transparency and provision status, and play a critical role in several phases of the CoEvolution project, including design, training, and testing.

Overall, AI Models encompass innovative computational frameworks that not only aim to learn from data but also maintain vigilance regarding associated security threats and vulnerabilities, contributing significantly to the establishment of a robust AI environment that adheres to ethical considerations and regulatory compliance. Their advancement within the CoEvolution project is pivotal for fostering secure applications, particularly in high-stakes areas like autonomous vehicles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db75b2cab1362b7796ff2a8753c4245e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb3c5a6faf3b857ba8d43ec98eb973c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ad886edb819a72a00a95a3d6cb0423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e82353b035ba082060e064ac9ff6c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba1c9f3141d753938298cb0137770fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9260f7f87786fb6b762b6bf5a25591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6a811cf4a60bc95db18b65f20632b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11568e1141436db1fb558509a57b48c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec24c7171d1f9190641a3a8d0adbdf96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efd11c9b0ab72e885216df0907238fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e396002be0503d0e0baac803477dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cafddfb6023f95166fd0911d6de46cf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df19f3e87623e77b4872532b8e5d92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5c42e7d5f67c2de98328269247dec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f7b898ba71a7016ad21ff4ed438387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d69ac7cb43276601482059fe1cb59288&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddfc5f9eb88fc57c1e7d42c942cb16c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5dd98f6f33ccb6a835a00ac3e5ca4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b717d4f1dbabcdf423e3b9ee479caad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c85ec84436942dd8fc56f3409a58ac9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425698</data>
</node>
<node id="T6.1">
  <data key="d0">T6.1</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">T6.1 is a task within the CoEvolution project that aims to utilize developed architecture and functional specifications.&lt;SEP&gt;T6.1 is another specific task that has undergone a duration adjustment as part of the project management.&lt;SEP&gt;T6.1 refers to a specific task within the CoEvolution project related to the integration and deployment processes of AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83b3630725878907a8a7fd7b403dc7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec24c7171d1f9190641a3a8d0adbdf96</data>
