</node>
<node id="AI MBOM">
  <data key="d0">AI MBOM</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI MBOM stands for AI Model Bill-of-Materials, a structure intended for comprehensive record-keeping regarding AI model training and security.&lt;SEP&gt;AI MBOM, which stands for Artificial Intelligence Bill of Materials, is a unique and critical data structure utilized within the CoEvolution framework. It provides detailed documentation regarding the design, development, and lifecycle of AI models, focusing significantly on aspects of security, transparency, and accountability. This comprehensive framework encapsulates core elements such as training data, dependencies, metadata, security assessments, vulnerabilities, ownership, and compliance tracking, all essential for ensuring the integrity and operational robustness of AI systems.

AI MBOM serves multiple functions, primarily targeting the management and validation of AI models. It meticulously tracks attributes, historical data, security postures, and associated risks, thus fostering enhanced security for the deployment and enhancement of AI models. The framework documents security vulnerabilities and the measures taken to mitigate them, integrating crucial concepts from both a Bill of Materials and a Model Baseline of Operations and Maintenance. Additionally, it includes elements like adversarial attack resistance and context-aware security metrics, crucial for understanding the operational contexts of AI components.

Developed through the CoEvolution solution process, AI MBOM supports transparency within the AI supply chain ecosystem by maintaining records that navigate the complexities of artificial intelligence. These models are stored in a shared repository with varying access tiers for different users, ensuring robust security monitoring and compliance throughout the AI model lifecycle. Overall, AI MBOM is vital for certifying the trust and security of AI models, significantly enhancing their resilience and management efficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-504206f0a7bf9dc2f99c1165d4800618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cea29209e72133bb93f48ee121efe0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041a92c5d6ba00b1fe79852f2d1bcf19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58bbe4f5990fa2bf4939eaf879cf277a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbd5dafa81256fe9f82cfcb884bca559&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a859909fffb7947b2b88ac3fcc588943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b217cefad4abec670ed7ca0d4128679d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a591c892291649de34c3de312c2e971a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c9765c6de5d09adbaa4008d62e0503a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff71b865dc936679ff717845aef86de4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81418f280483fb994ba74151f8e56fb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65261df93ed337be33236b9008ec65a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3c184b92e7717afad2ff103dd68dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77b8b5bf7e419d5685f26851e9d9d67a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d1f4cd119004da61bb670635808ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d107384e3edcbe7422a87890a602648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d6bf63b8e7794868c19826908bb0e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e2cc45e905008af3bd387b458c2d616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b65576c05d96906d2692fc35b3941f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4991d2b2e76403b019f2f16989b2a93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c63ecefae511a920b168080d05faae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fa9dfe5b39b5ec1975df01d2e4f7d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b95887f0a735a53175d3a901822dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f26601f4c4959a5a23ecaace643d0bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3d753a5ba3bfc0d8c4ec414093b1cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b977bae012f1a149c35d078f2c64ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f7c6a9a08e9c022ee9a774571a1ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6c9cfb6e7abe8b52771b95508dd1919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4af943851da76b28e80907078f658e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2be40177ccd661e4813abe35732bfb90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ef324e25221cc1aac49364c3a0e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6a811cf4a60bc95db18b65f20632b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39a1b5cf48158980a9cfbe239a3316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df6cb12c1afd7894243ba7d6eda4b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbbc377e2e04f5a8e60be464dfc0a17e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d36effac07d2e19625fcc31b88101b2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa4c1166600f780f6e57409778e6ccb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5395556365a730e