<node id="European Commission's AI Act">
  <data key="d0">European Commission's AI Act</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Commission's AI Act is a comprehensive regulatory framework designed to manage and regulate the use of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies across various industries. Its primary goal is to ensure the safety, transparency, and trustworthiness of AI applications, thereby promoting a safe and responsible environment for their integration into diverse sectors. By addressing potential risks and establishing guidelines and regulations for the deployment of AI, the Act seeks to foster public confidence in AI technologies while simultaneously facilitating innovation. This initiative by the European Union aims to create a structured approach to AI regulation that emphasizes not only safety but also accountability and ethical considerations in the deployment of AI solutions worldwide.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9870dfcb7b266f6b6ac1dd5222b5f58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f662d06ec1bd0b762ad34da27a7259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2be5c8354db5456b4254a51a65a6f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6e752def2c1fc953cab11b48652f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788baa379b81a91f164731d4acab9774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425684</data>
</node>
<node id="Google">
  <data key="d0">Google</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Google is a technology company that has developed and published the Secure AI Framework (SAIF), a conceptual framework aimed at identifying and addressing critical security issues related to artificial intelligence. The SAIF emphasizes the importance of securing AI systems, particularly with respect to the AI supply chain. Through this framework, Google intends to support the development of secure AI systems and draw attention to significant security challenges within the AI field. This initiative reflects Google's commitment to ensuring the robustness and security of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Google is a technology company that has published the Secure AI Framework (SAIF) to address AI security issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84cf7d8377823cd2796ee572ef8df58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8de9ab24149e20dd885bdf7aa0cbc37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fd21c4597a1403d202414c53457ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2be5c8354db5456b4254a51a65a6f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6e752def2c1fc953cab11b48652f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788baa379b81a91f164731d4acab9774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425682</data>
</node>
<node id="EU">
  <data key="d0">EU</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">The EU, or European Union, is a political and economic union comprised of member states primarily located in Europe. It is dedicated to fostering collaboration among its countries, facilitating cooperation, and implementing shared monetary policies while emphasizing common values. A central focus of the EU's mandate is to promote research and innovation across its member states through various funded initiatives.

In the realm of technology, particularly artificial intelligence (AI), the EU actively engages in establishing standards and regulatory compliance to ensure safety and trustworthiness in AI applications. This effort is exemplified by the EU AI Act, which aims to regulate AI practices to adhere to high ethical standards during the development and implementation of AI systems. The EU prioritizes ethics and safety in this context, reflecting its commitment to robust governance and ethical practices within the technology sector.

Additionally, the EU serves as a granting authority, overseeing the execution of grants and managing reimbursement rates for costs associated with projects like CoEvolution and other initiatives under its jurisdiction. Overall, the EU plays a pivotal role in financing and administering contributions for a diverse array of projects, while ensuring compliance with established rules and promoting ethical principles and safety, particularly in the field of artificial intelligence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95e581cb78a2c2aad223dc49965291dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65261df93ed337be33236b9008ec65a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0997e404b51fe3aa39a52767ed1caac5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c63ecefae511a920b168080d05faae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5704cabfb650f5e43d761190f9a6804e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3d753a5ba3bfc0d8c4ec414093b1cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65321e5c497565cf717aab53e5aa7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b977bae012f1a149c35d078f2c64ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f1982ab2664c79b22a447094fd7c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4011fe5c8f325cbfb6257057dcfc79c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27fa07b6f1f7106aece74437f014454c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddc1f667d5d7b593ff074f4172cecd6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7595c8200e32fa30ada5bd766b8a892&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f216fc14ce08511b03292fca3d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a296b5c4f24ed1a5eae98b2e605e9835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e4c02ab56fd93c5cc9c23327e28ccc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6e752def2c1fc953cab11b48652f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd07e02da457ab40f95f32db9e1c6587&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6587c0a38b949dea5de8a236e80407fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83e1fb202d9cabb7b747aef687ac4527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449cdb7f2dbaf658674f7d17457a5b29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc12431b623f53cd11ca16b1437d498</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425659</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Security Framework">
  <data key="d0">AI Security Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Security Framework includes guidelines and best practices for identifying and mitigating AI security vulnerabilities across development lifecycles.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Security Framework is a comprehensive approach developed under CoEvolution to enhance the resilience and trustworthiness of AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4011fe5c8f325cbfb6257057dcfc79c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419836</data>
</node>
<node id="poisoning attacks">
  <data key="d0">poisoning attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Poisoning attacks involve introducing malicious data into AI systems that can degrade the integrity of AI models and their outputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419836</data>
</node>
<node id="federated learning">
  <data key="d0">federated learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Federated learning is a decentralized machine learning approach that enables multiple participants to collaboratively train models across various devices or servers that hold local data samples. This method allows for the training of algorithms without the need to exchange sensitive data, thereby ensuring data privacy. It facilitates collaboration among numerous participants while maintaining the integrity and confidentiality of their individual datasets. Through this innovative approach, federated learning contributes to the development of machine learning models while respecting the privacy of local data holders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0be6b7a96133b91256e1b5134cbf3d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c59208a0ecce67d91fc2e55e630e3efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f36d4368a91cfa20fb1fbc19cc60bc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422744</data>
</node>
<node id="supply chain">
  <data key="d0">supply chain</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The supply chain in this context refers to the interconnected systems involved in the AI development process, from data collection to deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419836</data>
</node>
<node id="adversarial input">
  <data key="d0">adversarial input</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial input is a type of deceptive data designed to fool AI systems, potentially leading to misinformation and compromised function.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial input refers to deceptive or misleading data that can trick AI systems into making incorrect decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial input refers to inputs designed to deceive or manipulate AI systems, leading to potential errors or misinterpretations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a6e752def2c1fc953cab11b48652f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fd21c4597a1403d202414c53457ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425683</data>
</node>
<node id="contextual awareness">
  <data key="d0">contextual awareness</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Contextual awareness pertains to an AI system's understanding of its operational environment, which is essential for accurate decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Contextual awareness refers to the ability of a system to consider contextual information to enhance decision-making processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5092e32b5e7f6b1dc6a316b8941ea4c2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422747</data>
</node>
<node id="data collection">
  <data key="d0">data collection</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Data collection is a critical phase in the AI lifecycle where information is gathered to train models, and it can be susceptible to vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419836</data>
</node>
<node id="design">
  <data key="d0">design</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Design refers to the phase in the AI development process where models are formulated, which can be influenced by various security threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419836</data>
</node>
<node id="deployment">
  <data key="d0">deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment is the stage where AI models are put into use in real-world applications, and during this process, they may face various security risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419836</data>
</node>
<node id="security assessment flow">
  <data key="d0">security assessment flow</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The security assessment flow is a proposed systematic approach to identify AI security vulnerabilities and provide coherent defenses throughout the AI lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419836</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Model Lifecycle">
  <data key="d0">AI Model Lifecycle</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Model Lifecycle refers to the comprehensive series of phases that artificial intelligence models undergo from inception to deployment and ongoing maintenance. It encompasses the design, training, testing, validation, and deployment phases, integrating critical processes such as security assessments and risk management throughout each stage. 

The CoEvolution project specifically aims to enhance the security measures applied within this lifecycle, emphasizing the importance of robust defenses against adversarial attacks to ensure the resilience of AI models against potential threats. Each phase of the AI Model Lifecycle is designed to facilitate continuous improvement and adaptation in response to emerging challenges, underscoring the necessity of thorough risk evaluations at every step.

Furthermore, the lifecycle includes ongoing operational activities post-deployment, which are crucial for maintaining the effectiveness and safety of AI implementations over time. This holistic approach highlights the integral role of security and risk assessments in reinforcing the robustness of AI models, ensuring they remain effective and secure throughout their operational lifespan within the CoEvolution framework. Overall, the AI Model Lifecycle provides a structured pathway for the development and ongoing management of AI models, focusing on security enhancements at every stage to navigate the complexities associated with AI technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2186aff847bb122f1f1a8eba737faf56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f984a4687c34b201081d48b577fd5ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402e243c2b3772441ea35e8dba3c710c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e539403d1165017fce38ab358660244c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788baa379b81a91f164731d4acab9774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bdd45e641a1d84d501219cd34c72fbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f995ea0aa653e5c578ea2df5d9ff710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df19f3e87623e77b4872532b8e5d92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-007d04d0795b80a15b2632f97ec477dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5d99a66a08e8bad40aa04612a33b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53d45e1780332e8c3904aba8e79abbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b9d5508965f4ddd6b9dc8dab9cebb0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0be6b7a96133b91256e1b5134cbf3d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-624f2387785876b8e9add5d5b236075f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53324f76aa261271178fe84a61273b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8830be99a56abf88963043f2ab9507b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f662d06ec1bd0b762ad34da27a7259</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425669</data>
</node>
<node id="AI supply chain">
  <data key="d0">AI supply chain</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI supply chain refers to the interconnected processes and entities involved in the development and deployment of AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI supply chain refers to the comprehensive process that involves the development, deployment, and maintenance of AI systems. This supply chain is characterized by various risk assessments aimed at ensuring the security and trustworthiness of AI technologies throughout their lifecycle. It encompasses the entire journey from AI model design to deployment, highlighting the interconnected nature of developing and distributing AI technologies, while also addressing potential risks and vulnerabilities. Furthermore, the AI supply chain integrates AI technologies within industrial applications, with a strong emphasis on maintaining security and data integrity during the process.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI supply chain refers to the interconnected processes and components involved in the design, deployment, and operation of artificial intelligence models, emphasizing security and trust.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-446792d60e5d93623fac9c294023d709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8de9ab24149e20dd885bdf7aa0cbc37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc1079c5a2020c1fa8f7ce2c209e6097&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1adafa6fef16a603952c1b37f916c47e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423361</data>
</node>
<node id="Security and Trust Framework">
  <data key="d0">Security and Trust Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Security and Trust Framework is an approach designed to ensure the robust security of AI models throughout their lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security and Trust Framework is a comprehensive approach to ensure AI models are secure, robust, and trustworthy throughout their lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9870dfcb7b266f6b6ac1dd5222b5f58b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422740</data>
</node>
<node id="Heterogeneous AI Components">
  <data key="d0">Heterogeneous AI Components</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Heterogeneous AI components refer to different AI technologies and systems that can vary significantly in their design and function, complicating risk evaluation in the AI supply chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419837</data>
</node>
<node id="Collaborative Learning">
  <data key="d0">Collaborative Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Collaborative Learning is an advanced paradigm in artificial intelligence that involves multiple AI models or agents learning from each other in a cooperative manner, often through peer-to-peer or federated approaches. It emphasizes the sharing of insights and knowledge among participants while ensuring privacy and security throughout the collaborative processes. This methodology incorporates various techniques, particularly Federated Learning and decentralized learning systems, which enable AI models to jointly tackle problems efficiently by utilizing data sourced from multiple distributed locations.

The approach is designed to enhance learning outcomes while maintaining data privacy. Additionally, Collaborative Learning increases the complexity of risk assessments within the AI supply chain and is recognized for enhancing the resilience of AI models against adversarial attacks, thereby making them more robust. It serves as a synergistic strategy where the collective capabilities of participating systems lead to significantly improved learning experiences and results. Within this framework, techniques used in the CoEvolution project specifically focus on joint training to bolster AI systems' resistance to such adversarial threats. Overall, Collaborative Learning represents a cohesive strategy for advancing security and robustness in AI applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f24ba2d35feb8defe20b38929b8da11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-141753ac9ec7e83b0090d110cb431232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bdd45e641a1d84d501219cd34c72fbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d69ac7cb43276601482059fe1cb59288&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93da09e739b2b1da529a083098c37db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3c184b92e7717afad2ff103dd68dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55ca7f18d1ce8e9f212a8d9df6b96398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53324f76aa261271178fe84a61273b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28af3e5b46628e98e598a3a3fb2df917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df6cb12c1afd7894243ba7d6eda4b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f662d06ec1bd0b762ad34da27a7259</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425689</data>
</node>
<node id="Interconnected AI Agents">
  <data key="d0">Interconnected AI Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Interconnected AI agents are AI systems that interact with each other to tackle specific problems, playing a role in the AI supply chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419837</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Risk Database">
  <data key="d0">AI Risk Database</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Risk Database is a repository for reporting vulnerabilities in existing AI models and related threats.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Risk Database is an open-source knowledge base that serves as a comprehensive resource for documenting and analyzing the risks associated with artificial intelligence (AI). It focuses particularly on vulnerabilities and threats that may arise from AI supply chains and adversarial attacks. This database provides valuable data for risk analyses related to AI models and is instrumental for assessments conducted by organizations such as RAGRE. By compiling insights from multiple sources, the AI Risk Database functions as a central reference point for identifying and managing various risks that AI technologies may encounter. Its critical role in understanding and reporting on these risks makes it an essential tool for stakeholders in the field of artificial intelligence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e18b21ad0379cc822498960651f52b17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174fbb753863f4c7c5541414531510d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27653816af61fd8b863293d976ca9654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-156a8e85a6eb2d84a8dc90300df66a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0300fc77e55d052b584b44facfc08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425703</data>
</node>
<node id="OWASP AI Security">
  <data key="d0">OWASP AI Security</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">OWASP AI Security is a framework providing guidelines and best practices for securing AI applications against identified vulnerabilities and threats.&lt;SEP&gt;OWASP AI Security provides guidelines and frameworks for improving the security of AI systems against various threats and vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78f662d06ec1bd0b762ad34da27a7259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425684</data>
</node>
<node id="NIST AI 100-2 E2023">
  <data key="d0">NIST AI 100-2 E2023</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">NIST AI 100-2 E2023 is a document and standard developed by the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) that addresses adversarial and machine learning attack taxonomies. It serves as a framework for categorizing these types of attacks and highlights the importance of compliance and risk assessment in artificial intelligence (AI). This publication focuses on enhancing security and robustness in AI models, ensuring they meet established standards concerning adversarial attacks. The taxonomy provided by NIST AI 100-2 E2023 is aimed at assisting stakeholders in understanding and mitigating risks associated with adversarial and machine learning attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78f662d06ec1bd0b762ad34da27a7259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174fbb753863f4c7c5541414531510d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55ca7f18d1ce8e9f212a8d9df6b96398</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425689</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Assessment Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Security Assessment Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Security Assessment Metrics are defined measures and standards utilized to evaluate the security and robustness of AI models against various adversarial attacks and potential threats. These metrics quantify the security status of AI models, aiding in risk management by helping to gauge their robustness and identify potential vulnerabilities. By employing these metrics, stakeholders can effectively assess the security landscape of AI systems and work toward mitigating risks associated with adversarial challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-78f662d06ec1bd0b762ad34da27a7259&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45b51d1b85498bbe94caadd78db8dc28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bdd45e641a1d84d501219cd34c72fbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c63ecefae511a920b168080d05faae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425685</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Model Bills of Material (AI MBOM)">
  <data key="d0">AI Model Bills of Material (AI MBOM)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Model Bills of Material (AI MBOM) serve as a universal description structure for AI models intended to facilitate regulatory compliance and offer comprehensive support for AI models in a supply chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419838</data>
</node>
<node id="EU High-Level Expert Group on AI (AI HLEG)">
  <data key="d0">EU High-Level Expert Group on AI (AI HLEG)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The EU High-Level Expert Group on AI (AI HLEG) is a pivotal advisory body responsible for formulating comprehensive directives aimed at ensuring trust and fairness in artificial intelligence (AI) applications. This group plays a critical role in guiding adherence to regulatory frameworks, including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the European Data Governance Act. Through its directives, the AI HLEG influences key security standards and shapes the regulatory compliance landscape for AI technologies.

The guidelines established by the AI HLEG are designed to promote the responsible development and utilization of AI systems, upholding ethical standards and fostering public trust. Notably, projects such as CoEvolution align their objectives with the trust and fairness standards set forth by the AI HLEG, demonstrating the group's significant impact in shaping a compliant and ethically sound AI landscape across Europe. Overall, the AI HLEG is essential in driving the discourse on responsible AI integration and regulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f24ba2d35feb8defe20b38929b8da11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b95887f0a735a53175d3a901822dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f58584ea79a787e820a9f9468f6603f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-380d907a4d19fe1f921d130a17586031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9260f7f87786fb6b762b6bf5a25591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170412c84e579196d88270b9230595c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-007d04d0795b80a15b2632f97ec477dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1adafa6fef16a603952c1b37f916c47e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425736</data>
</node>
<node id="European Data Governance Act">
  <data key="d0">European Data Governance Act</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Data Governance Act is a regulatory framework designed to enhance data sharing and management within the European Union while ensuring compliance with privacy regulations. This legislation sets the groundwork for data sharing and governance, promoting principles of transparency and responsible data use. The Act aims to facilitate data sharing and reuse, ensuring that data can be accessed and utilized safely and trustworthily. Overall, it serves to strengthen data privacy and governance across the EU, contributing to a more coherent data ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-007d04d0795b80a15b2632f97ec477dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170412c84e579196d88270b9230595c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f2512422b89fb0b4ab5429166b5bbec</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425738</data>
</node>
<node id="General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)">
  <data key="d0">General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">GDPR is an EU regulation that governs data protection and privacy for individuals within the European Union, influencing the development of ethical AI frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;The GDPR is a comprehensive data protection law in the EU designed to enhance individuals' control and rights over their personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;The GDPR is a comprehensive data protection law in the EU that governs how personal data is processed and protected.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b572f48736ae09487e4539ae10df17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170412c84e579196d88270b9230595c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424890</data>
</node>
<node id="Adversarial Attack Detection and Reporting">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Attack Detection and Reporting</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial Attack Detection and Reporting are mechanisms implemented for identifying and managing potential security threats to AI models during operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419838</data>
</node>
<node id="Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring System">
  <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring System</data>
  <data key="d1">technology</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring System is a part of the CoEvolution approach that detects and reports attacks on AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring System is designed to oversee and report possible adversarial attacks on deployed AI models, enhancing security measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The cybersecurity runtime monitoring system detects and reports attacks on AI systems, enhancing their security during operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ba3c184b92e7717afad2ff103dd68dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71d059c64791540cd7b1be431b2bb96a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424165</data>
</node>
<node id="Work Program Compliance">
  <data key="d0">Work Program Compliance</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Work Program Compliance refers to a comprehensive framework that ensures adherence to structured methodologies and regulatory standards during the development and operation of AI technologies. It involves the integration of context-awareness in machine learning to enhance the resilience of AI applications. The concept encompasses a set of compliance goals, objectives, and key performance indicators (KPIs) established to align with regulatory frameworks and ensure ethical standards are maintained. Ultimately, Work Program Compliance aims to guarantee that AI models not only meet specified project goals but also achieve successful outcomes while adhering to necessary guidelines and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Work Program Compliance refers to the adherence to established secure data sharing protocols and compliance with data privacy laws as part of the CoEvolution project goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Work Program Compliance refers to the adherence to security-by-design principles and resilience against adversarial attacks during the AI model development process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5dd98f6f33ccb6a835a00ac3e5ca4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b717d4f1dbabcdf423e3b9ee479caad5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c021e32ade43efb9ce7c9f584aa7a10c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424893</data>
</node>
<node id="KPI (Key Performance Indicator)">
  <data key="d0">KPI (Key Performance Indicator)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">KPI (Key Performance Indicator) is a measurable value used to assess the performance of AI models in meeting design, security, and operational objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;KPIs are measurable values used to evaluate the success of an organization or project in achieving its objectives, including metrics like throughput, latency, and energy efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e76862a3bd9d83846a1046dc8821573f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755421338</data>
</node>
<node id="Security-by-Design Concept">
  <data key="d0">Security-by-Design Concept</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security-by-Design Concept is a fundamental approach that emphasizes the integration of security measures right from the initial design phase of artificial intelligence (AI) models. This concept is crucial for ensuring that these models are resilient against potential adversarial attacks. By incorporating security principles into the development process of AI solutions from the outset, the concept aims to enhance the overall robustness and integrity of systems. Notably, the Security-by-Design Concept is supported by the CoEvolution Project, which promotes this framework to strengthen AI models against various security threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2207c38cbb6b7a441c7e239591fe5e1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c021e32ade43efb9ce7c9f584aa7a10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73c97665e3b0a28f5563a3906757580a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebc1662a6a8a74f0b8c8d360bafee25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424944</data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Reinforcement Learning (MORL)">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Reinforcement Learning (MORL)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-Reinforcement Learning (MORL) is a sophisticated method utilized for decision-making within the framework of cybersecurity, optimizing actions based on a range of contextual cues and candidate actions. This approach integrates multiple reinforcement learning policies to enhance decision-making capabilities across varying contexts, particularly focusing on optimizing strategies over multiple objectives. MORL is particularly effective in dynamic cybersecurity environments, where it addresses the complexities of making optimal decisions under ever-changing conditions. Through its combination of varied reinforcement learning techniques and contextual vectors, MORL enhances the ability of AI systems to respond effectively to diverse challenges within cybersecurity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2df6cb12c1afd7894243ba7d6eda4b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7db5c56a64621f032196bb4e5b41ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5dd98f6f33ccb6a835a00ac3e5ca4e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425693</data>
</node>
<node id="Decision Transformers (DT)">
  <data key="d0">Decision Transformers (DT)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Decision Transformers (DT) is a method for making optimal mitigation actions based on contextual vectors and candidate actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Decision Transformers are models that utilize transformer architecture for efficient decision-making processes in AI applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Decision Transformers are an AI methodology used to select optimal actions based on context vectors and predefined objectives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2df6cb12c1afd7894243ba7d6eda4b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7db5c56a64621f032196bb4e5b41ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425690</data>
</node>
<node id="adversarial attacks">
  <data key="d0">adversarial attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial attacks are methods used to manipulate AI systems by introducing deceptive inputs or data.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial attacks refer to attempts to deceive artificial intelligence (AI) systems by manipulating input data, ultimately posing a significant threat to the integrity and security of AI models. These incidents target AI systems with the intent to distort their performance or outcomes, representing malicious efforts to confuse or mislead the models during various phases of their lifecycle, including design, training, and deployment. 

The strategies employed in adversarial attacks typically involve manipulating machine learning models, especially neural networks, by introducing misleading inputs or exploiting vulnerabilities that may exist during runtime. The primary goal of these attacks is to disrupt the normal operations of AI models, thereby compromising their effectiveness and reliability. Consequently, adversarial attacks are recognized as critical security threats, underscoring important concerns in risk assessments.

To combat these vulnerabilities, it is crucial to implement robust security measures, which can be monitored through tools such as the CoEvolution Security Runtime Monitoring Engine (SRME). This highlights the importance of ongoing vigilance and proactive protection of AI systems against these deceptive tactics. Evidence of adversarial attacks can also be documented through the SRME, further emphasizing the need for monitoring and addressing these threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial attacks are threats to AI systems that involve manipulating inputs to deceive models, leading to compromised integrity and functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f295eb2f2354216e1d16d8a2d43424b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-084175cf40e1017e4d88e3d24530a078&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b16b97eafd52b6ff9bbda7799176dd86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0be6b7a96133b91256e1b5134cbf3d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f39a1b5cf48158980a9cfbe239a3316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fd21c4597a1403d202414c53457ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d6bf63b8e7794868c19826908bb0e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6e752def2c1fc953cab11b48652f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244047fc3f3388f24f4da567dcd93b63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425682</data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian Techniques are advanced statistical methods that utilize Bayes' theorem to enhance decision-making and model calibration, particularly in uncertain environments. These techniques focus on improving the calibration of algorithms and reducing overconfidence, especially in critical applications where safety is of utmost importance. They are actively being investigated to refine decision support systems within artificial intelligence applications. By employing Bayesian methods, practitioners can effectively address challenges related to decision-making algorithms, thereby ensuring more reliable and robust outcomes in safety-critical scenarios. Overall, Bayesian Techniques play a crucial role in fostering better decision-making processes and enhancing the reliability of various AI-related systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian techniques are methods used for uncertainty quantification, enhancing model calibration and reducing overconfidence in AI-related applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81b5e09ae3d0f914dccc0db6a5f91e22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6047665c4bd29f334a06022d100213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b22cc6f8a153f6e262c2284ced50068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f105761f4d01e1ada210e596eb4751c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5dd98f6f33ccb6a835a00ac3e5ca4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df6cb12c1afd7894243ba7d6eda4b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76862a3bd9d83846a1046dc8821573f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425701</data>
</node>
<node id="EU AI Regulatory Framework">
  <data key="d0">EU AI Regulatory Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The EU AI Regulatory Framework establishes comprehensive guidelines and standards aimed at ensuring that artificial intelligence (AI) systems are safe, ethical, and respect user rights. It outlines clear rules for the implementation of AI technologies within the European Union, emphasizing compliance with safety standards and regulatory requirements. By focusing on the development and deployment of AI technologies in Europe, the framework promotes security and fosters trust, thereby facilitating responsible innovation in the field of artificial intelligence. Overall, the EU AI Regulatory Framework provides a structured approach to guide the ethical and safe use of AI across the continent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2df6cb12c1afd7894243ba7d6eda4b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09248fc5918c5f1aba6cb3c5425fc34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7db5c56a64621f032196bb4e5b41ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425693</data>
</node>
<node id="Genetic Algorithms">
  <data key="d0">Genetic Algorithms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Genetic Algorithms are computational methods used for optimization and search problems, inspired by the process of natural selection. They facilitate the continuous evolution of context vectors within AI systems. Specifically, Genetic Algorithms are utilized in CoEvolution to create and enhance these context vectors through mechanisms such as crossover and mutation. By generating diverse context vectors and operating according to fitness metrics, these algorithms enable the dynamic adaptation and resilience of AI systems, particularly in responding to challenges such as cybersecurity threats. Overall, Genetic Algorithms play a pivotal role in the CoEvolution process, significantly fostering the evolution of AI systems and improving their adaptability over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic Algorithms are computational methods used to evolve context vectors to address emerging cybersecurity threats in dynamic environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5c42e7d5f67c2de98328269247dec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea46f2ec6b238b94a61ace6d4787996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce588e6a41e4a19bd041531ec028f838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7db5c56a64621f032196bb4e5b41ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca81f943b62a3047ee028498003fcafd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09248fc5918c5f1aba6cb3c5425fc34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2df6cb12c1afd7894243ba7d6eda4b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f988512ec39614cc4546bf6fcbeb31e</data>
