  <data key="d2">KPIs (Key Performance Indicators) are measurable values used to evaluate the success of an organization or business process in achieving objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;KPIs refer to Key Performance Indicators set to measure the success of the CoEvolution framework's implementation, including establishing an exploitation group and business model development.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) represent measurable values, such as throughput and latency, that demonstrate the effectiveness of a system.</data>
