<node id="Machine Learning (ML)">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning (ML)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine Learning (ML) is a subset of artificial intelligence that encompasses algorithms and statistical models designed to enable computers to perform tasks without the need for explicit instructions. These algorithms allow systems to learn from data, improve their performance over time, and make predictions based on the information they process. ML is widely applied in a variety of fields, including cybersecurity. However, it is important to note that Machine Learning systems are susceptible to specific adversarial attacks, which can impact their effectiveness. Overall, ML plays a crucial role in data-driven applications, leveraging its ability to learn and adapt for enhanced decision-making and predictive capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-86a552b8b0b6e1c9d217e2714e332435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6eb6aae1af8d6225c491ae5dedc4268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c021e32ade43efb9ce7c9f584aa7a10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdd9d3fe303a1bbac3d5da89d437759c</data>
