<node id="SecML">
  <data key="d0">SecML</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SecML is an open-source Python library and framework developed and supported by UNICA, designed to enhance data protection and testing against adversarial attacks on artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) systems. Its primary goal is to improve adversarial robustness, addressing critical security concerns associated with these technologies. 

The library provides a comprehensive suite of tools and techniques tailored for the evaluation and enhancement of AI/ML security, focusing specifically on defending against various types of adversarial threats, including evasion and poisoning attacks. SecML serves as a vital resource for assessing the resilience of AI models, allowing researchers and practitioners to rigorously test their systems against potential vulnerabilities.

Additionally, SecML functions as an adversarial attack mitigation library that offers defenses related to data management, enhancing protections against both utility-based and privacy-based attacks on AI models. The library underscores the importance of data protection throughout the training and management phases of AI systems.

SecML also collaborates with CoEvolution to further enhance its functionality and security measures. Overall, SecML is an essential tool for anyone seeking to strengthen their AI systems against adversarial challenges while promoting robust and explainable machine learning practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb3c5a6faf3b857ba8d43ec98eb973c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f98f10ca7967e7c93ebec461a36b56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ad886edb819a72a00a95a3d6cb0423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2feb4344e03dd54c5451fb9791afdbfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4258dad8667e5dd4d7e54cbdb071a5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42e0bb84f87fb98c98fd4b4ef1c0cd89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ba33a72c094c154f14017eb9f433f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb47fa58e505f36db27509e998c725c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623872b535f731e898e49b91d42e77f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe098796fa5d6be15d6c84fbf01bf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f8a78502e4359c56e2de032610b38aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033993b2e553c1db5bbfda0fcb2881da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28af3e5b46628e98e598a3a3fb2df917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be52efab763a40f8468f52ebfb67c374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31852725a164a4dd52957ae5c1baa452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af819647c9c59cd69b68bf06821ed32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a53e39ebeb53771231e5e60fb82f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7f2c53ed2b4b73ced4214f41c6193a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f799d77b58dcf9852f1c75b35188b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9db1412409c67345807388c3e65bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4292aa5c93583e2c12ff833c47b4de66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79ea744ae4e3f1f659f9ca366d26d3a5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425705</data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning Adversarial Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning Adversarial Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine Learning Adversarial Attacks involve methods aimed at fooling AI models by providing deceptive input during training and testing phases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419843</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Supply Chain">
  <data key="d0">AI Supply Chain</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Supply Chain encompasses a comprehensive network integral to the lifecycle of artificial intelligence (AI) models and systems across various industries. It involves the processes of design, development, deployment, and management, illustrating the intricate interactions among diverse agents and components within a collaborative network. This framework emphasizes the significance of security and compliance, highlighting the necessity for effective security measures and adherence to regulatory standards to ensure the trustworthiness, safety, and effectiveness of AI technologies.

Specifically, the AI Supply Chain addresses the management of AI technologies in applications such as autonomous vehicles, elucidating the complexities tied to sourcing, governance, and collaboration among multiple vendors within the AI landscape. The interconnected nature of the AI Supply Chain signifies the collaborative efforts essential for secure deployment within established regulatory frameworks and showcases the importance of conducting risk and security assessments at every stage of the lifecycle.

Furthermore, through the lens of the CoEvolution framework, the AI Supply Chain aims to protect these interconnected systems from adversarial threats. The focus on security evaluations and fostering trust within this intricate ecosystem is paramount, as it covers all aspects related to the creation, operationalization, and safeguarding of AI models and their components. Overall, the AI Supply Chain is crucial for the successful deployment and management of AI applications, ensuring a secure and compliant operational environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53f31094c83ab0284e8e350e82c94a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58bbe4f5990fa2bf4939eaf879cf277a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbd5dafa81256fe9f82cfcb884bca559&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641f4278299d91bb3b1622868a1f623d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f98f10ca7967e7c93ebec461a36b56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c472b58c25e3714c3e83d561e34d32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f984a4687c34b201081d48b577fd5ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55ca7f18d1ce8e9f212a8d9df6b96398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402e243c2b3772441ea35e8dba3c710c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4991d2b2e76403b019f2f16989b2a93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ef9abce30618ad5e36237ec9cb39f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6c9cfb6e7abe8b52771b95508dd1919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e539403d1165017fce38ab358660244c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2be40177ccd661e4813abe35732bfb90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788baa379b81a91f164731d4acab9774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589ff2c6b80ad5646240c13df874e58a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11568e1141436db1fb558509a57b48c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5395556365a730e47d5041142ed23c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e396002be0503d0e0baac803477dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-141753ac9ec7e83b0090d110cb431232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d2ff0e7582f72b15822c3c3392a6345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bdd45e641a1d84d501219cd34c72fbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9870dfcb7b266f6b6ac1dd5222b5f58b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9db1412409c67345807388c3e65bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df19f3e87623e77b4872532b8e5d92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4cfff2edf2dca18d266e6392c6acf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce309416a5f270733627cf964258234f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04015f7fafd71cfbdff147b595674db3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f662d06ec1bd0b762ad34da27a7259</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425689</data>
</node>
<node id="Federated Learning">
  <data key="d0">Federated Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Federated Learning (FL) is a decentralized and collaborative machine learning approach designed to facilitate the training of artificial intelligence models across multiple devices or servers while ensuring the privacy and security of participants' data. This innovative methodology allows various entities to contribute to the enhancement of algorithms without the need to share their raw data, thus keeping sensitive information localized on individual devices. 

The primary objective of Federated Learning is to improve model performance by leveraging the diverse datasets held by each participating device while maintaining strict confidentiality regarding users' data throughout the training process. By allowing models to learn from these decentralized data sources, Federated Learning not only enhances machine learning capabilities but also upholds data privacy. It supports a framework where data remains local and secure, enabling multiple parties to collaboratively work on a shared prediction model while preserving the integrity of each user's information.

Overall, Federated Learning represents a significant advancement in the development of AI systems that are both effective and respectful of privacy concerns, allowing for the collaborative learning of a shared model without direct data sharing among participants. This collaborative learning is particularly emphasized within methodologies like CoEvolution, highlighting the innovative potential of multiple AI models training jointly while keeping their data decentralized.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bb3c5a6faf3b857ba8d43ec98eb973c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2feb4344e03dd54c5451fb9791afdbfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4258dad8667e5dd4d7e54cbdb071a5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ba33a72c094c154f14017eb9f433f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623872b535f731e898e49b91d42e77f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6c9cfb6e7abe8b52771b95508dd1919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e82353b035ba082060e064ac9ff6c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e539403d1165017fce38ab358660244c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31852725a164a4dd52957ae5c1baa452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-141753ac9ec7e83b0090d110cb431232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a53e39ebeb53771231e5e60fb82f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f995ea0aa653e5c578ea2df5d9ff710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9db1412409c67345807388c3e65bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0300fc77e55d052b584b44facfc08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5d99a66a08e8bad40aa04612a33b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7eb27e85547c9abe2d9ef4fddd0513a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4cfff2edf2dca18d266e6392c6acf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2be5c8354db5456b4254a51a65a6f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424910</data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Learning">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Decentralized Learning involves multiple independent learners that collaborate while not relying on a central data repository, allowing for diverse AI model training.&lt;SEP&gt;Decentralized Learning refers to the method of training machine learning models across multiple devices or nodes without requiring centralized data storage, enhancing privacy and collaboration among participants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-141753ac9ec7e83b0090d110cb431232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755421339</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Lifecycle">
  <data key="d0">AI Lifecycle</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Lifecycle encompasses all stages from data collection to deployment, highlighting the potential vulnerabilities at each stage.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Lifecycle encompasses all stages of an AI model's development, which include data collection, design, training, validation, deployment, and operation. This lifecycle highlights the importance of addressing security and robustness throughout each phase, as these stages can be affected by emerging threats and vulnerabilities. Each phase presents unique challenges and specific defense needs that must be considered to ensure the integrity of the AI models. Overall, the AI Lifecycle represents a comprehensive framework for developing and deploying AI models while safeguarding against various types of attacks and risks.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI lifecycle encompasses all phases of AI model development, from data collection to deployment and ongoing maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-141753ac9ec7e83b0090d110cb431232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84cf7d8377823cd2796ee572ef8df58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d913cb5322e69bb504986e2098e6b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5185d69b7c5d3118e3df0ca5a428a0e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65261df93ed337be33236b9008ec65a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2be5c8354db5456b4254a51a65a6f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4258dad8667e5dd4d7e54cbdb071a5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424130</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Assurance">
  <data key="d0">Security Assurance</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Security Assurance involves the measures and processes put in place to guarantee the security integrity and trustworthiness of AI models throughout their development lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d2b73d70ce8ebd7530d1462433b2054</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419843</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Risk Assessment and Guidelines/Recommendations Engine">
  <data key="d0">AI Risk Assessment and Guidelines/Recommendations Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Risk Assessment and Guidelines/Recommendations Engine is a component of CoEvolution that identifies risks associated with AI model designs and provides actionable recommendations for risk mitigation.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Risk Assessment and Guidelines/Recommendations Engine is a specialized tool designed to evaluate risks associated with AI models and offer comprehensive guidelines for risk mitigation and enhanced security. As a component of CoEvolution, this engine focuses on assessing various AI-related risks, particularly those arising during the model design phase. It utilizes cybersecurity threat intelligence to deliver valuable insights and recommends effective mitigation techniques tailored to the identified risks. Overall, the engine aims to strengthen the security framework surrounding AI models by providing actionable recommendations driven by threat assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Risk Assessment and Guidelines/Recommendations Engine provides insights on AI-associated risks related to model design and deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e18b21ad0379cc822498960651f52b17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27653816af61fd8b863293d976ca9654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0300fc77e55d052b584b44facfc08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd5d99a66a08e8bad40aa04612a33b6b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424905</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Testing/Assessment Engine">
  <data key="d0">Security Testing/Assessment Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Testing/Assessment Engine is a vital component of the CoEvolution system, specifically engineered to evaluate the security and robustness of AI models, especially those sourced from third parties. It plays a crucial role in discovering vulnerabilities within AI model designs and assessing data biases that could potentially lead to data poisoning attacks. The engine excels in identifying inherent weaknesses in AI models, and beyond merely uncovering these vulnerabilities, it also recommends robustification techniques aimed at hardening the models against various threats. By enhancing the security posture of AI systems, the Security Testing/Assessment Engine ensures that these models are better protected and more resilient to risks, significantly contributing to their overall integrity and reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d53d45e1780332e8c3904aba8e79abbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e18b21ad0379cc822498960651f52b17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27653816af61fd8b863293d976ca9654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425709</data>
</node>
<node id="Defence Flows">
  <data key="d0">Defence Flows</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Defence Flows are an integral component of the CoEvolution initiative, aimed at monitoring and securing AI models against adversarial threats. These Defense Flows consist of a series of complementary defense techniques that are strategically incorporated throughout the AI model's lifecycle. Their primary purpose is to enhance security and ensure robustness against adversarial attacks by assessing, hardening, assuring, and continuously monitoring AI models. By applying these strategies at each stage of the AI lifecycle, Defence Flows contribute to a more secure and resilient AI framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27653816af61fd8b863293d976ca9654</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425706</data>
</node>
<node id="MITRE ATLAS">
  <data key="d0">MITRE ATLAS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">MITRE ATLAS is an open-source framework and knowledge base that provides comprehensive information for conducting risk assessments on AI models. It focuses on adversarial attacks and vulnerabilities within AI systems, serving as a valuable resource for understanding and assessing the risks associated with AI technologies. The CoEvolution engines utilize this knowledge base to enhance their understanding of AI adversary tactics. Overall, MITRE ATLAS plays a crucial role in the ongoing efforts to identify and mitigate vulnerabilities in AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;MITRE ATLAS is an open-source knowledge base that provides information on AI supply chain risks and vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e18b21ad0379cc822498960651f52b17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27653816af61fd8b863293d976ca9654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-156a8e85a6eb2d84a8dc90300df66a77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0300fc77e55d052b584b44facfc08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425703</data>
</node>
<node id="Adversarial Threat Models">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Threat Models</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial Threat Models are various types of attacks considered within CoEvolution, including black-box, white-box, and gray-box attacks, aimed at manipulating AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419845</data>
</node>
<node id="Black-Box Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Black-Box Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Black-Box Attacks are a type of adversarial attack where attackers manipulate AI systems without prior knowledge of the model, relying on trial and error.&lt;SEP&gt;Black-box attacks refer to a type of adversarial attack where attackers have no prior knowledge of the AI model and manipulate systems through trial and error.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422751</data>
</node>
<node id="White-Box Attacks">
  <data key="d0">White-Box Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">White-Box Attacks are adversarial attacks in which attackers have complete knowledge of the AI model, including its architecture and weights.&lt;SEP&gt;White-box attacks involve cybercriminals who possess complete knowledge of the AI model, including its weights and architecture, allowing them to manipulate the system more effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422751</data>
</node>
<node id="Gray-Box Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Gray-Box Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gray-Box Attacks involve adversaries who possess partial knowledge of the AI model, allowing them to exploit certain aspects of it.&lt;SEP&gt;Gray-box attacks describe a type of adversarial attack where the attacker has partial information about the AI model's inner workings, giving them a tactical advantage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422751</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution Security Trust and Robustness (STR) Defence Framework">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution Security Trust and Robustness (STR) Defence Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The STR Defence Framework consists of methods, tools, and services designed to increase the robustness of AI models and mitigate biases in their training data.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Defence Framework is a component of CoEvolution that includes methods, libraries, and tools aimed at improving the resilience and robustness of AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27653816af61fd8b863293d976ca9654</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424142</data>
</node>
<node id="Defence Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Defence Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Defence Techniques are methods applied in the CoEvolution framework to enhance AI model security and robustness against adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Defence Techniques refer to various methods introduced during the AI design process to counter adversarial attacks and enhance model security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7f8a78502e4359c56e2de032610b38aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423380</data>
</node>
<node id="STR Defence Framework">
  <data key="d0">STR Defence Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The STR Defence Framework consists of methods and tools aimed at increasing the resilience of AI models through robustification and adversarial attack prevention.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Defence Framework encompasses subcomponents that provide context-awareness mechanisms for AI models, adapting to various lifecycle phases of deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422751</data>
</node>
<node id="Central Context-Awareness Engine">
  <data key="d0">Central Context-Awareness Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Central Context-Awareness Engine collects context input vectors and generates new context vectors for AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Central Context-Awareness Engine is a sophisticated system designed to collect context input vectors and adapt artificial intelligence (AI) models to varying dynamic conditions. It employs evolutionary algorithms to facilitate this adaptation, ensuring that the AI models are responsive to adversarial contexts. The engine not only gathers context input vectors but also generates relevant context vectors that enhance the operational efficiency of the AI models. Through its capability to continuously evolve based on the collected data, the Central Context-Awareness Engine plays a crucial role in optimizing AI performance in diverse environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c45633c6b079b86215891c3f1d283a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81418f280483fb994ba74151f8e56fb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fa0300fc77e55d052b584b44facfc08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9510fe2b92ae882d551007b5ee87df2e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425704</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution robust AI Model">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution robust AI Model</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution robust AI Model is an advanced AI system incorporating context awareness and security mechanisms to handle adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419845</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Assurance Process">
  <data key="d0">Security Assurance Process</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Assurance Process is an orchestrational framework within CoEvolution that coordinates security evaluations and enhancements for AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security Assurance Process within CoEvolution orchestrates security assessments, ensuring compliance with trustworthiness and fairness standards for AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81418f280483fb994ba74151f8e56fb2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424144</data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Base">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Base</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge Base is the repository of information used by CoEvolution to store data related to AI model vulnerabilities and security enhancement tactics.&lt;SEP&gt;The Knowledge Base in CoEvolution includes three data pools related to trusted AI models, trusted data, and management of AI MBOMs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Knowledge Base within CoEvolution contains trusted AI models, data pools of secured information, and learning resources related to AI security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9510fe2b92ae882d551007b5ee87df2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425704</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution context-awareness approach">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution context-awareness approach</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution context-awareness approach involves mechanisms for contextual adaptation based on adversarial attacks and information collected from AI deployment environments.&lt;SEP&gt;The CoEvolution context-awareness approach refers to the methodology that enables dynamic adaptation of AI models based on their operational context, categorized by various architectural paradigms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e18b21ad0379cc822498960651f52b17</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420441</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Model Security, Trust and Robustness Assurance Flow">
  <data key="d0">AI Model Security, Trust and Robustness Assurance Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Model Security, Trust and Robustness Assurance Flow outlines the processes for conducting security assessments, maintaining trust, and ensuring the robust performance of AI models throughout their lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419846</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution User">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution User</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">CoEvolution User refers to individuals who utilize the CoEvolution platform for enhancing AI model security and implementing corresponding enhancement plans.&lt;SEP&gt;CoEvolution user refers to individuals or entities utilizing the CoEvolution system to realize an STR enhancement plan for AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The CoEvolution User is a role involved in managing the STR enhancement process, realizing enhancement plans for AI models based on the CoEvolution framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d53d45e1780332e8c3904aba8e79abbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425706</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Enhancement Tools and Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Security Enhancement Tools and Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Security enhancement tools and techniques are methods employed to mitigate risks associated with AI model vulnerabilities and adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419846</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Adversarial Attack Techniques">
  <data key="d0">AI Adversarial Attack Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI adversarial attack techniques are strategies used by adversaries to exploit vulnerabilities in AI models, aiming to deceive or manipulate their outputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419846</data>
</node>
<node id="Training Data">
  <data key="d0">Training Data</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Training Data refers to the dataset used in the AI model training process, which is assessed for safety, bias, and fairness in the CoEvolution framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data refers to the data used during the creation of AI models, which must be evaluated for bias and security vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77b8b5bf7e419d5685f26851e9d9d67a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420442</data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Phase Tools and Services">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Phase Tools and Services</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment Phase Tools and Services are critical components utilized during the deployment of AI models, specifically designed to enhance their security and ensure reliable operation in potentially hostile environments. These tools and services work within the framework of CoEvolution, where they provide mechanisms aimed at protecting AI models from adversarial attacks. By focusing on security and adaptability, Deployment Phase Tools and Services help maintain the robustness of AI systems during their operational phase, enabling them to perform effectively in real-time scenarios while withstanding various challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-66fca2dcc4ffc686abf4bc2b366e1860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c45633c6b079b86215891c3f1d283a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424147</data>
</node>
<node id="Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring Engine">
  <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring Engine is a sophisticated system associated with CoEvolution that is specifically designed to monitor the deployment of AI models for security breaches and adversarial attacks. This engine plays a crucial role in observing and reporting potential incidents related to adversarial attacks on these deployed AI models. It functions as a vital component that not only detects attack attempts against the models but also aids in maintaining their security throughout their operational lifespan. By overseeing the entire process, the Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring Engine ensures that AI models remain secure while in use.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cybersecurity Runtime Monitoring Engine is part of the CoEvolution framework that monitors attacks on AI models and reports incidents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f24ba2d35feb8defe20b38929b8da11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bdd45e641a1d84d501219cd34c72fbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f735046fbbdc14f326a8f041cac6de9a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424910</data>
</node>
<node id="Data Generation Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Data Generation Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Data Generation Mechanism is a sophisticated tool being developed within the CoEvolution project, aimed at generating necessary data for various use cases. It serves as a reliable ground truth for diverse datasets, playing a crucial role in supporting the training of artificial intelligence models. By generating trusted data, the Data Generation Mechanism ensures that adequate test scenarios and model evaluations are conducted, which enhances the utility of AI training processes.

Often referred to as the CoEvolution simulator, this mechanism is tailored to meet use-case specific requirements, thereby ensuring the integrity and relevance of the datasets utilized. Additionally, it facilitates the generation of data that can assist third-party datasets, making it an essential component of the CoEvolution hub's offerings. Through its comprehensive capabilities, the Data Generation Mechanism significantly contributes to the advancement and reliability of AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-66fca2dcc4ffc686abf4bc2b366e1860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53d45e1780332e8c3904aba8e79abbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6a0f23e95fea1a56df838e0e512fb24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f735046fbbdc14f326a8f041cac6de9a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426350</data>
</node>
<node id="Trusted Data Pool">
  <data key="d0">Trusted Data Pool</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Trusted Data Pool is a repository where data, after undergoing security enhancements, is stored for use in training AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Trusted Data Pool is a secure repository within CoEvolution where data that has passed security checks is stored for use in AI model training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423376</data>
</node>
<node id="Simulation Environment">
  <data key="d0">Simulation Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Simulation Environment is a controlled setting where CoEvolution generated models can be tested for their performance and security against adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Simulation Environment is a setting in which the CoEvolution generated models can be tested to ensure their performance and robustness under various conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-66fca2dcc4ffc686abf4bc2b366e1860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424146</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution Threat Models">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution Threat Models</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">CoEvolution Threat Models are comprehensive frameworks or schemas designed to outline and analyze potential threats and vulnerabilities faced by AI systems throughout their lifecycle. These models play a critical role during the assessment process, helping to identify and mitigate potential risks related to adversarial attacks on AI models. By encompassing various scenarios, CoEvolution Threat Models effectively represent the spectrum of possible threats against AI systems, ensuring a thorough understanding of their vulnerabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;CoEvolution Threat Models encompass various strategies and methodologies employed to assess the vulnerability of AI models during their operational phases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdf0ef74c7d451fed43129ef79275910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f799d77b58dcf9852f1c75b35188b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425709</data>
</node>
<node id="STR Assurance Flow">
  <data key="d0">STR Assurance Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The STR Assurance Flow is a process within CoEvolution aimed at ensuring the security and robustness of AI models throughout their lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Assurance Flow is a systematic approach used by CoEvolution to enhance security, trust, and robustness in AI models throughout their lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Assurance Flow is a systematic process for securing AI models and assessing their vulnerabilities and risks during development and deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c366ab8df2f44a9f385a6868c2d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecbb8d6faeb4401c8c7650d9f9d214d1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422754</data>
</node>
<node id="RAGRE">
  <data key="d0">RAGRE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">RAGRE, which stands for Risk Assessment, Guidelines, and Recommendations Engine, is a comprehensive engine specifically designed for the systematic assessment and management of risks associated with artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It prioritizes proactive risk identification and compliance with relevant AI regulations and ethical standards. As an integral part of the CoEvolution framework, RAGRE serves a critical role within the AI supply chain ecosystem, enabling effective risk management practices tailored to the entire lifecycle of AI development.

RAGRE is particularly focused on evaluating AI-related risks through a structured algorithm that generates initial risk assessment results. These results are subsequently utilized by the STR Testing/Assessment Engine for security testing. The engine is adept at extracting pertinent regulatory and legislative risks, facilitating the creation of a regulatory sandbox for the AI models being evaluated. This allows for a more comprehensive approach to risk management as it not only assesses security risks but also provides robust recommendations and contextual guidelines that support the secure development and deployment of AI technologies.

By systematically evaluating risks tied to AI development, RAGRE enhances the ability to recommend optimal mitigation actions based on contextual awareness, contributing significantly to the risk assessment processes within the AI ecosystem. Overall, RAGRE aims to ensure the effective implementation of risk management practices throughout the entire AI development process, reinforcing the importance of security and compliance in the evolving landscape of artificial intelligence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cea29209e72133bb93f48ee121efe0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b73d4bb0dd8d885f8eae5c8842c1ea98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2a45c222140df04434355f127ac357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174fbb753863f4c7c5541414531510d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f799d77b58dcf9852f1c75b35188b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c366ab8df2f44a9f385a6868c2d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f7c6a9a08e9c022ee9a774571a1ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-368e0742f36b9f4943d23f312bee77a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f735046fbbdc14f326a8f041cac6de9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424918</data>
</node>
<node id="STR Testing/Assessment Engine">
  <data key="d0">STR Testing/Assessment Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The STR Testing/Assessment Engine is an advanced entity that extends the functionality of the RAGRE framework, specifically designed to conduct adversarial attack security testing on AI models throughout their lifecycle. This engine focuses on assessing the security vulnerabilities and resilience of AI models by simulating adversarial attacks. It also incorporates risk assessment results into its methodologies, enhancing the overall effectiveness of the security testing processes. The STR Testing/Assessment Engine operates at various stages of the AI model lifecycle, ensuring comprehensive security evaluations against potential threats.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Testing/Assessment Engine performs adversarial attack security tests on AI models during different phases of their lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b73d4bb0dd8d885f8eae5c8842c1ea98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2a45c222140df04434355f127ac357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424146</data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Services Act (DSA)">
  <data key="d0">Digital Services Act (DSA)</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Digital Services Act (DSA) is a comprehensive piece of legislation in the European Union that governs digital services, focusing on enhancing transparency and accountability in online activities, including the deployment of artificial intelligence (AI). Aimed at creating a safer digital environment, the DSA seeks to protect users' rights and addresses various online issues. This proposed regulation is designed to influence ethical considerations in AI deployment and data usage practices, establishing a robust legislative framework for the digital space.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digital Services Act aims to create a safer digital space by regulating content and enhancing accountability for online platforms.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digital Services Act is a regulation that addresses digital services and online platforms, focusing on user safety and accountability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-174fbb753863f4c7c5541414531510d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d31a9f46c18f75b8bffad97afd44ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32c9082aac6fd2a45950240834514168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f7c6a9a08e9c022ee9a774571a1ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425707</data>
</node>
<node id="cyber security">
  <data key="d0">cyber security</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Cyber security encompasses various practices aimed at protecting digital systems and data from cyber threats, and is a central theme in the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419847</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Model">
  <data key="d0">AI Model</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Models are sophisticated representations of artificial intelligence systems, specifically associated with AI MBOM, that capture essential data and attributes critical for governance and validation. They encompass various forms of AI that are assessed, enhanced, and managed within the CoEvolution framework. An AI Model represents a machine learning or deep learning system scrutinized for security vulnerabilities and compliance with established standards.

These models consist of a structured set of algorithms and computational systems designed to simulate human intelligence and perform tasks autonomously in diverse applications. Within the CoEvolution initiative, AI Models are fortified with strong defenses to ensure their robustness against adversarial attacks and issues related to data privacy. They employ security mechanisms that are vital for sectors like supply chain operations, where the models learn from data inputs and adapt to changing conditions.

To uphold their effectiveness and integrity, AI Models undergo rigorous testing and validation processes, particularly through the CoEvolution testing protocols. This detailed evaluation is crucial for identifying potential vulnerabilities and mitigating associated risks, underscoring the necessity for robust design and thorough security measures. Additionally, compliance with stringent security and regulatory standards necessitates careful documentation and validation of training procedures, performance metrics, and risk assessments.

Continuous updates are essential for fortifying the security and adaptability of AI Models, reflecting a proactive approach to managing emerging challenges. Frameworks such as the SRME are instrumental in this validation process, ensuring that AI Models remain not only secure but also optimized for performance. Overall, AI Models play a pivotal role in the CoEvolution ecosystem, highlighting the importance of maintaining robust security protocols while adapting to the dynamic technological landscape.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-641f4278299d91bb3b1622868a1f623d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b217cefad4abec670ed7ca0d4128679d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a591c892291649de34c3de312c2e971a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c9765c6de5d09adbaa4008d62e0503a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77b8b5bf7e419d5685f26851e9d9d67a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d1f4cd119004da61bb670635808ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b65576c05d96906d2692fc35b3941f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-237babba3957b0c4786b5021cd8884d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1fe0ecca82dae0573c929fdb53a66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d31a9f46c18f75b8bffad97afd44ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c45633c6b079b86215891c3f1d283a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dd242577c3ba63c0f548e5aa31a5820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033993b2e553c1db5bbfda0fcb2881da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ca67a0bb25d96a23d5612a2c95b2d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa4c1166600f780f6e57409778e6ccb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f799d77b58dcf9852f1c75b35188b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c366ab8df2f44a9f385a6868c2d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f735046fbbdc14f326a8f041cac6de9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bf89d2914639395cf5f6232246af9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f295eb2f2354216e1d16d8a2d43424b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb4040a2488eeffc23e871128baac597&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169bce82366b2fa52a6ddd1e7e226f5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32c9082aac6fd2a45950240834514168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36176d0f31881be69e8416ed157129c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9510fe2b92ae882d551007b5ee87df2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c59208a0ecce67d91fc2e55e630e3efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425711</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution Security Runtime Monitoring Engine">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution Security Runtime Monitoring Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution Security Runtime Monitoring Engine is a comprehensive system designed to enhance the security of AI operations by monitoring them for vulnerabilities and protecting against adversarial cyberattacks throughout the runtime of AI models. This engine plays a pivotal role in detecting and reporting inference-related adversarial attacks that may occur during the deployment of these models. It is responsible for managing and validating AI Model-Based Operations Models (MBOMs), ensuring these models are updated and secure from unauthorized access.

As part of the broader CoEvolution project, the Security Runtime Monitoring Engine facilitates security assessment and monitoring for AI models. It orchestrates the STR assurance flow, thereby ensuring the security and robustness of AI applications. Additionally, the engine enhances security awareness by providing thorough incident reporting mechanisms, which are crucial for managing attacks on AI models. The CoEvolution Security Runtime Monitoring Engine also oversees the AI MBOM pool, implementing authorization and governance procedures that contribute to the overall security assessment of AI operations. Through real-time oversight and feedback mechanisms, it effectively addresses security concerns, making it an integral component in the protection and operational integrity of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The CoEvolution Security Runtime Monitoring Engine is responsible for managing the AI MBOM structure and orchestrating the STR assurance flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b73d4bb0dd8d885f8eae5c8842c1ea98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f25b7f6ba3568504f9c7a701e1f5090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d31a9f46c18f75b8bffad97afd44ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27b1556780c0b0e7572891216ab0741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c366ab8df2f44a9f385a6868c2d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dd242577c3ba63c0f548e5aa31a5820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e2cc45e905008af3bd387b458c2d616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c45633c6b079b86215891c3f1d283a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c63ecefae511a920b168080d05faae</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425706</data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Evaluation Engine">
  <data key="d0">Technical Evaluation Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Technical Evaluation Engine is a key component within the RAGRE framework, tasked with evaluating risks associated with AI models. It implements a regulatory sandbox approach to assess identified risks comprehensively. This engine conducts evaluations across various risk verticals, ensuring that AI models comply with both regulatory and industry standards. Through its systematic assessment process, the Technical Evaluation Engine plays a crucial role in the broader context of responsible AI governance and regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Technical Evaluation Engine within RAGRE scrutinizes and evaluates AI models against regulatory and industry standards for risk assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Technical Evaluation Engine is part of RAGRE that evaluates identified risks in AI models by ensuring they meet regulatory and industry standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b73d4bb0dd8d885f8eae5c8842c1ea98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2a45c222140df04434355f127ac357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424913</data>
</node>
<node id="supply chain ecosystem">
  <data key="d0">supply chain ecosystem</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The supply chain ecosystem refers to the network formed by AI development and deployment, encompassing all actors, models, and processes involved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419847</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution STR Testing/Assessment Engine">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution STR Testing/Assessment Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution STR Testing/Assessment Engine is a specialized and advanced tool designed for conducting security assessments and adversarial attack testing specifically on AI models. It plays a crucial role in risk assessment and security validation, utilizing results from initial risk assessments to inform regulatory compliance. This comprehensive system aids organizations in identifying vulnerabilities within their AI models, thereby enhancing the overall security posture against potential adversarial threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f799d77b58dcf9852f1c75b35188b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf0ef74c7d451fed43129ef79275910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bf89d2914639395cf5f6232246af9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425710</data>
</node>
<node id="Adversarial Attack Red Team">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Attack Red Team</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Adversarial Attack Red Team functions as a dedicated group intended to conduct security testing and identify vulnerabilities in AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Adversarial Attack Red Team refers to a group or concept focused on evaluating AI models through simulated attacks for security testing purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Adversarial Attack Red Team refers to a group or framework that conducts targeted adversarial attack simulations on AI models to identify weaknesses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdf0ef74c7d451fed43129ef79275910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bf89d2914639395cf5f6232246af9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425710</data>
</node>
<node id="Adversarial Attack Libraries">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Attack Libraries</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial Attack Libraries are collections of tools and techniques designed for evaluating and testing AI models against adversarial attacks. These libraries, such as SecML and the Adversarial Robustness Toolbox (ART), offer essential resources for security testing, enabling users to assess how AI models perform under various adversarial attack scenarios and vectors. By providing comprehensive frameworks, these libraries play a crucial role in the robustness evaluation of AI systems, ensuring that vulnerabilities to adversarial attacks are identified and addressed effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdf0ef74c7d451fed43129ef79275910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174fbb753863f4c7c5541414531510d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425711</data>
</node>
<node id="Generative Learning Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Generative Learning Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Generative Learning Techniques are a set of methodologies employed in artificial intelligence (AI) aimed at enhancing learning processes and improving the security and resilience of AI models against potential threats. These techniques involve the creation of perturbated data derived from existing datasets, which is especially useful in adversarial training scenarios. By generating this altered data, Generative Learning Techniques contribute significantly to testing and reinforcing the robustness of AI models, effectively mitigating the impact of adversarial attacks and thereby strengthening the security and reliability of AI systems.

These methods are not only mentioned in the context of data generation mechanisms but are also specifically proposed by projects such as the CoEvolution project, with the goal of disrupting adversarial attacks and creating more secure AI systems. Additionally, Generative Learning Techniques are utilized to create synthetic data that serves to train AI models, further enhancing their robustness against potential adversarial threats. In essence, Generative Learning Techniques encompass a range of strategies for generating data and improving model training through techniques like perturbation, making them integral components in the ongoing effort to fortify AI against malicious interference.&lt;SEP&gt;Generative Learning Techniques are advanced methodologies used to create perturbated data for testing AI models, focusing on attacks like Adversarial Sample Generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Generative Learning Techniques are methods incorporated in the CoEvolution project to improve AI models' robustness to adversarial challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdf0ef74c7d451fed43129ef79275910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d69ac7cb43276601482059fe1cb59288&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8782f7bcbf75d4d1028092d25490a43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb9ddb0c5f55caea9f52e4feaa7073c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f984a4687c34b201081d48b577fd5ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e00a0c381689061b9602b16e3966e85a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebc1662a6a8a74f0b8c8d360bafee25</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425708</data>
</node>
<node id="Membership Inference Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Membership Inference Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Membership Inference Techniques are methods employed to ascertain whether a specific data point was included in the training dataset of a machine learning model. These techniques are crucial for evaluating privacy risks associated with artificial intelligence systems, as they can potentially compromise individual privacy. By exploiting the parameters or structures of the model, Membership Inference Techniques can be used to recover details about the training datasets, raising concerns about data confidentiality. Overall, these methods highlight the vulnerabilities present in AI systems regarding the protection of sensitive information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f799d77b58dcf9852f1c75b35188b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f984a4687c34b201081d48b577fd5ba</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424920</data>
</node>
<node id="Side Channel Analysis Leakage Assessment Laboratory">
  <data key="d0">Side Channel Analysis Leakage Assessment Laboratory</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Side Channel Analysis Leakage Assessment Laboratory is a specialized facility that provides comprehensive assessments concerning side channel information leakage from AI model infrastructures. The laboratory evaluates vulnerabilities in AI models specifically related to side-channel attacks, concentrating on the computational infrastructure, which includes various components such as CPUs and GPUs. Through its assessments, the laboratory aims to identify potential weaknesses in AI models during computation, thereby enhancing the security of these systems against side channel attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fdf0ef74c7d451fed43129ef79275910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425713</data>
</node>
<node id="Adversarial Attack Categories">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Attack Categories</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial Attack Categories classify different types of attacks that can undermine the integrity and performance of AI models, necessitating specific defensive strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial Attack Categories refer to different types of attacks that can be launched against AI models, including poisoning attacks, model extraction attacks, and inference attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial Attack Categories refer to distinct types of strategies or methods used to challenge the robustness of AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-007d04d0795b80a15b2632f97ec477dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170412c84e579196d88270b9230595c0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424890</data>
</node>
<node id="Poisoning Attack">
  <data key="d0">Poisoning Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A Poisoning Attack refers to a type of adversarial attack specifically aimed at compromising the integrity of an AI model by manipulating its training data. This is achieved through the injection of malicious input into the training dataset, which can alter the model's performance and functionality. As a focused concern within AI security, poisoning attacks target the data used for training, ultimately aiming to undermine the reliability and effectiveness of AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6a811cf4a60bc95db18b65f20632b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa30290535797abf91b21ba17f34f254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4292aa5c93583e2c12ff833c47b4de66</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425713</data>
</node>
<node id="Model Extraction Attack">
  <data key="d0">Model Extraction Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Model Extraction Attack involves attempts to reverse-engineer a model to understand its architecture and parameters, typically by querying it.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419848</data>
</node>
<node id="Model Inference Attack">
  <data key="d0">Model Inference Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Model Inference Attack refers to attempts to infer sensitive information about the training data from the output of the AI model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419848</data>
</node>
<node id="FL Cases">
  <data key="d0">FL Cases</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">FL Cases refer to scenarios involving Federated Learning, a machine learning approach that trains models across decentralized devices while keeping data localized.&lt;SEP&gt;FL cases refer to scenarios in Federated Learning where multiple client models are aggregated and can be susceptible to adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df9be928781e92fad424ec1fee49772f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420445</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution Security Assessment Engine">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution Security Assessment Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution Security Assessment Engine is a system that evaluates adversarial attack metrics, providing percentage values for various detection and repair rates.&lt;SEP&gt;The CoEvolution Security Assessment Engine is a tool designed to assess various metrics related to adversarial attacks on AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;The CoEvolution Security Assessment Engine is responsible for providing assessment metrics regarding AI model security, particularly focusing on adversarial attack resistance and optimization of various detection and repair rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa30290535797abf91b21ba17f34f254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef3f714a2a32270c0d8af28dae9557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-624f2387785876b8e9add5d5b236075f</data>
