<node id="EU AI Act">
  <data key="d0">EU AI Act</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The EU AI Act is a comprehensive legislative framework proposed by the European Union that aims to regulate artificial intelligence (AI) systems within its member states. Its primary objectives are to ensure safety, accountability, and ethical usage of AI technologies, particularly those classified as high-risk. The Act encompasses regulations that govern the entire lifecycle of AI technologies, from design and implementation to decommissioning. This process promotes safety and trustworthiness in accordance with established European regulations.

Central to the EU AI Act are essential principles such as transparency, security, and ethical standards, which are vital for managing the risks associated with advanced AI technologies. The Act mandates compliance with specific guidelines that influence various aspects of AI applications, including rigorous risk assessments and security mechanisms. By addressing concerns related to security and privacy, the EU AI Act aims to foster the positive societal impacts of AI while effectively mitigating potential harms.

The framework reflects the EU's commitment to balancing rapid technological advancements with existing legal and moral boundaries. It promotes accountability across all sectors involved in AI applications and ensures that AI systems align with European ethics and legal standards. Furthermore, the EU AI Act highlights the need for proper management of weaknesses in the AI supply chain and underscores its relevance to initiatives such as the CoEvolution project, which aims to adhere to ethical standards and promote responsible AI development.

Overall, the EU AI Act represents a significant step towards the responsible and ethical deployment of AI in Europe, emphasizing the importance of ethical considerations, compliance, and data privacy in the development of AI technologies and their implications for the market.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db75b2cab1362b7796ff2a8753c4245e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbd5dafa81256fe9f82cfcb884bca559&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-174fbb753863f4c7c5541414531510d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a849a6c0719d6015ef6c319e7b3a4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b217cefad4abec670ed7ca0d4128679d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6353e9bcf3d45e130811688e5860477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a591c892291649de34c3de312c2e971a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55ca7f18d1ce8e9f212a8d9df6b96398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fd21c4597a1403d202414c53457ac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d6bf63b8e7794868c19826908bb0e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c67b0558b13d1d04ff0092eb88d7122&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b65576c05d96906d2692fc35b3941f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b8f0f1e7c38faeeea47d2a2b05dab74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c655315fcd0b9413217de724415bfd65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d31a9f46c18f75b8bffad97afd44ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27983f12f5c86c0463eca065b4d5542d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f7c6a9a08e9c022ee9a774571a1ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8de9ab24149e20dd885bdf7aa0cbc37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5bd329614b1182e2be9469625326eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4af943851da76b28e80907078f658e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecef4657b9eaa07737a23410c0933ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4011fe5c8f325cbfb6257057dcfc79c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2be40177ccd661e4813abe35732bfb90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788baa379b81a91f164731d4acab9774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ca67a0bb25d96a23d5612a2c95b2d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa4c1166600f780f6e57409778e6ccb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f40649ce109d07f952bef06c2fd267e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce588e6a41e4a19bd041531ec028f838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e396002be0503d0e0baac803477dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a47fdddee4a142d2b715a993f104b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7595c8200e32fa30ada5bd766b8a892&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c366ab8df2f44a9f385a6868c2d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75efa432cb6a9347528127bab93b2e22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f735046fbbdc14f326a8f041cac6de9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-799b067a273693cb100c626ffac8631e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4e4ed58eff7ae3d119d2cc4a4dc34f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd021e77c6a98f8d589a96e248297baf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284cd6a9713f3db6c2c93c7cc55157ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f295eb2f2354216e1