<node id="Policy Makers">
  <data key="d0">Policy Makers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Policy Makers are individuals and regulatory bodies responsible for developing and overseeing regulations and frameworks pertinent to artificial intelligence (AI) practices. They play a crucial role in formulating policy frameworks that directly impact the implementation and standards of AI systems, particularly significant for CoEvolution initiatives. Engaged in AI ethics and governance, Policy Makers ensure that AI technologies comply with established regulations, thereby fostering safety and trustworthiness in AI models. 

By leveraging frameworks aligned with regulatory standards, notably those of the European Union, Policy Makers support the development of trustworthy AI. They are tasked with creating regulations and guidelines that govern AI technology and its use, while also promoting ethical governance in AI systems and ensuring adherence to evolving regulatory requirements. Furthermore, they can utilize CoEvolution's frameworks to align with EU regulations, facilitating the establishment of secure and ethical AI standards. Thus, Policy Makers play an integral role in shaping the ethical landscape and governance of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Policy Makers are involved with CoEvolution for the development of AI governance frameworks and security standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a11effda0341e9607fb32b151bd7543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebc1662a6a8a74f0b8c8d360bafee25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a859909fffb7947b2b88ac3fcc588943&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d69ac7cb43276601482059fe1cb59288&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3d753a5ba3bfc0d8c4ec414093b1cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb9ddb0c5f55caea9f52e4feaa7073c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71d059c64791540cd7b1be431b2bb96a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5c5b42d758f0e912d601391fdcb4fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce309416a5f270733627cf964258234f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba3c184b92e7717afad2ff103dd68dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8782f7bcbf75d4d1028092d25490a43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70312df5ac32f2a784376ec9acd8debe</data>
