</node>
<node id="European Data Governance ACT">
  <data key="d0">European Data Governance ACT</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Data Governance ACT establishes a comprehensive framework for data sharing, management, and governance within the European Union. Its primary objective is to enhance data accessibility while promoting trust in data-driven innovations and ensuring the ethical and compliant use of data. The act encompasses specific guidelines and regulations pertinent to the handling of data in the context of artificial intelligence (AI) applications, influencing how data is utilized within these frameworks. 

Throughout its provisions, the European Data Governance ACT emphasizes the significance of privacy and security, thereby fostering an environment that balances innovation with the protection of individual rights. It outlines regulations for data usage and governance within the EU, which are essential for the development of trustworthy AI systems. Additionally, the act pertains to regulations that ensure compliance in data processing projects, such as CoEvolution, and relates to guidelines that facilitate effective governance of data handling in alignment with European regulations. Overall, the European Data Governance ACT serves as a pivotal piece of legislation aimed at ensuring robust data governance and compliance standards across the European Union, particularly in relation to AI and data processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f24ba2d35feb8defe20b38929b8da11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f31094c83ab0284e8e350e82c94a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b95887f0a735a53175d3a901822dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f58584ea79a787e820a9f9468f6603f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bed3e842d53d9202844347e7525f7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dda1f142513f65880057e0292e6bbdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c59208a0ecce67d91fc2e55e630e3efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1adafa6fef16a603952c1b37f916c47e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425690</data>
</node>
<node id="GDPR guidelines">
  <data key="d0">GDPR guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">GDPR guidelines provide a regulatory framework for data protection and privacy in the EU, influencing the design and implementation of AI systems to ensure compliance and ethical data governance.&lt;SEP&gt;The GDPR guidelines provide a regulatory framework for data protection that affects the development and deployment of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The GDPR guidelines set directives for data protection and privacy within the European Union and the European Economic Area, impacting AI and data processing practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-007d04d0795b80a15b2632f97ec477dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7595c8200e32fa30ada5bd766b8a892&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1adafa6fef16a603952c1b37f916c47e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424134</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Assurance Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Security Assurance Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Assurance Mechanism is a crucial component of the CoEvolution project, encompassing a series of processes and activities aimed at validating, certifying, and enhancing the security and robustness of artificial intelligence models. This mechanism systematically records all assessments and security processes undertaken to secure AI models, ensuring that they remain secure and trustworthy throughout their lifecycle. By documenting activities related to the enhancement and assessment of these models, the Security Assurance Mechanism generates and maintains security credentials that reinforce the integrity and reliability of AI systems from their inception to deployment. Ultimately, it plays a vital role in the overall validation of the security and robustness of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security Assurance Mechanism within CoEvolution records assessment and robustification activities aimed at ensuring AI models are secure and trusted throughout their lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-141753ac9ec7e83b0090d110cb431232&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff534ba90f98663c29a13338a46795d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef20bc6bd70a2d4b389a72d582866c02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e581cb78a2c2aad223dc49965291dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4cfff2edf2dca18d266e6392c6acf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9db1412409c67345807388c3e65bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e82353b035ba082060e064ac9ff6c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1adafa6fef16a603952c1b37f916c47e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424905</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Researchers and Developers">
  <data key="d0">AI Researchers and Developers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Researchers and Developers are a target group for the CoEvolution project, aimed at being provided with tools and frameworks for building secure AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Researchers and Developers are individuals and organizations actively engaged in the creation, study, and enhancement of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies and methodologies. They play a significant role as stakeholders in the AI ecosystem, focusing on the development of secure, robust, and trustworthy AI systems. These professionals are deeply involved in innovation and the practical application of AI models.

A key aspect of their work is participation in the CoEvolution project, an initiative aimed at refining methods within the AI domain. This project underscores the importance of AI Researchers and Developers in acquiring new research and development knowledge that can inspire innovations specifically designed to detect and mitigate adversarial attacks on AI models. By collaborating with the CoEvolution framework, they gain access to advanced security tools and frameworks that assist in building secure and resilient AI systems.

Overall, AI Researchers and Developers are essential contributors to the progression of AI technologies, dedicated to finding solutions that ensure the safety and effectiveness of AI applications. Through their involvement in initiatives like CoEvolution, they continually strive for innovation in the field while addressing critical challenges such as adversarial risks.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Researchers and Developers are target groups intended to benefit from the project’s advancements in detecting and mitigating adversarial attacks in AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a11effda0341e9607fb32b151bd7543&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba1c9f3141d753938298cb0137770fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9260f7f87786fb6b762b6bf5a25591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ebc1662a6a8a74f0b8c8d360bafee25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71d059c64791540cd7b1be431b2bb96a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5c5b42d758f0e912d601391fdcb4fc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e581cb78a2c2aad223dc49965291dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce309416a5f270733627cf964258234f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c472b58c25e3714c3e83d561e34d32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8782f7bcbf75d4d1028092d25490a43d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70312df5ac32f2a784376ec9acd8debe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1adafa6fef16a603952c1b37f916c47e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2248d6022b436a47f7e30a79038af6d0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756144343</data>
</node>
<node id="Cyber-Security Professionals">
  <data key="d0">Cyber-Security Professionals</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cyber-Security Professionals are individuals dedicated to safeguarding computer systems, networks, and data from various cyber threats. They hold a crucial role within the cybersecurity field, particularly emphasizing the protection of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and infrastructures. These professionals are deeply involved in ensuring the security and integrity of digital environments. Additionally, they are identified as key stakeholders in the CoEvolution project, actively contributing to its objectives related to cybersecurity and the enhancement of security measures in the context of AI. Their expertise is vital in preventing security breaches and maintaining the overall resilience of information systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9260f7f87786fb6b762b6bf5a25591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2248d6022b436a47f7e30a79038af6d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b95887f0a735a53175d3a901822dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1adafa6fef16a603952c1b37f916c47e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
