<node id="EUIPO">
  <data key="d0">EUIPO</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">EUIPO is the European Union Intellectual Property Office that manages the registration of intellectual property rights.&lt;SEP&gt;EUIPO, the European Union Intellectual Property Office, is an agency responsible for managing intellectual property rights within the European Union. Its key functions include the registration and protection of patents, trademarks, and designs. EUIPO plays a crucial role in safeguarding intellectual property and ensuring the protection of innovations across Europe, thereby supporting creativity and innovation in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;The EUIPO (European Union Intellectual Property Office) is involved in the registration and protection of intellectual property rights within the European Union.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f83b9a010b72a12ec39799a44f8c865&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cafddfb6023f95166fd0911d6de46cf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce0736a59c30f8d082e4197fbe818d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7a35ac3afd89edc447fd80276a26a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ee7f9cc09dacb04da20b5e541d35880&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d72b113a4fa1ce0763800ea6022d752f</data>
