<node id="Key Exploitable Results (KERs)">
  <data key="d0">Key Exploitable Results (KERs)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Key Exploitable Results (KERs) are the primary outputs of the CoEvolution project that can be commercially exploited. These results encompass a range of products, services, and demonstrators developed within the project specifically for market exploitation. KERs refer to various valuable outputs generated by the CoEvolution initiative, which are identified as having potential for commercial use. Overall, KERs embody the strategic outcomes aimed at fostering commercial opportunities from the innovations arising from the CoEvolution project.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Exploitable Results (KERs) refer to the significant outcomes from the CoEvolution project, including products, services, and demonstrators, aimed at enhancing data exploitation in industries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-77b573e7bb5a4593f8be0bc8fdb90d44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f83b9a010b72a12ec39799a44f8c865&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7a7b0b92b7a91568312a9b54197ef7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7a35ac3afd89edc447fd80276a26a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d72b113a4fa1ce0763800ea6022d752f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425741</data>
</node>
<node id="Consortium Agreement (CA)">
  <data key="d0">Consortium Agreement (CA)</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">The Consortium Agreement (CA) is a document that outlines the rules concerning IP ownership, access rights, and protections for results generated during the project.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consortium Agreement (CA) outlines the rules regarding intellectual property ownership, access rights, and management among the contributing partners.&lt;SEP&gt;The Consortium Agreement (CA) is a legal document that outlines the rules regarding IP ownership and access rights among the CoEvolution partners.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5611f1258fe52c0e8568e9fe484f3f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6a51bbd5d1752076fc6d00e1c7fb0a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f83b9a010b72a12ec39799a44f8c865</data>
