<node id="Adversarial Attack Detection, Prevention, and Mitigation Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Attack Detection, Prevention, and Mitigation Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial Attack Detection, Prevention, and Mitigation Techniques refer to actions that contribute to enhancing the security of AI models against adversarial threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419863</data>
</node>
<node id="Bills-of-Materials (BOM)">
  <data key="d0">Bills-of-Materials (BOM)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bills-of-Materials (BOM) is a concept introduced in the CoEvolution project that standardizes the description of AI models in the supply chain to improve transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;Bills-of-Materials (BOM) is a concept introduced in the CoEvolution project to unify the description of AI model security components.&lt;SEP&gt;Bills-of-Materials (BOM) is a concept used to describe AI models in a supply chain context, offering a unified approach for ensuring compliance with security and trust standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420432</data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Management and IPR Activities">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Management and IPR Activities</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge Management and IPR Activities refer to tasks within the CoEvolution project focused on innovation tracking, data management, and the development of strategies related to intellectual property rights.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419863</data>
</node>
<node id="Prior Notification">
  <data key="d0">Prior Notification</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Prior Notification is a concept related to the agreements between consortium partners regarding the transfer of jointly created results without advance notice.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419863</data>
</node>
<node id="Open Science">
  <data key="d0">Open Science</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Open Science encompasses a set of principles aimed at promoting transparency, accessibility, and collaboration in scientific research. It encourages open access to scientific publications and responsible management of research data, ensuring that research outputs are publicly accessible. The approach emphasizes open cooperative work, the use of open tools, and the dissemination of knowledge throughout the scientific community. While advocating for these principles, Open Science also seeks to protect intellectual property rights, thereby maintaining a balance between openness and the safeguarding of creators' rights. Overall, it represents a commitment to enhancing the integrity and inclusiveness of scientific processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Open Science promotes transparency and accessibility in research, aligning with the principles of collaboration and knowledge sharing within the CoEvolution initiative.&lt;SEP&gt;Open Science refers to the principle of making research outputs openly available to align with guidelines in EU-funded projects and national policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-39e3880f9db30fa735ddba92055e2f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fed663f83e00c26d63223d3e166e75c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6fbf5dd7af05fd0e193c115784651e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d913cb5322e69bb504986e2098e6b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5185d69b7c5d3118e3df0ca5a428a0e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445008e17e64c0438134e1fefbcf5dfa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425726</data>
</node>
<node id="Compliance Declarations of IP Policies and Procedures">
  <data key="d0">Compliance Declarations of IP Policies and Procedures</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Compliance Declarations of IP Policies and Procedures are agreements signed by partners to adhere to intellectual property regulations during the project lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance Declarations of IP Policies and Procedures are formal agreements signed by project partners to adhere to the established intellectual property regulations and practices in the CoEvolution project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba1c9f3141d753938298cb0137770fa9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425742</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Model Bill of Materials (AI MBOM)">
  <data key="d0">AI Model Bill of Materials (AI MBOM)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Model Bill of Materials (AI MBOM) is a comprehensive framework developed to track the components and security posture of AI models throughout their lifecycle. This framework aims to facilitate enhanced management of the safety of AI systems, ensuring that all elements associated with an AI model are documented and maintained properly. The AI MBOM plays a vital role in the CoEvolution initiative, which emphasizes the importance of managing AI artifacts and their integrity effectively. By offering this structured approach, the AI MBOM significantly contributes to the overall security and reliability of AI technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04015f7fafd71cfbdff147b595674db3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a491dd9e4e112c6a3057fa684923aa8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59ff7acc22c62d7a4184fa090eb2a7c3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424157</data>
</node>
<node id="Security, Trust and Robustness Defences">
  <data key="d0">Security, Trust and Robustness Defences</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Security, Trust and Robustness Defences are measures intended to enhance the safety and reliability of AI systems against potential vulnerabilities and threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Security, Trust and Robustness Defences encompass the methodologies developed to ensure AI systems are secure and reliable in their operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Security, Trust and Robustness Defences refer to measures aimed at enhancing the reliability and trustworthiness of AI models in various applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5611f1258fe52c0e8568e9fe484f3f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70312df5ac32f2a784376ec9acd8debe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424965</data>
</node>
<node id="Collaborative AI Environments">
  <data key="d0">Collaborative AI Environments</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Collaborative AI Environments describe systems designed for sharing data and resources among AI models while ensuring security and privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Collaborative AI environments are systems designed for multiple AI agents to work together, which are considered within the project's scope for security enhancements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04015f7fafd71cfbdff147b595674db3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422781</data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Peer-to-Peer Learning">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Peer-to-Peer Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Decentralized Peer-to-Peer Learning describes an innovative educational system in which individuals, or peers, engage in direct learning from one another without relying on a central authority. This model facilitates effective knowledge sharing and collaboration among participants. The concept encompasses various strategies aimed at enhancing communication and learning for artificial intelligence (AI) within a network, particularly in scenarios where bandwidth is limited. Additionally, it signifies a learning model designed to promote autonomy among AI systems, enabling them to learn independently without centralized control. Moreover, Decentralized Peer-to-Peer Learning fosters a collaborative environment for AI, ensuring that the learning process occurs in a decentralized manner, which contributes to improved security and resilience within the learning framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-237babba3957b0c4786b5021cd8884d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-596574041ec0c369e8cbf7ec7ac9da13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5611f1258fe52c0e8568e9fe484f3f3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755421357</data>
</node>
<node id="AI models">
  <data key="d0">AI models</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI models refer to algorithms and systems designed for various applications of artificial intelligence, particularly in cybersecurity resilience and adaptation.&lt;SEP&gt;AI models refer to the algorithms and frameworks that are trained to perform tasks such as analysis and decision-making within AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422743</data>
</node>
<node id="Work Plan">
  <data key="d0">Work Plan</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Work Plan outlines the structure and schedule for the CoEvolution project, organized into work packages focused on both technical and non-technical activities related to AI model development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419863</data>
</node>
<node id="Cybersecurity">
  <data key="d0">Cybersecurity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Cybersecurity encompasses a range of methods and practices designed to protect computers and networks from digital attacks and damage. It involves not only safeguarding sensitive data and ensuring system integrity but also adapting strategies to counter various threats posed by adversarial entities. The field of cybersecurity is central to initiatives like the CoEvolution project, emphasizing the importance of protecting systems and networks from evolving digital threats. Overall, cybersecurity is essential for maintaining the security and resilience of digital infrastructures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a552b8b0b6e1c9d217e2714e332435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-994816b1606be733f0a98e855a2dbf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09248fc5918c5f1aba6cb3c5425fc34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424138</data>
</node>
<node id="Gantt Chart">
  <data key="d0">Gantt Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Gantt Chart is a project management tool utilized to visualize the timeline and scheduling of tasks within the context of the CoEvolution project. It is instrumental in illustrating the schedule of tasks and milestones over the project's 36-month duration, helping to structure timelines and track progress across various work packages and tasks related to the implementation of the AI project. Overall, the Gantt Chart serves as a critical resource in project planning and management, facilitating effective coordination and oversight of activities throughout the project's lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab48b662719cb842a1786a0c13a6d2cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b3630725878907a8a7fd7b403dc7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589ff2c6b80ad5646240c13df874e58a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424176</data>
</node>
<node id="Consortium">
  <data key="d0">Consortium</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution Consortium is a collaborative group comprised of 18 organizations, including research centers, universities, industrial companies, and SMEs, all focused on addressing challenges related to cybersecurity and artificial intelligence (AI). This consortium operates under the framework of EU funding, which supports financial distributions for its initiatives. The members, from multiple countries, work together to tackle a variety of technological issues and are responsible for managing access to research infrastructure. Additionally, the Consortium oversees the selection of user groups, ensuring that resources are effectively allocated among its members. Through their collaboration, the participants aim to achieve the goals set forth in the CoEvolution project, adhering to the project's terms and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e293777d71c3ca9709a65d86e40e18b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b72b3e7ba1aaeb63a98bb04479fd99ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab48b662719cb842a1786a0c13a6d2cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f0e52ffd2cfc0cefb2f4e79d13f201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bef6d6959d6bcf368dc857e36330e25e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-672abb4b4d866c235db2385a6641554e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424889</data>
</node>
<node id="Austria">
  <data key="d0">Austria</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Austria is a significant participant in the CoEvolution Consortium, where it contributes through its established organizations and specifically brings research and technological expertise to the project. The country is actively involved alongside various nations, focusing on advancements in cybersecurity and AI systems. Furthermore, Austria serves as the base for VELEDAR OMAR, with its specific location situated in Graz. Overall, Austria plays a pivotal role in the consortium's research initiatives and collaborative efforts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80dbc2c57631e342a48a24b95f6e1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd2acaeb0d9437c3f09baa7c94ddf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f80aa6caf939e06fbb5e4bab717d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecef4657b9eaa07737a23410c0933ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7e190ff7826e647efd60e074ebf9f3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425801</data>
</node>
<node id="Italy">
  <data key="d0">Italy</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Italy is a country actively involved in the CoEvolution Consortium, playing a significant role in collaborative research efforts focused on innovating in AI technologies and cybersecurity. As a key contributor and partner in the consortium, Italy provides valuable expertise and resources to help achieve the project's objectives, showcasing its active participation in various initiatives. The contribution of academic institutions within Italy, such as the UNIVERSITA DEGLI STUDI DI CAGLIARI, further emphasizes the country's commitment to the consortium’s goals through its educational and research capabilities. Italy's involvement highlights the importance of international collaboration in advancing technological innovation.&lt;SEP&gt;Italy is a partner country in the CoEvolution project consortium, involved in the development of solutions for AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80dbc2c57631e342a48a24b95f6e1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337883c2db61f2b342a431e196a403af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f80aa6caf939e06fbb5e4bab717d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecef4657b9eaa07737a23410c0933ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f0e52ffd2cfc0cefb2f4e79d13f201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd2acaeb0d9437c3f09baa7c94ddf8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425743</data>
</node>
<node id="Ireland">
  <data key="d0">Ireland</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Ireland is an active participant in the CoEvolution Consortium, contributing significantly to the collaborative research initiatives within the CoEvolution project. Ireland's involvement is marked by its role as a contributing partner, collaborating with other nations to advance the project's goals. The country focuses on various aspects of artificial intelligence and cybersecurity, playing a crucial role in the development and progress of these fields through its participation in the consortium. Overall, Ireland is recognized as one of the key countries engaged in the efforts of the CoEvolution project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80dbc2c57631e342a48a24b95f6e1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f80aa6caf939e06fbb5e4bab717d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecef4657b9eaa07737a23410c0933ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f0e52ffd2cfc0cefb2f4e79d13f201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd2acaeb0d9437c3f09baa7c94ddf8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425804</data>
</node>
<node id="Germany">
  <data key="d0">Germany</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Germany is a participant in the CoEvolution consortium, bringing expertise in machine learning and robustness.&lt;SEP&gt;Germany is a significant participant in the CoEvolution consortium, contributing its advanced research capabilities and expertise in technological advancements. As one of the countries represented in the consortium, Germany plays a vital role in the collaborative efforts of various organizations dedicated to cybersecurity and artificial intelligence (AI). Furthermore, Germany is home to prominent companies such as SIEMENS AKTIENGESELLSCHAFT and SAP SE, the latter of which is located in Waldorf. Through its involvement in the CoEvolution consortium, Germany is not only committed to the project's goals but also supports its development initiatives, highlighting its importance in the fields of technology and industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0797f992209f90df906499cd0d556dd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80dbc2c57631e342a48a24b95f6e1b6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337883c2db61f2b342a431e196a403af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4f80aa6caf939e06fbb5e4bab717d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02286c7e1707a806f9e9959dada558a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-812fdbf446b497f8be08cbf393777bcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecef4657b9eaa07737a23410c0933ea8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2f0e52ffd2cfc0cefb2f4e79d13f201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cd2acaeb0d9437c3f09baa7c94ddf8</data>
