<node id="European Charter of Human Rights">
  <data key="d0">European Charter of Human Rights</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Charter of Human Rights (ECHR) is a significant legal document that aims to safeguard human rights and fundamental freedoms within the European Union. It serves as a foundational text that enshrines essential rights and freedoms for individuals across Europe, reflecting the EU's commitment to protecting these rights. The ECHR delineates fundamental rights that must be respected by all EU member states, which includes legal obligations concerning personal rights. Furthermore, the Charter influences the ethical guidelines of various organizations, including initiatives such as the CoEvolution consortium. Through its provisions, the ECHR establishes a robust framework for the protection and promotion of human rights and fundamental freedoms throughout the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Charter of Human Rights outlines fundamental rights and freedoms within the EU framework, aiming to protect individuals against discrimination and ensuring access to essential services.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06a47fdddee4a142d2b715a993f104b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d798311ba09f5fcfd50eafd690ade83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09c33ff0da3223617dcddd9463b4752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d680583096f4188d4745b78c423dfc52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f0d1e34de2be2bf0ff36b6e60cd080b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1d59e9a7b134e8ee357ab390899ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b8f0f1e7c38faeeea47d2a2b05dab74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c655315fcd0b9413217de724415bfd65</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425745</data>
</node>
<node id="ECHR Article 7 and 8">
  <data key="d0">ECHR Article 7 and 8</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Articles 7 and 8 of the ECHR safeguard the right to private and family life and the right to respect for privacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06a47fdddee4a142d2b715a993f104b5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419865</data>
</node>
