</node>
<node id="AI Model Bill of Materials">
  <data key="d0">AI Model Bill of Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Model Bill of Materials (MBOM) is a novel framework introduced by CoEvolution designed to manage the lifecycle of AI models in compliance with EU directives. This methodology enhances transparency and accountability throughout the entire process of AI model management. By drawing parallels to Software Bills of Materials, the AI Model Bill of Materials aims to report on critical aspects of AI models, including their robustness, security, trust, explainability, and fairness. Through its comprehensive approach, the AI Model Bill of Materials supports the effective oversight and responsible development of AI technologies within the CoEvolution project.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Model Bill of Materials provides a structured description of AI models within supply chains and emphasizes compliance with trust and security standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Model Bill of Materials provides a structured approach to describing AI models in supply chains, focusing on security, trust, and robustness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06a47fdddee4a142d2b715a993f104b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65261df93ed337be33236b9008ec65a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c655315fcd0b9413217de724415bfd65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f179be12e924e7455c61badff1b4c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d09c826db6cef6eb005a363f6b7421e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4490ece625d5431730795ad841da7ddd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425821</data>
</node>
<node id="National Frameworks">
  <data key="d0">National Frameworks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">National frameworks refer to the legal regulations and obligations that member states of the EU must comply with alongside EU legislation such as GDPR and the EU AI Act.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06a47fdddee4a142d2b715a993f104b5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755419865</data>
</node>
