<node id="Matteo Pirotta">
  <data key="d0">Matteo Pirotta</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Matteo Pirotta is a researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the field of multi-objective reinforcement learning. His work gained attention when he presented findings at the AAAI Conference in 2015 and later at the IEEE Symposium on Adaptive Dynamic Programming and Reinforcement Learning held in Singapore. Pirotta's research specifically focuses on the continuous Pareto frontier approximation within the domain of multi-objective reinforcement learning, showcasing his commitment to advancing understanding and methodologies in this area.&lt;SEP&gt;Matteo Pirotta is an author mentioned in connection with research on multi-objective reinforcement learning and continuous Pareto frontier approximation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-084175cf40e1017e4d88e3d24530a078&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353ef7f826378ce1a36bf963412c479b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47baf120bd02482c6b5e1ef64c734077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe098796fa5d6be15d6c84fbf01bf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa31071d35121fae851cd169db2f541</data>
