<node id="Marcello Restelli">
  <data key="d0">Marcello Restelli</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Marcello Restelli is a prominent researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the field of reinforcement learning, particularly focusing on multi-objective reinforcement learning techniques. He has authored numerous publications and is actively engaged in research that encompasses various aspects of reinforcement learning and machine learning. Restelli's work includes multiple research papers presented at various conferences, demonstrating his involvement and interaction with the academic community. He has conducted research on fitted Q-iteration, which further enriches the existing literature on multi-objective reinforcement learning. Additionally, he has made notable contributions to the discussion of Pareto frontier approximation within reinforcement learning studies, enhancing the understanding of multi-objective frameworks in the field. Overall, Marcello Restelli’s research efforts and publications have significantly impacted the domain of reinforcement learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7c3a99346fbbe87f9977443bb6d30d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-084175cf40e1017e4d88e3d24530a078&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353ef7f826378ce1a36bf963412c479b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47baf120bd02482c6b5e1ef64c734077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe098796fa5d6be15d6c84fbf01bf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6926cccac37b74cab2b0acdae6794c42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa31071d35121fae851cd169db2f541</data>
