<node id="Kazuyuki Hiraoka">
  <data key="d0">Kazuyuki Hiraoka</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Kazuyuki Hiraoka is a researcher recognized for his contributions to the fields of parallel reinforcement learning and multi-criteria models. He has presented significant work at the ICONIP 2007 conference, where he focused on the applications and developments within parallel reinforcement learning. His research encompasses a thorough investigation of parallel reinforcement learning techniques, particularly as they relate to weighted multi-criteria models. Hiraoka has authored several papers discussing these techniques, demonstrating his expertise and influence in the study of how parallel reinforcement learning can be applied to various model criteria. Overall, his work highlights the intersection of parallel reinforcement learning and multi-criteria decision-making processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Kazuyuki Hiraoka is a researcher referenced in a paper on parallel reinforcement learning presented at the Neural Information Processing conference.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7c3a99346fbbe87f9977443bb6d30d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-084175cf40e1017e4d88e3d24530a078&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353ef7f826378ce1a36bf963412c479b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47baf120bd02482c6b5e1ef64c734077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe098796fa5d6be15d6c84fbf01bf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6926cccac37b74cab2b0acdae6794c42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa31071d35121fae851cd169db2f541&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42e0bb84f87fb98c98fd4b4ef1c0cd89</data>
