<node id="Manabu Yoshida">
  <data key="d0">Manabu Yoshida</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Manabu Yoshida is a co-author noted in the context of a paper on parallel reinforcement learning presented at the Neural Information Processing conference.&lt;SEP&gt;Manabu Yoshida is a prominent researcher and co-author recognized for his significant contributions to the field of reinforcement learning. He has collaborated with Kazuyuki Hiraoka on a study discussing parallel reinforcement learning methods. His research encompasses multi-objective reinforcement learning and includes participation in discussions and studies related to parallel reinforcement learning, notably during the ICONIP 2007 conference. 

Additionally, Yoshida has worked on weighted multi-criteria models within the realm of reinforcement learning, contributing to a deeper understanding of the complexities associated with this area. He is actively engaged in exploring advanced concepts of reinforcement learning and adaptive margins, reflecting his commitment to advancing methodologies and knowledge in this dynamic field. Overall, his work highlights a comprehensive involvement in various dimensions of reinforcement learning, establishing him as an influential figure in this research domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7c3a99346fbbe87f9977443bb6d30d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-084175cf40e1017e4d88e3d24530a078&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-353ef7f826378ce1a36bf963412c479b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47baf120bd02482c6b5e1ef64c734077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fe098796fa5d6be15d6c84fbf01bf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6926cccac37b74cab2b0acdae6794c42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfa31071d35121fae851cd169db2f541&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42e0bb84f87fb98c98fd4b4ef1c0cd89</data>
