<node id="Taketoshi Mishima">
  <data key="d0">Taketoshi Mishima</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Taketoshi Mishima is a prominent researcher specializing in the realm of reinforcement learning and decision-making models. He has made significant contributions to the study of parallel reinforcement learning methods, collaborating with other experts such as Kazuyuki Hiraoka and Manabu Yoshida. Mishima is particularly noted for his role as an author in presenting research at the ICONIP 2007 conference, where he focused on parallel reinforcement learning techniques. Additionally, he has co-authored research on adaptive margin within the context of reinforcement learning, further showcasing his expertise and active involvement in academic discussions surrounding this field. His work also addresses reinforcement learning in multi-criteria model contexts, underscoring his diverse interests and contributions to advancing knowledge in reinforcement learning and its applications. Overall, Taketoshi Mishima is recognized as a notable figure in related research endeavors, with a strong emphasis on various aspects of reinforcement learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Taketoshi Mishima is a researcher who co-authored a paper on parallel reinforcement learning presented at the Neural Information Processing conference.</data>
