<node id="Work Package 6">
  <data key="d0">Work Package 6</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-504206f0a7bf9dc2f99c1165d4800618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932f1546ff56a5a50a861aaa39f75771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29a64033d909953d984427106205f924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2997d250b69def216aa03988b3bbd6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c3ab8cb1038a2d7402e7c20f7922fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65e8629ae207ceb542cf05ec02b99e6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4810c9b22b0ce26c963075600f4dbd84</data>
  <data key="d2">Work Package 6 (WP6) is a critical component of the CoEvolution project, led by AVI. This work package is primarily focused on the integration and evaluation of project outcomes, emphasizing sustainability planning within its operational framework. WP6 is tasked with collaborating with other packages to ensure effective integration and testing tasks, although it has been identified as needing additional resources to enhance its contributions. Overall, Work Package 6 is dedicated to achieving defined functions related to integration, evaluation, and the successful implementation of outcomes within the CoEvolution project.&lt;SEP&gt;Work Package 6 involves the integration, evaluation, and final project outcomes for the CoEvolution project.&lt;SEP&gt;Work Package 6 is a part of the CoEvolution project focused on particular tasks and deliverables.</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426357</data>
</node>
<node id="SRME">
  <data key="d0">SRME</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f295eb2f2354216e1d16d8a2d43424b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc5395556365a730e47d5041142ed23c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cea29209e72133bb93f48ee121efe0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169bce82366b2fa52a6ddd1e7e226f5c</data>
  <data key="d2">SRME, or Security Runtime Monitoring Engine, is a critical component in the management of AI model integrity and security. Its primary functions include ensuring the authenticity of AI Bills of Material (MBOM) and overseeing the entire lifecycle of AI models. SRME is dedicated to monitoring incidents of adversarial attacks, collecting evidence, and reporting such incidents to safeguard the security of AI models. As a root of trust within the CoEvolution hub, SRME is responsible for validating AI MBOMs, as well as managing their updates or revocation in cases where models are compromised. Overall, SRME plays a vital role in maintaining the trustworthiness and integrity of AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424911</data>
</node>
<node id="SRME AI MBOM Management Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">SRME AI MBOM Management Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb4040a2488eeffc23e871128baac597&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa4c1166600f780f6e57409778e6ccb9</data>
  <data key="d2">The SRME AI MBOM Management Mechanism is responsible for managing AI MBOMs, validating their authenticity and integrity, and providing detailed risk assessment and guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;The SRME AI MBOM Management Mechanism oversees the management and integrity of AI MBOMs throughout their lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424155</data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Agent-Path Planning (MAPP)">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Agent-Path Planning (MAPP)</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71092d984871a58c8af5088c4c2d7412&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afe62a9898a9c027310dea499cc4c9f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbd860797355477b1a599735726a034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04eb3908a7e782600d03aac5599f2893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51db1d0ebfb384f2340004d2031fd42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc1b93aa71559fbb79284d33ce689351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75554414522e9656908eb2a8c6a7c1b6</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-Agent-Path Planning (MAPP) is an advanced collaborative autonomous navigation system designed to coordinate multiple vehicles for efficient travel and pathfinding. It serves as a framework for autonomous vehicles, specifically Connected and Autonomous Vehicles (CAVs), to collaboratively plan paths and navigate complex environments. MAPP enhances operational effectiveness by facilitating cooperative navigation among various autonomous agents, allowing them to seamlessly work together in shared spaces. The primary focus of MAPP is to optimize the path planning process, enabling simultaneous navigation of multiple agents even in intricate scenarios. Through its innovative methodologies, Multi-Agent-Path Planning significantly improves cooperation among vehicles, ensuring efficient and effective navigation tasks in environments that present challenges to autonomous driving.</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424935</data>
</node>
