<node id="Project Work Packages">
  <data key="d0">Project Work Packages</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Project work packages in the CoEvolution Project define specific tasks and roles related to AI model security and data requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420135</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 3.4">
  <data key="d0">Task 3.4</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 3.4 involves data requirements and collection emphasizing the need for understanding data sources for AI model lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;Task 3.4 is an essential component of the CoEvolution Project, centered on the critical processes of data requirements and collection necessary for the effective management of AI models. This task emphasizes the foundational role of data, underscoring its importance in the development, deployment, and ongoing improvement of AI models within the project. By detailing the requirements and collection activities, Task 3.4 plays a vital role in ensuring that the lifecycle of AI models is adequately supported and managed. It highlights the dependence of AI models on data throughout their lifecycle, thereby reinforcing the overall objectives of the CoEvolution Project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f7b898ba71a7016ad21ff4ed438387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8bb95ba3048fe4ba1a028477aaf2b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6a0f23e95fea1a56df838e0e512fb24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d36e00d6638001bed983791ad13038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e66856c7c61c57841b490bae9b068261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b3fb37f452cc350584ba9af9445a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d40ee8239b5807a75857260b7afe44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-853e3c305e010114288cc805df7be8a4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426344</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 4.1">
  <data key="d0">Task 4.1</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 4.1 is dedicated to the development of adversarial attack security testing and assessment techniques for artificial intelligence models, specifically within the framework of the CoEvolution Project. This task aims to discover vulnerabilities in AI models through innovative testing methodologies designed to evaluate their security against adversarial attacks. By focusing on both the development of these techniques and their application in security assessments, Task 4.1 plays a crucial role in enhancing the resilience of AI systems within the project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6a0f23e95fea1a56df838e0e512fb24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f7b898ba71a7016ad21ff4ed438387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d36e00d6638001bed983791ad13038</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755426348</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 4.2">
  <data key="d0">Task 4.2</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 4.2 develops defenses technologies for the design and training phases of AI models to protect against various attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Task 4.2 is an integral component of the CoEvolution project, led by UNICA, dedicated to enhancing the security of artificial intelligence during the training phase. This task specifically focuses on designing technologies and tools aimed at defending AI models against adversarial attacks and poisoning attempts. By concentrating on improving AI training security, Task 4.2 addresses the critical need for robust defenses in AI systems, ensuring their resilience against potential vulnerabilities that could undermine their effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c4f7b898ba71a7016ad21ff4ed438387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19d36e00d6638001bed983791ad13038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c51e62034d566f8ec8ff4a84d94f137&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1bbb9e746eec802a40ceda441e1c95e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911f0045819caa0ee2d858aae2c793ce</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424114</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 4.3 - Deployment Phase Defences Technologies">
  <data key="d0">Task 4.3 - Deployment Phase Defences Technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 4.3 focuses on developing protective technologies for AI models during the deployment phase to mitigate various security threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Task 4.3 focuses on developing security measures for AI models during their deployment phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e930d25a22cedceebd24b60e07cebcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7086ddfd2becc56c4a5d794fb4aa63db</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425667</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 4.4 - AI Model Context-Awareness Enablers for Security, Robustness and Performance">
  <data key="d0">Task 4.4 - AI Model Context-Awareness Enablers for Security, Robustness and Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 4.4 aims to develop a technological framework for context-aware AI resilience in distributed architectures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e930d25a22cedceebd24b60e07cebcd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420136</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 4.5 - Continuous Post-Deployment Defence through Incremental training technologies">
  <data key="d0">Task 4.5 - Continuous Post-Deployment Defence through Incremental training technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 4.5 is focused on developing novel training techniques for AI models to enhance security and robustness incrementally.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e930d25a22cedceebd24b60e07cebcd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420136</data>
</node>
<node id="Task 5.1 - STR AI Model Bills-of-Material Definition, Design and Management">
  <data key="d0">Task 5.1 - STR AI Model Bills-of-Material Definition, Design and Management</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Task 5.1 - STR AI Model Bills-of-Material Definition, Design and Management is a critical initiative within the CoEvolution project, concentrating on the definition, design, and management of AI Bills-of-Materials (BOM). This task is vital for the effective organization and oversight of AI models that are fundamental to the project’s operations. Task 5.1 involves detailing the structure of Bills-of-Material, which includes the training data, dependencies, and the users engaged with the AI models. Through these efforts, Task 5.1 ensures that the components necessary for AI model management are systematically addressed, fostering the successful implementation and functionality of the CoEvolution project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-95ef324e25221cc1aac49364c3a0e044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57d2c1e316de666f7e622f4fd8100245&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e930d25a22cedceebd24b60e07cebcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7086ddfd2becc56c4a5d794fb4aa63db</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425671</data>
</node>
<node id="Security and Risk Assessment engine">
  <data key="d0">Security and Risk Assessment engine</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security and Risk Assessment engine is part of the CoEvolution project, focusing on assessing security risks associated with AI model deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e930d25a22cedceebd24b60e07cebcd</data>
