<node id="Research Data Management">
  <data key="d0">Research Data Management</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Research Data Management encompasses a comprehensive framework that involves the organization, storage, preservation, and dissemination of data generated from research activities, particularly in fields such as artificial intelligence (AI). This framework includes systematic processes for data collection, assessment of technology effectiveness through demonstration tests, and ensuring compliance with various regulations. Research Data Management focuses on developing strategies and practices to effectively handle the data collected during research projects, with an emphasis on maintaining the integrity and accessibility of the information throughout its lifecycle.

Furthermore, it involves adhering to ethical guidelines and legal requirements in the processing and management of research data. This is especially vital in contexts such as AI projects, exemplified by initiatives like CoEvolution, which highlight the need for reliable data management practices to support effective research outputs and facilitate knowledge sharing within the scientific community.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f53ece2cac0b6e9ce607bb71e4557106&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc6fbf5dd7af05fd0e193c115784651e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93ceeb9a936cfc772c88beda8e90f8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d913cb5322e69bb504986e2098e6b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445008e17e64c0438134e1fefbcf5dfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5185d69b7c5d3118e3df0ca5a428a0e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39e3880f9db30fa735ddba92055e2f7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589ff2c6b80ad5646240c13df874e58a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425730</data>
</node>
