<node id="Supply Chain">
  <data key="d0">Supply Chain</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Supply Chain encompasses the entire lifecycle of an AI model, spanning various phases from design to deployment, as discussed in the CoEvolution project. It represents an interconnected network of organizations that are involved in the provision of goods and services from supplier to consumer, particularly in the context of utilizing AI to manage supply processes effectively. This network includes multiple tiers of AI components and vendors contributing to the development, production, processing, and distribution of AI solutions. Furthermore, the Supply Chain relies on AI Model Bills of Materials (MBOMs) for validation and management, highlighting its critical role in ensuring the integrity and efficiency of AI model production and distribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b65576c05d96906d2692fc35b3941f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-380d907a4d19fe1f921d130a17586031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ae0f0567a0d81633f1194f5d9d67365</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425723</data>
</node>
<node id="International Standards">
  <data key="d0">International Standards</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">International Standards are guidelines that aim to regulate and standardize the development, deployment, and improvement of AI systems for enhanced security and ethics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420429</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Assessment Engine">
  <data key="d0">Security Assessment Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Assessment Engine in CoEvolution assesses privacy-related attacks and evaluates defense mechanisms within AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security Assessment Engine is a tool designed to evaluate and quantify the security status of AI models against various adversarial threats.&lt;SEP&gt;The Security Assessment Engine is a tool proposed to evaluate the security of AI models, including their resilience against adversarial attacks and compliance with security metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53324f76aa261271178fe84a61273b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55ca7f18d1ce8e9f212a8d9df6b96398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424889</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Model Bills of Material">
  <data key="d0">AI Model Bills of Material</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Model Bills of Material provide a structured description of AI models, helping to convey compliance with security and trust regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Model Bills of Material provide a structured framework for describing AI models within a supply chain. This proposed universal structure is designed to ensure compliance with regulatory frameworks while enhancing security, trust, and robustness in the use of AI technologies. By standardizing the way AI models are documented, AI Model Bills of Material facilitate regulatory compliance and aim to improve the overall integrity of AI systems in the supply chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f24ba2d35feb8defe20b38929b8da11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f31094c83ab0284e8e350e82c94a02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53324f76aa261271178fe84a61273b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-402e243c2b3772441ea35e8dba3c710c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c59208a0ecce67d91fc2e55e630e3efd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425686</data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralised Peer-to-Peer Learning">
  <data key="d0">Decentralised Peer-to-Peer Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Decentralised Peer-to-Peer Learning is a method of collaborative AI training that enhances model learning by utilizing distributed data sources without centralizing data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53324f76aa261271178fe84a61273b51</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420430</data>
</node>
<node id="Interconnected AI Agents Supply Chain">
  <data key="d0">Interconnected AI Agents Supply Chain</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Interconnected AI Agents Supply Chain refers to a network of AI agents working together to solve problems, each contributing insights derived from its unique data sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53324f76aa261271178fe84a61273b51</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420430</data>
</node>
<node id="AI MBOM Paradigm">
  <data key="d0">AI MBOM Paradigm</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI MBOM Paradigm refers to a method of describing AI models within a supply chain that provides Security, Trust, and Robustness guarantees compliant with various regulatory directives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420431</data>
</node>
<node id="EU Regulation">
  <data key="d0">EU Regulation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">EU Regulation pertains to guidelines that CoEvolution aims to harmonize its project results with, particularly regarding data privacy and security.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Regulation encompasses laws and directives aimed at governing the ethical use and deployment of AI technologies in Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;EU Regulation refers to the legal frameworks and guidelines that the CoEvolution project aims to harmonize with.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff71b865dc936679ff717845aef86de4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5dd98f6f33ccb6a835a00ac3e5ca4e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423365</data>
</node>
<node id="Security, Trust and Robustness">
  <data key="d0">Security, Trust and Robustness</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Security, Trust, and Robustness refers to core principles ensuring that AI models are secure, reliable, and able to operate within ethical standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420431</data>
</node>
<node id="AI MBOM Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">AI MBOM Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI MBOM mechanism refers to a novel design and implementation aimed at providing a framework to guarantee security, trust, and robustness for AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420432</data>
</node>
<node id="KPI3.1">
  <data key="d0">KPI3.1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">KPI3.1 is a specific Key Performance Indicator focused on the design and development of at least two variants of AI MBOM structures within the CoEvolution framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5dfa0262d9cf1261fde3b563bc7f361</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
