<node id="AI Ecosystem Diversity">
  <data key="d0">AI Ecosystem Diversity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Ecosystem Diversity refers to the range of ways AI models are designed and utilized within different systems and applications.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Ecosystem Diversity refers to the variety of AI models and approaches being used within the CoEvolution framework, acknowledging the differences in design and application.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a4e82353b035ba082060e064ac9ff6c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31852725a164a4dd52957ae5c1baa452</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422750</data>
</node>
<node id="Context Awareness Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Context Awareness Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Context Awareness Mechanism is a sophisticated feature that enables AI models to adapt their behavior based on environmental contexts and interactions with their surroundings. In the context of CoEvolution, this mechanism employs a multi-objective decision support system to effectively tailor AI responses to varying environmental conditions. By leveraging decision support systems and strategic adaptation, the Context Awareness Mechanism ensures that AI models can respond dynamically and efficiently to their environments, ultimately enhancing their security status in the process. This novel feature exemplifies an advanced approach to contextual adaptation in AI technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0c4cfff2edf2dca18d266e6392c6acf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4e82353b035ba082060e064ac9ff6c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9db1412409c67345807388c3e65bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9</data>
