  <data key="d2">ISO27001 is a standard for information security management systems (ISMS) that organizations can adopt to manage the security of their information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-174fbb753863f4c7c5541414531510d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420444</data>
</node>
<node id="Privacy Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Privacy Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Privacy Attacks are strategies designed to extract confidential information from machine learning systems by querying them iteratively. These attacks pose significant risks to user privacy by threatening the confidentiality of training data within the models. By employing various techniques, Privacy Attacks can infer sensitive details about the datasets used, thereby compromising the security of both the system and its users. Overall, Privacy Attacks encompass methods that systematically target machine learning systems, exploiting their vulnerabilities to retrieve confidential information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b95c94affa550c2a005eb66b83e0f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6eb6aae1af8d6225c491ae5dedc4268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d188b520ae593ffa16184991a28ba19</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425700</data>
</node>
<node id="STR Assessment Engine">
  <data key="d0">STR Assessment Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The STR Assessment Engine generates reports on security metrics related to adversarial attacks, aiding in the STR enhancement procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Assessment Engine is a component involved in assessing the safety of datasets in terms of bias and poisoning, as well as evaluating AI model vulnerabilities to adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Assessment Engine is a sophisticated tool developed by CoEvolution that focuses on assessing the safety and integrity of datasets and artificial intelligence (AI) models. It establishes methodologies aimed at evaluating the safety of datasets, including their vulnerabilities to adversarial samples. This engine is instrumental in developing metrics that measure the impact of adversarial attacks on AI models. Additionally, the STR Assessment Engine generates detailed reports that outline the security metrics of AI models following the evaluation of these adversarial threats. Through its comprehensive approach, the STR Assessment Engine plays a crucial role in enhancing the robustness and reliability of AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2186aff847bb122f1f1a8eba737faf56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f984a4687c34b201081d48b577fd5ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4292aa5c93583e2c12ff833c47b4de66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6a811cf4a60bc95db18b65f20632b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa30290535797abf91b21ba17f34f254</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425711</data>
</node>
<node id="Defense-in-depth">
  <data key="d0">Defense-in-depth</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Defense-in-depth is a security strategy employed in AI model lifecycles, where multiple layers of defenses are integrated to enhance robustness against attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420445</data>
</node>
<node id="Adversarial Attacks Assessment Laboratory">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Attacks Assessment Laboratory</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Adversarial Attacks Assessment Laboratory, associated with ISI partners, is designed to perform assessments of side-channel-based adversarial attacks and their impacts on AI models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420445</data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Tenant FPGAs">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Tenant FPGAs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-Tenant FPGAs refer to field-programmable gate arrays deployed on shared infrastructures, relevant in the context of federated learning and adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-tenant FPGAs are computing resources that can host multiple client applications, raising concerns regarding security when used in Federated Learning environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-Tenant FPGAs refer to field-programmable gate arrays that are deployed in a shared environment, where multiple clients use the same FPGA hardware for different applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8a6a811cf4a60bc95db18b65f20632b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2186aff847bb122f1f1a8eba737faf56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423378</data>
</node>
<node id="Coevolution">
  <data key="d0">Coevolution</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Coevolution refers to a project focused on enhancing AI design and deployment by implementing various defensive strategies throughout the AI lifecycle to combat adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Coevolution refers to a project that develops robust AI models and technologies to enhance security against adversarial attacks during deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420445</data>
</node>
<node id="Ensemble Learning AI">
  <data key="d0">Ensemble Learning AI</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Ensemble Learning AI is a machine learning technique that combines multiple models to improve prediction accuracy and increase robustness against adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Ensemble Learning AI is a method where multiple models collaborate under a voting system to enhance performance during the AI design phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa30290535797abf91b21ba17f34f254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422758</data>
</node>
<node id="Defensive Distillation Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Defensive Distillation Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Defensive Distillation Techniques involve training base models in an ensemble as teachers and students to improve robustness against adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420445</data>
</node>
<node id="FPGA Fabric">
  <data key="d0">FPGA Fabric</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">FPGA Fabric refers to edge devices that allow for parallel processing and computation, enhancing the robustness of AI models during deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420445</data>
</node>
<node id="Defense-in-Depth Principle">
  <data key="d0">Defense-in-Depth Principle</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Defense-in-Depth Principle refers to a security strategy employed in the design flow of AI models where multiple layers of defense are implemented to protect against adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420446</data>
</node>
<node id="Training Phase">
  <data key="d0">Training Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Training Phase is a part of the AI Model lifecycle focused on preparing the model through data management and defense strategies against threats.&lt;SEP&gt;The Training Phase refers to a stage in the AI lifecycle where models are refined and defenses against attacks are integrated, particularly in compliance with the core technology being used.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6ef3f714a2a32270c0d8af28dae9557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424151</data>
</node>
<node id="Data Management Phase">
  <data key="d0">Data Management Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Data Management Phase involves strategies to protect and manage data used in training AI Models, addressing potential adversarial threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420446</data>
</node>
<node id="Runtime Monitoring Engine">
  <data key="d0">Runtime Monitoring Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Runtime Monitoring Engine is a system that tracks the operational status of the AI model and reports incidents related to adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Runtime Monitoring Engine is a system component responsible for monitoring AI models in operation to detect adversarial activities and report incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;The Runtime Monitoring Engine is responsible for overseeing deployed models, reporting incidents, and ensuring dynamic updates for maintaining security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-033993b2e553c1db5bbfda0fcb2881da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424917</data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Update Mechanisms">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Update Mechanisms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic Update Mechanisms are systems integrated into AI Models to enable real-time updates in response to security threats and new version deployments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-702b309f7879ea6c02c535b54964d126</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420446</data>
</node>
<node id="HE Schemes">
  <data key="d0">HE Schemes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">HE (Homomorphic Encryption) schemes are privacy-preserving methods considered for secure transmission and aggregation of models in federated learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dd67768c95c1d599e1e7d53f932c680</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420446</data>
</node>
<node id="SMPC Schemes">
  <data key="d0">SMPC Schemes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">SMPC (Secure Multi-Party Computation) schemes are also considered for enhancing privacy protection in federated learning applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dd67768c95c1d599e1e7d53f932c680</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420446</data>
</node>
<node id="UCA">
  <data key="d0">UCA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">UCA is associated with well-provisioned adversarial attack mitigation libraries, contributing to the field of machine learning security.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dd67768c95c1d599e1e7d53f932c680</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420447</data>
</node>
<node id="Client Models">
  <data key="d0">Client Models</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Client models are individual machine learning models trained on localized data sets within the federated learning framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dd67768c95c1d599e1e7d53f932c680</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420447</data>
</node>
<node id="Anomaly Detection Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Detection Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Anomaly detection mechanism refers to processes used to identify and reject abnormal or malicious models in a federated learning environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dd67768c95c1d599e1e7d53f932c680</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420447</data>
</node>
<node id="Diversity among Base Models">
  <data key="d0">Diversity among Base Models</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Diversity among base models is a principle in ensemble learning that enhances prediction accuracy and robustness against adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dd67768c95c1d599e1e7d53f932c680</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420447</data>
</node>
<node id="Transfer Learning">
  <data key="d0">Transfer Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfer Learning is an approach in machine learning where a model developed for one task is adapted for a different but related task, enhancing efficiency in AI model deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Transfer learning is a machine learning technique that leverages knowledge from one domain to improve learning in another domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7dd67768c95c1d599e1e7d53f932c680&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4991d2b2e76403b019f2f16989b2a93f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425722</data>
</node>
<node id="Defensive Gadgets">
  <data key="d0">Defensive Gadgets</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Defensive Gadgets are enhancements or add-ons introduced to AI models to improve security, enabling detection and response to adversarial attacks during operation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420447</data>
</node>
<node id="Client">
  <data key="d0">Client</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Client refers to an external or internal entity that interacts with the AI model and may pose threats, such as adversarial attacks, during the AI's lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;In the context of Federated Learning, the Client refers to nodes or devices that participate in the model training process while maintaining data privacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-033993b2e553c1db5bbfda0fcb2881da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424916</data>
</node>
<node id="Server">
  <data key="d0">Server</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Server in Federated Learning acts as the central coordinator that aggregates model updates from multiple Clients without accessing their data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420448</data>
</node>
<node id="Malicious Client Detection Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Malicious Client Detection Techniques</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Malicious Client Detection Techniques are strategies employed to identify and mitigate the impact of clients that may compromise the learning process in Federated Learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420448</data>
</node>
<node id="Design Phase">
  <data key="d0">Design Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Design Phase in AI model development involves creating the architecture and foundational techniques that will guide the model's operations, including security considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Design Phase is a stage in the Coevolution project where foundational defenses are established for AI models to prepare for adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Design Phase refers to the initial stage in the AI model lifecycle where guidelines for enhancing AI design and defense strategies are established.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4258dad8667e5dd4d7e54cbdb071a5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755421348</data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Phase">
  <data key="d0">Operational Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Operational Phase in the context of AI models refers to the stage where models are actively used to solve problems in real-world applications following deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Operational Phase refers to the stage in the AI model lifecycle after training, where the model is deployed into actual systems for inference and regression.&lt;SEP&gt;The Operational Phase represents the stage following model training where an AI model is deployed into real systems for active use and further monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3efd11c9b0ab72e885216df0907238fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a53e39ebeb53771231e5e60fb82f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423383</data>
</node>
<node id="Runtime Detection Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Runtime Detection Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Runtime Detection Mechanism refers to systems or techniques that monitor ongoing interactions and inputs to an AI model to detect any signs of adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420448</data>
</node>
<node id="Input Validation Procedures">
  <data key="d0">Input Validation Procedures</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Input Validation Procedures are methods employed to ensure data integrity and prevent malicious or suspicious inputs in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Input Validation Procedures are processes used to ensure that incoming data is correct, secure, and suitable for the AI model, preventing various attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Input Validation Procedures are security measures implemented to check the integrity and authenticity of input data to AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2feb4344e03dd54c5451fb9791afdbfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5210e5acaba1db19cd65c4e39977b68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a53e39ebeb53771231e5e60fb82f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424152</data>
</node>
<node id="AVISENSE">
  <data key="d0">AVISENSE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">AVISENSE is a simulation platform used for creating virtual environments to test and validate Autonomous Vehicle (AV) software.&lt;SEP&gt;AVISENSE is a specialized company that develops simulation platforms for testing Autonomous Driving (AD) software. Its primary focus is on creating adaptable and scalable architectures suitable for various scenarios, particularly in constrained environments. The AVISENSE simulation platform is utilized by Coevolution to construct virtual environments specifically designed for evaluating Autonomous Vehicle (AV) software.

In addition to general simulation capabilities, AVISENSE emphasizes the incorporation of Vehicle-to-Everything (V2X) communication in its solutions. The company also offers a Connected and Automated Vehicle (CAV) simulation platform and possesses substantial expertise in model-based network design methodologies, placing particular importance on resilience against adversarial attacks. Overall, AVISENSE aims to provide robust and versatile tools to enhance the testing and optimization of Autonomous Driving technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f40649ce109d07f952bef06c2fd267e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20c0cc0a37ebaa1bdc18241b7b7a42f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b22cc6f8a153f6e262c2284ced50068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b5e09ae3d0f914dccc0db6a5f91e22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425717</data>
</node>
<node id="Peer-to-Peer Learning (P2PL)">
  <data key="d0">Peer-to-Peer Learning (P2PL)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Peer-to-Peer Learning (P2PL) encompasses a decentralized approach for enabling end-to-end communication and collaborations among peers in a network.&lt;SEP&gt;Peer-to-Peer Learning (P2PL) is a decentralized learning framework utilized in the Coevolution project, aimed at enhancing communication and collaboration among peers within artificial intelligence (AI) networks. This approach allows interconnected AI agents to engage in collaborative learning, facilitating knowledge sharing and end-to-end communication. By enabling these agents to communicate and adapt independently, P2PL promotes a system where learning occurs without centralized control, effectively leveraging the collaborative capabilities of decentralized AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f40649ce109d07f952bef06c2fd267e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce588e6a41e4a19bd041531ec028f838&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-237babba3957b0c4786b5021cd8884d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ca67a0bb25d96a23d5612a2c95b2d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425718</data>
</node>
<node id="P2P Engine">
  <data key="d0">P2P Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The P2P Engine, developed by TID, is utilized in Coevolution to simulate decentralized peer-to-peer networking, enabling realistic testing of artificial intelligence interactions. It is designed to facilitate simulations of peer-to-peer learning networks, which enhance communication between network peers. By employing this engine, Coevolution can create a realistic environment for peer-to-peer interactions, thereby advancing the study and application of collaborative learning among artificial intelligence agents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-641f4278299d91bb3b1622868a1f623d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cea46f2ec6b238b94a61ace6d4787996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6353e9bcf3d45e130811688e5860477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424927</data>
</node>
<node id="Collaborative Perception Solutions">
  <data key="d0">Collaborative Perception Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Collaborative Perception Solutions involve shared sensory information among AI agents to improve environmental awareness and decision-making within the AI supply chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Collaborative Perception Solutions refers to a set of technologies deployed to enhance the perception capabilities of autonomous vehicles through collaborative learning approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-237babba3957b0c4786b5021cd8884d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755421351</data>
</node>
<node id="Gadget">
  <data key="d0">Gadget</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Gadget in the context of Coevolution refers to an add-on designed to enhance an AI model's defense capabilities, particularly in detecting attacks and misclassifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420449</data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Phase">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Deployment Phase is a crucial stage in the AI lifecycle, where models, after being trained, are integrated into operational systems to provide services. This phase involves the incorporation of secure gadgets and systems with the final AI model to enhance its robustness against potential adversarial attacks. During the Deployment Phase, security measures are implemented to monitor the AI models for threats, ensuring their reliability and safety during operational use. It serves as an essential part of the CoEvolution Security Enhancement Flow, emphasizing the importance of security in AI deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4258dad8667e5dd4d7e54cbdb071a5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53d45e1780332e8c3904aba8e79abbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efd11c9b0ab72e885216df0907238fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425709</data>
</node>
<node id="Operation Phase">
  <data key="d0">Operation Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Operation Phase of the AI lifecycle includes ongoing updates and decommissioning processes to ensure security and compliance over time.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4486370e0771aa76fa9c8a98d04ffc56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420449</data>
</node>
<node id="Context-Aware Decision Support (CDS)">
  <data key="d0">Context-Aware Decision Support (CDS)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CDS is a crucial component of CoEvolution that operationalizes information extracted from the environment to enhance decision-making and mitigate emerging security threats.&lt;SEP&gt;The CDS is a decision-making component in the CoEvolution framework that leverages environmental information to optimize actions and mitigate risks in AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5c42e7d5f67c2de98328269247dec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a491dd9e4e112c6a3057fa684923aa8b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424154</data>
</node>
<node id="P2P and FL">
  <data key="d0">P2P and FL</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">P2P (Peer-to-Peer) and FL (Federated Learning) represent frameworks within which decentralized AI systems operate, focusing on collaborative data usage and model training.&lt;SEP&gt;P2P (peer-to-peer) and FL (federated learning) are methodologies that CoEvolution utilizes to enhance context awareness and collaborative AI resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5c42e7d5f67c2de98328269247dec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6353e9bcf3d45e130811688e5860477</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423384</data>
</node>
<node id="Acuity">
  <data key="d0">Acuity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Acuity in CoEvolution refers to the level of sensory information derived implicitly through policy learning for optimal decision support.&lt;SEP&gt;Acuity in this context refers to the sharpness or precision of sensory information as processed within context vectors in the CoEvolution framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f5c42e7d5f67c2de98328269247dec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a491dd9e4e112c6a3057fa684923aa8b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424154</data>
</node>
<node id="P2P">
  <data key="d0">P2P</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">P2P, or peer-to-peer, describes a decentralized network where peers interact directly to share resources or data, often used in collaborative learning paradigms.&lt;SEP&gt;P2P, or peer-to-peer, refers to a distributed network architecture that enables direct connections and communication among devices without a central server, crucial for collaborative AI experiences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f24ba2d35feb8defe20b38929b8da11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5c42e7d5f67c2de98328269247dec4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755421326</data>
</node>
<node id="FL">
  <data key="d0">FL</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">FL represents Federated Learning, a machine learning approach that enables models to learn from decentralized data without sharing it directly, highlighted in the context of CoEvolution.&lt;SEP&gt;FL, or federated learning, is a machine learning approach that trains algorithms across multiple decentralized devices holding local data samples, preserving user privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;FL, or federated learning, is a machine learning technique that allows models to be trained across multiple decentralized devices or servers holding local data samples, ensuring data privacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f24ba2d35feb8defe20b38929b8da11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5c42e7d5f67c2de98328269247dec4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a491dd9e4e112c6a3057fa684923aa8b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424155</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution AI Security Runtime Monitoring Engine">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution AI Security Runtime Monitoring Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution AI Security Runtime Monitoring Engine (SRME) is responsible for monitoring AI model security and managing AI MBOMs for trust and compliance within the CoEvolution ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b217cefad4abec670ed7ca0d4128679d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420449</data>
</node>
<node id="CoEvolution Dashboard">
  <data key="d0">CoEvolution Dashboard</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CoEvolution Dashboard is a comprehensive platform designed for reporting adversarial attack incidents and monitoring the performance of AI models. It serves as a user interface that allows users to report and analyze incidents related to adversarial attacks on AI models within the CoEvolution framework. As a reporting tool, the CoEvolution Dashboard presents evidence of these adversarial attacks to human users, ensuring that they have access to critical information. Additionally, the dashboard provides visual insights on security incidents that affect AI models throughout the entire CoEvolution lifecycle, enhancing the ability to understand and respond to potential threats effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;The CoEvolution Dashboard is a user interface that reports incidents affecting AI models and potential adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f295eb2f2354216e1d16d8a2d43424b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b217cefad4abec670ed7ca0d4128679d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-169bce82366b2fa52a6ddd1e7e226f5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8908f5d82a665a2008f9859e10755f6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36176d0f31881be69e8416ed157129c1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425719</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Assurance Flow">
  <data key="d0">Security Assurance Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Assurance Flow refers to a comprehensive framework and process designed to ensure the compliance, security, and trustworthiness of AI models, particularly focusing on AI MBOMs (Model-Based Object Models). It is a critical component of the CoEvolution project, wherein it outlines the necessary steps for assessing, enhancing, and assuring the security of these models throughout their entire lifecycle. This framework includes key elements such as providing security assessment metrics and documentation aimed at evaluating AI model resilience against adversarial attacks. Ultimately, the Security Assurance Flow integrates various aspects of security management to uphold the integrity and reliability of AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b217cefad4abec670ed7ca0d4128679d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef3f714a2a32270c0d8af28dae9557e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7db5c56a64621f032196bb4e5b41ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425694</data>
</node>
<node id="Collaborative Learning Paradigm">
  <data key="d0">Collaborative Learning Paradigm</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Collaborative Learning Paradigm is an advanced artificial intelligence framework that emphasizes the collective learning of multiple AI models or agents. This paradigm involves techniques for training AI models through shared learning among distributed agents or devices. It is characterized by interconnected AI agents that collaborate to enhance their learning capabilities and model robustness under various conditions. Participants in this framework contribute to the training of a shared model while maintaining the privacy of their local data, thus ensuring data security and confidentiality.

Moreover, the Collaborative Learning Paradigm operates within a shared supply chain context, which necessitates the implementation of targeted defenses against potential cybersecurity threats that may affect communication flows among the agents. Ultimately, this collaborative approach allows multiple agents or clients to work together effectively to improve AI learned behaviors while also implementing necessary cybersecurity measures for secure communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79ea744ae4e3f1f659f9ca366d26d3a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641f4278299d91bb3b1622868a1f623d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b217cefad4abec670ed7ca0d4128679d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ba33a72c094c154f14017eb9f433f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dd242577c3ba63c0f548e5aa31a5820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c72c011b17c39e8efb359d372a0af32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6353e9bcf3d45e130811688e5860477</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425717</data>
</node>
