<node id="Edge Computing Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Edge Computing Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Edge Computing Infrastructure encompasses the physical and logistical systems that support artificial intelligence (AI) applications at the edge, significantly enhancing efficiency in process management. This technological environment enables the execution of applications and the management of resources in close proximity to data sources, which is essential for optimizing processes in industrial automation. Additionally, Edge Computing Infrastructure refers to networks that facilitate the execution of applications near data sources, thereby improving processing speed and reliability. It consists of applications that can be executed in a manufacturing environment, allowing for more effective data management closer to where the data is generated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fbd5dafa81256fe9f82cfcb884bca559&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4e03def65d484eab2ad54aa7cdf54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4991d2b2e76403b019f2f16989b2a93f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbbc377e2e04f5a8e60be464dfc0a17e</data>
