<node id="CAV Simulation Platform">
  <data key="d0">CAV Simulation Platform</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The CAV Simulation Platform is a comprehensive environment developed by AviSense for simulating, validating, and testing software related to autonomous vehicles. Specifically tailored for the development and assessment of Autonomous Driving software, the platform emphasizes simulation within constrained scenarios and supports the integration of multiple agents and scenarios. This robust platform aims to facilitate the various stages of software development, ensuring that the solutions are effective and reliable in real-world applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The CAV Simulation Platform is a tool specifically designed for developing, validating, and testing autonomous driving software in CAVs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-20c0cc0a37ebaa1bdc18241b7b7a42f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1085773cd43df1afe7247dd49f7475fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afe62a9898a9c027310dea499cc4c9f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbd860797355477b1a599735726a034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc1b93aa71559fbb79284d33ce689351</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425724</data>
</node>
<node id="KPI-UC2.5">
  <data key="d0">KPI-UC2.5</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">KPI-UC2.5 refers to a key performance indicator that evaluates the overall energy footprint caused by cyber-attacks. This encompasses the energy expenditure associated with both computational resources and the motion of vehicles. Specifically, KPI-UC2.5 measures not only the energy allocated during the cyber-attack itself but also includes the resources dedicated to mitigating such attacks. It serves as an essential metric for assessing the environmental impact of cybersecurity incidents within this context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83520039a2f79f9b345e28a4597ef09b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beda666afc02f488950a3cdbad5279e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887086309908477c67923883cfe88f91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd918c8cc0ef3c8f701d30a2593d7cb3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425733</data>
</node>
<node id="KPI-UC2.6">
  <data key="d0">KPI-UC2.6</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">KPI-UC2.6 is a key performance indicator that evaluates the deterministic capability of the mitigation strategy for vehicle planning in the aftermath of a cyber-attack, specifically concerning Connected and Autonomous Vehicles (CAV). This KPI focuses on assessing how effectively the mitigation strategy can ensure reliable and predictable planning for CAVs following such an attack. Overall, KPI-UC2.6 is crucial for understanding the robustness of automotive strategies in maintaining operational integrity after cybersecurity threats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83520039a2f79f9b345e28a4597ef09b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beda666afc02f488950a3cdbad5279e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-887086309908477c67923883cfe88f91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd918c8cc0ef3c8f701d30a2593d7cb3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425728</data>
</node>
<node id="Strengthening Privacy in AI">
  <data key="d0">Strengthening Privacy in AI</data>
  <data key="d1">project</data>
  <data key="d2">This project focuses on enhancing privacy-preserving techniques for AI applications and is part of the broader objectives of CoEvolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-beda666afc02f488950a3cdbad5279e2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420453</data>
</node>
