<node id="Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms">
  <data key="d0">Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms is an international treaty designed to uphold human rights standards across Europe. It serves as a fundamental legal framework within the European Union, emphasizing the protection of human rights and fundamental freedoms. Notably, it includes critical articles, particularly articles 7 and 8, which focus on the rights related to privacy and non-discrimination. The Convention plays a crucial role in safeguarding these rights and has gained increasing relevance in contemporary discussions surrounding artificial intelligence and data protection, highlighting its importance in today's digital age. Overall, the Convention is an essential legal agreement dedicated to the protection and promotion of human rights across the European landscape.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b572f48736ae09487e4539ae10df17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d798311ba09f5fcfd50eafd690ade83a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27983f12f5c86c0463eca065b4d5542d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09c33ff0da3223617dcddd9463b4752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f0d1e34de2be2bf0ff36b6e60cd080b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1d59e9a7b134e8ee357ab390899ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c655315fcd0b9413217de724415bfd65</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424177</data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Data Clause">
  <data key="d0">Personal Data Clause</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Personal Data Clause is a crucial component of the Consortium Agreement that ensures compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) concerning the sharing and processing of personal data. This provision outlines the specifics related to the handling and management of personal data, particularly within the context of contractual agreements between partners. Furthermore, the Personal Data Clause includes measures that allow partners to reclaim rights in the event of data breaches, thereby reinforcing the commitment to safeguard personal data as mandated by GDPR principles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d81cd4432e3bdb75c5cf56e4525d3ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750697798fe8d5704aacb6736b165901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b4f9a1d0ca30881b230205e59ea3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1d59e9a7b134e8ee357ab390899ab9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425804</data>
</node>
<node id="Code of Nuremberg">
  <data key="d0">Code of Nuremberg</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Code of Nuremberg outlines fundamental ethical principles for conducting research, particularly in the realm of human experimentation. It establishes guidelines that ensure the ethical treatment of participants and the integrity of scientific inquiry. Specifically, the Code is relevant for research ethics in a variety of projects, emphasizing the necessity of ethical considerations in all aspects of scientific experimentation. Furthermore, the Code of Nuremberg's principles are incorporated into the research ethics framework of the CoEvolution project, highlighting its importance in guiding ethical practices within contemporary research endeavors.&lt;SEP&gt;The Code of Nuremberg outlines principles for ethical scientific experimentation, emphasizing integrity and responsible research practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b572f48736ae09487e4539ae10df17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d32cbd08ce6f50d78ff9bcc410caf04d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85b4f9a1d0ca30881b230205e59ea3ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-750697798fe8d5704aacb6736b165901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1d59e9a7b134e8ee357ab390899ab9</data>
