  <data key="d5">1755425809</data>
</node>
<node id="David Silver">
  <data key="d0">David Silver</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">David Silver is a prominent researcher and core contributor to the field of reinforcement learning and game strategies utilizing neural networks. He is particularly recognized for his significant contributions to mastering the game of Go through the application of deep neural networks, culminating in a landmark publication in Nature in 2016. His expertise notably extends to deep reinforcement learning, with a focus primarily on games like Go, where he has made substantial advancements that have influenced ongoing research and developments in the area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97a3313621eefb917746103c785eb45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982f3025d9a427791d44ea6a2957bf9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c3df02680dda5cc2badd5ac6d69054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3cd138afdd4c8ce77f816e48769d91</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425809</data>
</node>
<node id="Aja Huang">
  <data key="d0">Aja Huang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Aja Huang is a prominent researcher and collaborator in the field of mastering games through deep learning and search techniques. He has been significantly involved in a team effort that applied deep neural networks combined with tree search methodologies to the ancient game of Go, a development that was announced in the journal Nature. Additionally, Aja Huang is recognized as an author contributing to research focused on the application of deep neural networks in gaming contexts. His work has notably involved collaboration with David Silver, where they focused on developing deep reinforcement learning strategies for various games.&lt;SEP&gt;Aja Huang is involved in research focusing on deep learning applied to games.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97a3313621eefb917746103c785eb45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c3df02680dda5cc2badd5ac6d69054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982f3025d9a427791d44ea6a2957bf9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3cd138afdd4c8ce77f816e48769d91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7108c4595e4bb4501f0013cf316c6d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425807</data>
</node>
<node id="Chris J Maddison">
  <data key="d0">Chris J Maddison</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Chris J Maddison is a prominent figure in the fields of deep reinforcement learning and game theory. He has made significant contributions to the development of deep reinforcement learning methods, particularly in applications related to gaming and artificial intelligence. As an author, Maddison is recognized for his scholarly work that integrates these complex domains. His research includes the use of deep learning techniques to enhance game strategies, specifically in games such as Go, demonstrating his expertise and influence in the intersection of AI and strategic gameplay.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bc7108c4595e4bb4501f0013cf316c6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982f3025d9a427791d44ea6a2957bf9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c3df02680dda5cc2badd5ac6d69054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97a3313621eefb917746103c785eb45c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425809</data>
</node>
<node id="Arthur Guez">
  <data key="d0">Arthur Guez</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Arthur Guez is a researcher and author who specializes in the application of deep neural networks, particularly in the context of strategy games such as Go. He contributed to significant research published in the journal Nature in 2016, highlighting his involvement in the development of game-playing AI that leverages neural networks and advanced searching techniques. Guez is part of a dedicated team focused on enhancing the performance of artificial intelligence within games, demonstrating a strong commitment to advancing the field of deep learning research in gaming.&lt;SEP&gt;Arthur Guez is engaged in research on machine learning strategies for game development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97a3313621eefb917746103c785eb45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c3df02680dda5cc2badd5ac6d69054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982f3025d9a427791d44ea6a2957bf9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3cd138afdd4c8ce77f816e48769d91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7108c4595e4bb4501f0013cf316c6d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425807</data>
</node>
<node id="Laurent Sifre">
  <data key="d0">Laurent Sifre</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Laurent Sifre is a contributor studying the application of deep neural networks in gaming.&lt;SEP&gt;Laurent Sifre is a prominent researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of artificial intelligence, particularly in relation to neural networks and gaming strategies. He has co-authored research that focuses on the application of deep learning to understand and master complex games, including the strategic board game Go. Sifre was part of the team that developed a deep learning strategy for mastering Go, a notable achievement that was published in the prestigious journal Nature. His work encompasses various aspects of neural network methodologies, demonstrating their applicability to game strategies and contributing to the broader understanding of deep neural networks within the context of gaming.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97a3313621eefb917746103c785eb45c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c3df02680dda5cc2badd5ac6d69054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-982f3025d9a427791d44ea6a2957bf9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3cd138afdd4c8ce77f816e48769d91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7108c4595e4bb4501f0013cf316c6d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425807</data>
</node>
<node id="George Van Den Driessche">
  <data key="d0">George Van Den Driessche</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
