  <data key="d2">The Funding &amp; Tenders Portal is a platform developed by the European Commission for managing transactions related to funding and tenders.&lt;SEP&gt;The Funding &amp; Tenders Portal is an online platform managed by the European Commission for managing grants and funding applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Funding &amp; Tenders Portal is an online platform provided by the European Commission, designed to facilitate access to funding opportunities and tenders. It serves as a resource for grant management, offering tools for continuous reporting and supporting the submission and management of funding applications and tenders. Additionally, the portal is a point of contact for specific accounting tools and details regarding claims for reimbursements, ensuring comprehensive support for users navigating the funding landscape.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3c2dea0bb4e4a68977fe9ae011d6c5b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f216fc14ce08511b03292fca3d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b33dd17c4669f5a8bcc3fc405a6a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-315481829958213fce3674f0a85f2bf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2800fd1db09254940cc4a13a8d3cb57c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50145640220186d61e1c1fddbec1a547</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425825</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 6">
  <data key="d0">Article 6</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 6 outlines eligibility conditions related to EU funding for organizations participating in the consortium.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 6 outlines the eligibility and ineligibility of costs and contributions associated with the CoEvolution project. It details the legitimacy of costs and contributions that beneficiaries must substantiate in their reports, providing guidance on which financial claims can be made within the EU context. The article specifies eligible costs and contributions related to various budget categories, along with specific conditions related to the costs incurred by beneficiaries. Additionally, Article 6 refers to a specific part of the grant agreement that clarifies ineligible costs or contributions, ensuring that beneficiaries are aware of what can and cannot be claimed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4d11e0e789971dbd47542c636e3dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3431bd3a1c9c4041b4bc155e957326da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f216fc14ce08511b03292fca3d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb4f50a59cc14eb247934005c503a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7a7f20ec997cb53fbd114a846573bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66775d2ca4e61f236e59e3423f42a76e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423140</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 21">
  <data key="d0">Article 21</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 21 describes the conversion rules for expressing amounts in EUR according to the EU's regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 21 encompasses several important aspects related to financial reporting and compliance within the scope of the EU regulations. It addresses currency conversion for financial statements, ensuring adherence to standard accounting practices, particularly the conversion of amounts expressed in EUR. Additionally, Article 21 outlines specific reporting requirements that beneficiaries must meet to process payments effectively. It also establishes the necessary regulations regarding reporting periods as stipulated in the relevant Agreement, and mandates both continuous and periodic reporting obligations for beneficiaries of funded projects. Overall, Article 21 serves as a comprehensive framework guiding the financial reporting and compliance processes for entities involved in EU-funded initiatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4d11e0e789971dbd47542c636e3dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f216fc14ce08511b03292fca3d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27d0350792bd2bf2a5044cc72cd8959b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb4f50a59cc14eb247934005c503a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423140</data>
</node>
<node id="Data Sheet">
  <data key="d0">Data Sheet</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Data Sheet contains time limits and other important information regarding records and supporting documents that beneficiaries must maintain.&lt;SEP&gt;The Data Sheet is a comprehensive document that serves multiple purposes in the context of EU funding and compliance. It outlines crucial points related to obligations following action funding, ensuring that beneficiaries are aware of their responsibilities. The Data Sheet includes important financial information such as reimbursement rates and other relevant financial details. Additionally, it contains specific sections that outline special rules applicable to certain beneficiaries or situations under EU agreements. 

Moreover, the Data Sheet plays a critical role in audits and checks related to grants within the EU program, ensuring transparency and accountability. It also provides key information and requirements essential for the implementation of projects, although the document does not specify these details explicitly. Furthermore, it outlines the schedule and modalities for reporting and payments associated with the CoEvolution project, contributing to the effective management and oversight of funding processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Data Sheet is a reference document outlining payment schedules, modalities, and conditions relevant to funding under the Horizon CL3 program.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-da85149284498fc139e8be382b981003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cef03a8059a065d6002cea06de607314&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e311b0bf4e60d61a3a28a1b7cce6c4af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65321e5c497565cf717aab53e5aa7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e9aa7ab49a00972f3d46c56705b630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebde38c3cbda883291428373982665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f216fc14ce08511b03292fca3d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6587c0a38b949dea5de8a236e80407fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422090</data>
</node>
<node id="Annex 2">
  <data key="d0">Annex 2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Annex 2 is a crucial document associated with the CoEvolution project, containing comprehensive information about the estimated budget, eligible costs, and a breakdown of budget categories. It holds significant importance as it takes precedence over Annex 1 according to the Agreement. This document presents detailed insights into the estimated budget for the project, including various budget categories pertinent to the action outlined in the project documentation. 

Furthermore, Annex 2 articulates the conditions under which expenses can be declared, ensuring clarity in budget management for the involved parties. It specifically details the total estimated costs of subcontracting for each beneficiary, which is essential for accounting purposes. In addition to outlining direct costs, Annex 2 also includes third-party contributions, further emphasizing its role in providing a structured overview of all financial aspects associated with the CoEvolution project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8e293777d71c3ca9709a65d86e40e18b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ba5723f8c11853502f9c64b427fd38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9941c6cbac26f2073168a5b30c17afcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3431bd3a1c9c4041b4bc155e957326da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575f216fc14ce08511b03292fca3d54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb7a7f20ec997cb53fbd114a846573bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca56f67073468dac14fea47e10463965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a5bb32d295f690e6535a7cb23fa6baa</data>
