<node id="HE MGA">
  <data key="d0">HE MGA</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">HE MGA is an organizational body that plays a crucial role in the funding and financial management of projects under the Horizon Europe initiative. It is specifically involved in overseeing the CoEvolution project, facilitating prefinancing payments and grants, and managing the associated budget and actions. Additionally, HE MGA likely works alongside the Multi &amp; Mono project guidelines and regulations concerning grant agreements. The acronym HE MGA stands for 'Horizon Europe Model Grant Agreement,' which establishes the rules and policies governing Horizon projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b12294f744da8f2db1893e5324f5ccd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395405bf739ba7ab815c034dae49720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e901df4ec4c380c4f63b0cd3f4cc859&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3431bd3a1c9c4041b4bc155e957326da</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422078</data>
</node>
<node id="Annex 1">
  <data key="d0">Annex 1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Annex 1 is a critical document related to the CoEvolution project, containing specific details and tasks assigned to associated partners involved in the project. It serves as a comprehensive reference that describes the actions associated with the project, detailing the specific requirements concerning budget categories and eligible costs. As part of the grant documentation, Annex 1 holds precedence over Annex 2 within the framework of the Agreement.

Furthermore, Annex 1 outlines the tasks that are to be subcontracted, along with the estimated costs associated with each subcontract for the action or project. This makes it an indispensable element of the overall Agreement, providing essential information regarding the project's description, requirements, and financial framework. It also includes definitions and classifications related to action tasks and contracting processes, ensuring compliance and proper implementation of the project.

In addition, Annex 1 specifies the conditions and requirements for direct costs that must be met, making it a crucial section of the EU grant documentation that articulates the description of the action to be implemented by the beneficiaries.</data>
