  <data key="d2">EU Grants refer to financial awards provided by the European Union to support specific actions and projects. These grants encompass financial contributions awarded by various EU institutions, bodies, offices, or agencies, and are subject to detailed eligibility conditions related to different budget categories. Significant projects such as CoEvolution are examples of initiatives that benefit from EU Grants, illustrating the diverse applications of this financial support.&lt;SEP&gt;EU Grants refers to funding opportunities provided by the European Union for research and innovation projects, including the CoEvolution project.</data>
