  <data key="d5">1755420995</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 19">
  <data key="d0">Article 19</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 19 mandates the sharing of information by beneficiaries as part of their obligations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-66775d2ca4e61f236e59e3423f42a76e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420995</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 20">
  <data key="d0">Article 20</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 20 pertains to record-keeping guidelines as part of the EU Financial Regulation, detailing how participants must manage documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 20 pertains to record-keeping responsibilities for beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-66775d2ca4e61f236e59e3423f42a76e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422084</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 25">
  <data key="d0">Article 25</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 25 establishes a comprehensive framework regarding financial oversight and compliance within the context of grants, particularly relating to the CoEvolution project. It defines the conditions under which the granting authority has the authority to recover funds due to substantial errors or breaches of obligations by beneficiaries or subcontractors. The article identifies relevant bodies, including the granting authority and OLAF (the European Anti-Fraud Office), that hold rights towards these parties.

Furthermore, Article 25 delineates the procedures for checks, reviews, audits, and investigations conducted by the European Union to ensure adherence to financial guidelines, thus safeguarding the integrity of fund management. It also emphasizes specific guidelines pertaining to the management and storage of records by beneficiaries, ensuring that necessary documentation is maintained appropriately.

Additionally, Article 25 refers to a section of the agreement that addresses rights relating to third parties, particularly in the context of contributions and compliance obligations. Overall, Article 25 serves as a crucial legal framework for ensuring accountability and transparency in the administration of grants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4d11e0e789971dbd47542c636e3dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b345cada8d617efdc8dbd31168fa0f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66775d2ca4e61f236e59e3423f42a76e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422087</data>
</node>
<node id="Participant">
  <data key="d0">Participant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Participants are entities involved in the CoEvolution project that must adhere to specific terms regarding implementation and compliance with the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755420995</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 22">
  <data key="d0">Article 22</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 22 provides a comprehensive overview of procedures related to the recovery or adjustments of grant amounts within the context of the CoEvolution project. It elaborates on the necessary protocols that the granting authority must follow concerning cost and contribution declarations, emphasizing the need for clarity and adherence to specified processes. Additionally, Article 22 outlines particular provisions regarding situations where recovery may not be applicable, ensuring that conditions for non-recovery are clearly stipulated. The article also addresses rules governing recoveries related to financial support offered to third parties, affirming the importance of project compliance in these financial transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422087</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 26">
  <data key="d0">Article 26</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 26 discusses impact evaluation based on participant’s internal rules in accordance with the framework agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 26 discusses the impact evaluation processes under the CoEvolution project, highlighting the need for compliance with internal rules and procedures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422085</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 31">
  <data key="d0">Article 31</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 31 indicates the regulations pertaining to grant reductions in the case of improper terminations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 relates to the terms under which grant agreement suspension is permitted, detailing the conditions for eligible costs during such suspensions.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 outlines conditions under which costs during grant agreement suspension become eligible for coverage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-27d0350792bd2bf2a5044cc72cd8959b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422085</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 32">
  <data key="d0">Article 32</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 32 outlines crucial procedures and guidelines related to the management of grants, specifically focusing on the process of calculating final grant amounts and payments after the termination of agreements. It details the conditions that may lead to the termination of a grant or the participation of the coordinator and beneficiaries, particularly emphasizing instances of non-compliance. Additionally, Article 32 provides clear instructions on how final payments and associated costs are to be assessed in the aftermath of such terminations. Overall, Article 32 serves as a comprehensive framework for understanding the implications and processes involved when grants are terminated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ee3eb87a546ba8ada176f900494902b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27d0350792bd2bf2a5044cc72cd8959b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422089</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 33.2">
  <data key="d0">Article 33.2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 33.2 clarifies the liability for damages the granting authority may claim, relating to actions not implemented in compliance with the agreement.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 33.2 mandates compensation of the granting authority for damages resulting from non-compliance with agreements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e557b68414afd58cab58755db5cf3a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422085</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 15">
  <data key="d0">Article 15</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 15 addresses data protection rules, outlining guidelines for participants to follow in relation to personal data handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 15 relates to data protection and outlines the responsibilities of the granting authority regarding personal data processing under the Agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7019b56e282d7e9dc7527aa2932219f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d57502f9241a83df154e24913d21904</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422088</data>
</node>
<node id="granting authority">
  <data key="d0">granting authority</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The granting authority is an organization responsible for managing grants for various projects, including the CoEvolution project. It plays a crucial role in the approval and distribution of funds, ensuring that financial oversight is maintained throughout the grant process. The granting authority is tasked with monitoring compliance with grant agreements and project terms, ensuring adherence to all relevant regulations.

In its capacity, the granting authority oversees the administration of grants, making critical decisions regarding eligibility and the potential suspension or termination of grants. Additionally, it communicates with involved consortia to manage and distribute payments related to projects, highlighting its importance in the overall administration of grants and the efficient execution of funded initiatives. Overall, the granting authority is pivotal in providing financial support and maintaining compliance for the projects it oversees.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4ba5723f8c11853502f9c64b427fd38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66b48a08b5a1dfe503764abaf73f0cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-513280f6927e9d616d879baf249f9364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153d0d25b1dc6cfa0bcf7a7947b40d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27d0350792bd2bf2a5044cc72cd8959b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1e6845be0998259ad41a50c2e648ae7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422085</data>
</node>
<node id="Article 28">
  <data key="d0">Article 28</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Article 28 outlines the conditions under which grants may be reduced for beneficiaries. It specifically describes the circumstances that allow the granting authority to reduce these grants, particularly in cases where the coordinator breaches their obligations. Additionally, Article 28 refers to regulations that establish the consequences of such breaches, emphasizing the penalties associated with reductions in grants. The article also highlights specific provisions concerning the circumstances leading to reductions for beneficiaries who fail to meet their obligations under the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4d11e0e789971dbd47542c636e3dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e311b0bf4e60d61a3a28a1b7cce6c4af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65321e5c497565cf717aab53e5aa7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ee3eb87a546ba8ada176f900494902b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422092</data>
</node>
<node id="Chapter 5">
  <data key="d0">Chapter 5</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Chapter 5 describes the measures and consequences that apply to beneficiaries who breach obligations under the terms of grant agreements. It details the additional measures that may be enacted in response to such breaches, focusing on grant compliance and reporting requirements within the project implementation context. This section outlines the consequences of non-compliance for beneficiaries in relation to grants and funding, emphasizing the importance of adhering to the stipulated obligations. Chapter 5 serves as a critical component of the EU grant agreements, providing clarity on the repercussions for failing to meet grant obligations as outlined in the governing documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4d11e0e789971dbd47542c636e3dd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e311b0bf4e60d61a3a28a1b7cce6c4af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65321e5c497565cf717aab53e5aa7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8719a38bb7a9f42229f7fe81c9bf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebde38c3cbda883291428373982665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7019b56e282d7e9dc7527aa2932219f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7998d7f556fa82a3f85973da5a1f2d77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422089</data>
</node>
<node id="Regulation 2018/1725">
  <data key="d0">Regulation 2018/1725</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Regulation 2018/1725 establishes the framework for protecting personal data processed by the Union institutions, bodies, offices, and agencies.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation 2018/1725 governs the processing of personal data by EU institutions, affecting how data is handled in grants.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation 2018/1725 is a legal framework governing the processing of personal data by EU institutions and bodies, focused on ensuring data protection rights.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b65321e5c497565cf717aab53e5aa7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22cbe105bf419f163813e1e4122e6db8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7019b56e282d7e9dc7527aa2932219f0</data>
