<node id="grant">
  <data key="d0">grant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A grant is a financial award provided by an organization to support specific projects or activities. It is a sum of money given by a granting authority, contingent on adherence to specific rules and conditions set forth in an agreement. Grants serve as financial contributions aimed at assisting beneficiaries in implementing designated actions. The funding may be subject to termination or suspension under various circumstances if compliance with the stipulated conditions is not maintained. Overall, grants are instrumental in facilitating the execution of initiatives while ensuring that certain guidelines are met.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-36658fffc2a66839fd311a671e81c140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66b48a08b5a1dfe503764abaf73f0cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebde38c3cbda883291428373982665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1e6845be0998259ad41a50c2e648ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31116ac4e46d186dea94d94a7702584</data>
