<node id="Final Payment">
  <data key="d0">Final Payment</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Final Payment is described as financial support given after the completion of reports, marking the end of the funding cycle for grantees.&lt;SEP&gt;Final Payment refers to the last disbursement of funds made to the beneficiary, occurring after the completion of a project action. This payment is contingent upon the beneficiary's compliance with grant terms and the fulfillment of all conditions and calculations regarding eligible costs and contributions. It may also be influenced by any suspensions or compliance issues that arise. The Final Payment effectively represents the reimbursement of the remaining portion of the eligible costs and contributions claimed by the beneficiary.&lt;SEP&gt;Final payment represents the last disbursement made to beneficiaries upon completion of their projects or reporting requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ef1f5817b40d920cdf33d4c4a68e437e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8719a38bb7a9f42229f7fe81c9bf9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ee906c164033c38c47ee9b5abf0836f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-897fe30d76da92eef8ab39f6f37362da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-340cab0aeae7a8a4e864f5fb97fb2b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-315481829958213fce3674f0a85f2bf7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422810</data>
</node>
<node id="Periodic Report">
  <data key="d0">Periodic Report</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The Periodic Report is a crucial document that serves multiple purposes in the context of project management and financial oversight. It summarizes the progress and financial situation of the project and must receive approval for costs to be recognized. This report plays a key role in ensuring compliance and authorizing interim or final payments associated with the project.

The coordinator is responsible for submitting the Periodic Report, which must include relevant certificates related to the project's financial statements and progress updates. Additionally, this report must be submitted within 60 days following the termination of the grant, summarizing both the financial status and the activities conducted. Overall, the Periodic Report is a documentation process mandated by the agreement, occurring 60 days after the conclusion of each reporting period to ensure transparency and accountability in project funding and activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68530f7500a72fc731f00e3c4c766df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d3c3eaedec46daebd343527b0c0d92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66b48a08b5a1dfe503764abaf73f0cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-897fe30d76da92eef8ab39f6f37362da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6395405bf739ba7ab815c034dae49720</data>
