</node>
<node id="beneficiary">
  <data key="d0">beneficiary</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A beneficiary is a person or entity eligible to receive funds under a grant and is obligated to adhere to the terms set forth in the grant agreement. This includes individuals or organizations that are entitled to receive funding or grants managed by the granting authority. Beneficiaries must comply with the regulations and obligations established by the granting authority to ensure the proper execution of the funded activities. In essence, beneficiaries are the entities or partners that utilize grant funding to carry out specific activities as outlined in their agreements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153d0d25b1dc6cfa0bcf7a7947b40d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27d0350792bd2bf2a5044cc72cd8959b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1e6845be0998259ad41a50c2e648ae7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
