<node id="European Court of Auditors">
  <data key="d0">European Court of Auditors</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Court of Auditors (ECA) is an institution of the European Union (EU) tasked with the critical role of auditing EU finances. It ensures that both the revenue and expenditure of the EU are properly spent and managed. The primary objectives of the ECA include promoting accountability and improving financial management within the EU by conducting thorough audits of EU funds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68530f7500a72fc731f00e3c4c766df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b040918a9ab9d53eb1630a7309bd1d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925b1f5a2133d1fdc125c610bbbae027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce05917392d14a6ff1f6d80ad2f3e51f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422094</data>
</node>
<node id="European Public Prosecutors Office">
  <data key="d0">European Public Prosecutors Office</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Public Prosecutor’s Office (EPPO) is an independent public prosecution office of the European Union, tasked with investigating and prosecuting crimes that affect the EU budget and the financial interests of the Union. As an institution of the EU, the EPPO plays a crucial role in safeguarding the financial integrity of the Union by pursuing crimes against its budget. This independent body is dedicated to ensuring accountability and combating fraud related to EU finances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68530f7500a72fc731f00e3c4c766df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b040918a9ab9d53eb1630a7309bd1d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925b1f5a2133d1fdc125c610bbbae027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce05917392d14a6ff1f6d80ad2f3e51f</data>
