<node id="European Anti-Fraud Office">
  <data key="d0">European Anti-Fraud Office</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The European Anti-Fraud Office (OLAF) is an agency dedicated to investigating fraud and corruption that affects the European Union (EU) budget. Its primary responsibility revolves around developing and implementing anti-fraud strategies to safeguard the financial interests of the EU. OLAF works to ensure that resources are used properly and that any fraudulent or corrupt activities are thoroughly investigated, reflecting its commitment to protecting the integrity of EU finances.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68530f7500a72fc731f00e3c4c766df6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b040918a9ab9d53eb1630a7309bd1d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925b1f5a2133d1fdc125c610bbbae027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce05917392d14a6ff1f6d80ad2f3e51f</data>
