</node>
<node id="Data Poisoning">
  <data key="d0">Data Poisoning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Data Poisoning is a specific type of adversarial attack that involves the injection of harmful or malicious data into training datasets, with the intention of compromising the integrity and performance of artificial intelligence (AI) models. This attack undermines the integrity of the datasets that are crucial for training AI systems, leading to potential corruption of the model's learning process. By introducing defective data during the training phase, data poisoning poses significant risks to the overall reliability and effectiveness of AI applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05ba33a72c094c154f14017eb9f433f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d913cb5322e69bb504986e2098e6b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2be5c8354db5456b4254a51a65a6f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84cf7d8377823cd2796ee572ef8df58e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424132</data>
</node>
<node id="Man-in-the-Middle Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Man-in-the-Middle Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Man-in-the-Middle Attacks are a security threat where an attacker intercepts communication between two parties, potentially altering the information exchanged.&lt;SEP&gt;Man-in-the-Middle Attacks represent a security threat where an attacker intercepts communication between two parties, relevant in the context of AI supply chains.&lt;SEP&gt;Man-in-the-middle attacks involve an unauthorized party intercepting communication between two systems to manipulate data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84cf7d8377823cd2796ee572ef8df58e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62d913cb5322e69bb504986e2098e6b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2be5c8354db5456b4254a51a65a6f69</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424130</data>
