</node>
<node id="Poisoning Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Poisoning Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Poisoning Attacks are a specific form of adversarial attack that targets machine learning algorithms. These attacks involve the deliberate injection of harmful samples into the training data, which compromises the learning process of AI models. The goal of Poisoning Attacks is to disrupt the integrity of the algorithm, potentially leading to denial of service or causing intentional misclassifications. By manipulating the training data, attackers can significantly undermine the effectiveness and reliability of the machine learning systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b95c94affa550c2a005eb66b83e0f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a552b8b0b6e1c9d217e2714e332435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6eb6aae1af8d6225c491ae5dedc4268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d188b520ae593ffa16184991a28ba19</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425699</data>
</node>
<node id="Evasion Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Evasion Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Evasion Attacks refer to adversarial techniques employed to manipulate input data in order to cause misclassification during the operation of trained machine learning models. These tactics, often known as adversarial examples, specifically target the operational phases of AI systems, aiming to deceive them and lead to incorrect interpretations of the data. By tampering with input data at test time, Evasion Attacks can result in unintended outcomes, thereby highlighting vulnerabilities in AI models during the testing phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Evasion attacks are adversarial examples that disrupt the operation of trained models by perturbing input data to achieve misclassification during testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Evasion Attacks, also known as adversarial examples, target trained models during operation, involving changes to input data that lead to misclassification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4b95c94affa550c2a005eb66b83e0f70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86a552b8b0b6e1c9d217e2714e332435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28af3e5b46628e98e598a3a3fb2df917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6eb6aae1af8d6225c491ae5dedc4268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d188b520ae593ffa16184991a28ba19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efd11c9b0ab72e885216df0907238fd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425697</data>
</node>
<node id="Cybersecurity-Related Domains">
  <data key="d0">Cybersecurity-Related Domains</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Cybersecurity-Related Domains are fields that focus on protecting computer systems from theft, damage, and unauthorized access, often utilizing AI and machine learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d188b520ae593ffa16184991a28ba19</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
