  <data key="d5">1755421336</data>
</node>
<node id="Homomorphic Encryption (HE)">
  <data key="d0">Homomorphic Encryption (HE)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Homomorphic Encryption (HE) is a sophisticated cryptographic method that allows computations to be performed directly on encrypted data without the necessity of decryption. This unique capability ensures the confidentiality of the data throughout the computational process. When operations are executed on ciphertexts, HE produces an encrypted result that, upon decryption, corresponds to the output that would have been obtained if the calculations had been conducted on the plaintext. As a privacy-preserving technology, HE plays a crucial role in secure computations, significantly preventing the leakage of sensitive information during various interactions, particularly within AI models and projects such as CoEvolution. Overall, Homomorphic Encryption is an essential tool for maintaining data confidentiality while enabling meaningful computations on that data, serving as a vital defense technology against privacy breaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f13e4e9d2acd6290e2eddd212bdd3df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79ea744ae4e3f1f659f9ca366d26d3a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b9d5508965f4ddd6b9dc8dab9cebb0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05ba33a72c094c154f14017eb9f433f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5092e32b5e7f6b1dc6a316b8941ea4c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f8a78502e4359c56e2de032610b38aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71006e55cf73aa373312d69b3b443261</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425716</data>
</node>
