<node id="Utility-based Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Utility-based Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Utility-based Attacks are a specific category of adversarial attacks that concentrate on undermining the utility and performance of AI models. These attacks aim to compromise the operational capabilities of these models by manipulating their inputs, thereby degrading their functional efficiency. The significance of addressing Utility-based Attacks is also recognized in the CoEvolution project, which seeks to enhance the resilience of AI systems against such vulnerabilities. Overall, Utility-based Attacks pose a critical threat to the effectiveness of AI systems by targeting their capacity to deliver reliable outputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28af3e5b46628e98e598a3a3fb2df917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623872b535f731e898e49b91d42e77f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a53e39ebeb53771231e5e60fb82f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ad886edb819a72a00a95a3d6cb0423</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755424923</data>
</node>
<node id="Privacy-based Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Privacy-based Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Privacy-based Attacks are adversarial attacks designed to compromise the privacy and confidentiality of sensitive information utilized in the training and operation of AI systems. These attacks specifically target the sensitive data within AI models, aiming to undermine the confidentiality of the information being processed. CoEvolution recognizes the significance of these threats and actively seeks to defend against Privacy-based Attacks to protect the integrity of AI systems and the sensitive data they handle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28af3e5b46628e98e598a3a3fb2df917&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-623872b535f731e898e49b91d42e77f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21a53e39ebeb53771231e5e60fb82f69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80ad886edb819a72a00a95a3d6cb0423</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
