<node id="Peter Vamplew">
  <data key="d0">Peter Vamplew</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Peter Vamplew is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of decision-making in artificial intelligence. He is particularly noted for his involvement in a survey of multi-objective sequential decision-making published in 2013, in which he is acknowledged as one of the authors. Additionally, Vamplew has engaged in discussions surrounding multi-objective reinforcement learning techniques, further highlighting his expertise and focus within this area of study.&lt;SEP&gt;Peter Vamplew is a researcher working with Diederik M. Roijers on multi-objective decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Peter Vamplew is engaged in research regarding decision-making methodologies in AI.</data>
