  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Muhammad Usman is a researcher known for his significant contributions to the field of artificial intelligence, particularly in the area of neural networks. He authored a study titled "AntidoteRT," which focuses on the run-time detection and correction of poison attacks that can compromise the integrity of neural networks. His work includes co-authoring a paper published in 2022 that discusses the mechanisms for detecting and correcting such attacks, highlighting his dedication to enhancing the security and reliability of neural network systems. Through these efforts, Muhammad Usman has established himself as a key figure in addressing the challenges posed by poison attacks in artificial intelligence.</data>
