<node id="adversarial attack">
  <data key="d0">adversarial attack</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial attack refers to methods that attempt to deceive AI models by introducing malicious inputs during training or deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial attacks are attempts to fool AI models through input manipulation, posing a significant security threat.&lt;SEP&gt;An adversarial attack refers to incidents targeting AI models that can compromise their security and functionality, reported and monitored by the SRME.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c59208a0ecce67d91fc2e55e630e3efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a491dd9e4e112c6a3057fa684923aa8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8de9ab24149e20dd885bdf7aa0cbc37</data>
