<node id="Reinforcement Learning">
  <data key="d0">Reinforcement Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Reinforcement Learning is a machine learning paradigm that emphasizes how agents should take actions within an environment to maximize cumulative rewards. As a subset of machine learning, it focuses on training decision-making agents that learn to make optimal choices based on the outcomes of their actions within that environment. This approach has proven successful in addressing complex problems across various fields by effectively maximizing cumulative rewards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2b22cc6f8a153f6e262c2284ced50068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-125a6d8c6730e236d423f077d38dc767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20c0cc0a37ebaa1bdc18241b7b7a42f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81418f280483fb994ba74151f8e56fb2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425701</data>
</node>
<node id="AI Security and Trust Assurance">
  <data key="d0">AI Security and Trust Assurance</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">AI Security and Trust Assurance encompasses the measures and mechanisms aimed at ensuring that AI models are secure and trusted.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Security and Trust Assurance is a focus area of CoEvolution, aiming to enhance the trustworthiness of AI models through robustification processes.&lt;SEP&gt;AI Security and Trust Assurance refers to the mechanisms and operations implemented to ensure AI models are secure and trustworthy throughout their lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9db1412409c67345807388c3e65bc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f98f10ca7967e7c93ebec461a36b56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31852725a164a4dd52957ae5c1baa452</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425701</data>
</node>
<node id="ML Model Replacement">
  <data key="d0">ML Model Replacement</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">ML Model Replacement is a threat model wherein a malicious actor aims to substitute a legitimate machine learning model with a compromised one.&lt;SEP&gt;ML model replacement is a specified threat model in CoEvolution that involves replacing an existing machine learning model with a malicious version to degrade system security.&lt;SEP&gt;ML model replacement refers to a specific threat model focused on substituting an original machine learning model with a malicious one.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425703</data>
</node>
<node id="Poisoning of Training Data">
  <data key="d0">Poisoning of Training Data</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Poisoning of Training Data is a threat model that involves introducing misleading or harmful data into the training set to degrade the integrity of the AI model.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisoning of training data refers to the threat where malicious data is introduced into the training dataset to compromise the integrity of the AI model.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisoning of training data is a threat model that involves corrupting the data used to train AI models, thus compromising their performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425703</data>
</node>
<node id="Adversarial Examples">
  <data key="d0">Adversarial Examples</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Adversarial Examples refer to inputs that have been intentionally designed to deceive an AI model, causing it to err.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial examples are inputs specifically designed to deceive AI models into making incorrect predictions or classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial examples are specifically crafted inputs designed to deceive AI models into making incorrect predictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425703</data>
</node>
<node id="Membership Inference">
  <data key="d0">Membership Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Membership Inference pertains to a threat model where an actor attempts to determine whether a specific data point was part of the training dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;Membership inference is a type of attack where an adversary tries to determine whether a particular data point was part of the training dataset for the AI model.&lt;SEP&gt;Membership inference is a threat model that allows an attacker to determine if a specific data point was included in the training dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425703</data>
</node>
<node id="Model Inversion">
  <data key="d0">Model Inversion</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Model Inversion is a threat model in which an attacker infers sensitive information about the training data from the model outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Model inversion is a threat model that allows an attacker to retrieve sensitive information from the AI model, undermining user privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Model inversion is a technique used by attackers to reverse-engineer information about the dataset used to train a machine learning model.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c8def759f18995b41ea21003cc5dcc30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7cc5c6e530f1da15321ba18788990ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c57d3ea1e6c2e634c6f78e88a9a227d9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425704</data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Base Data Pools">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Base Data Pools</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge Base Data Pools consist of three data segments within CoEvolution that include trusted AI models, open access trusted data, and management of AI MBOMs.&lt;SEP&gt;Knowledge Base Data Pools refer to the structured data repositories within the CoEvolution Hub that store information on trusted AI models, data, and management of AI MBOMs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9510fe2b92ae882d551007b5ee87df2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c45633c6b079b86215891c3f1d283a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425706</data>
</node>
<node id="Security Enhancement Engine">
  <data key="d0">Security Enhancement Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Security Enhancement Engine is a fundamental component of CoEvolution, designed to assess and implement security measures for AI models throughout their lifecycle. It serves as a tool that not only evaluates the security measures of AI models but also enhances them, with a particular focus on preventing adversarial attacks. Furthermore, the Security Enhancement Engine is utilized to modify the structure of AI models, integrating countermeasures aimed at protecting against such adversarial threats. Overall, it offers a range of tools and techniques that help in mitigating risks associated with AI model designs, ensuring a more secure deployment of artificial intelligence systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9510fe2b92ae882d551007b5ee87df2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d53d45e1780332e8c3904aba8e79abbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755425709</data>
</node>
<node id="Deployment Phase Tools">
  <data key="d0">Deployment Phase Tools</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment Phase Tools are utilized during the deployment of AI models to ensure security against inference adversarial attacks and other vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422755</data>
</node>
<node id="Training Phase Tools and Services">
  <data key="d0">Training Phase Tools and Services</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Training Phase Tools and Services are resources provided by CoEvolution to ensure the safe and effective training of AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Training Phase Tools and Services are tools used during the training of AI models to ensure security and reduce bias in the training data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aa83eb77b884af99d8cd56eafdf08c61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755423376</data>
</node>
<node id="Secure Training Process">
  <data key="d0">Secure Training Process</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Secure Training Process encompasses methodologies employed during the training phase of AI models to ensure resilience against adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f5d57fd30405ff0a9f46bc2a7e01ff0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1755422755</data>
