<node id="Trusted Execution Environments (TEE)">
  <data key="d0">Trusted Execution Environments (TEE)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Trusted Execution Environments (TEE) are secure areas within main processors designed to offer an isolated environment for the execution of artificial intelligence (AI) models while safeguarding sensitive data. These environments play a crucial role in maintaining data confidentiality and integrity during execution, making them particularly valuable for deploying AI models. Specific implementations of Trusted Execution Environments, such as ARM Trust Zone and Intel Software Guard Extensions (SGX), are equipped to create secure enclaves that protect against privacy-related attacks. Overall, TEEs ensure a secure framework for AI model deployment, effectively mitigating risks associated with data security and unauthorized access.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-641f4278299d91bb3b1622868a1f623d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c72c011b17c39e8efb359d372a0af32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dd242577c3ba63c0f548e5aa31a5820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93da09e739b2b1da529a083098c37db</data>
