<node id="AI Ecosystem">
  <data key="d0">AI Ecosystem</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The AI Ecosystem refers to the interconnected network of stakeholders, technologies, and practices involved in the development, deployment, and utilization of artificial intelligence solutions. It encompasses a diverse range of AI models designed for various applications, highlighting the complexity and variety inherent in AI development. This ecosystem includes various systems and components essential for AI technologies' progression and implementation, specifically noting the significance of collaboration among different stakeholders. Additionally, the AI Ecosystem is characterized by its interconnected systems and processes, which, while facilitating innovation, also present vulnerabilities to various types of attacks. Within the context of the European Union, this ecosystem encapsulates the collective set of components and stakeholders that work together to drive the advancement of AI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32e396002be0503d0e0baac803477dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4cfff2edf2dca18d266e6392c6acf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd49d5a257b3871e2279f29bb34ee6c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a6e752def2c1fc953cab11b48652f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-589ff2c6b80ad5646240c13df874e58a</data>
