<node id="GDPR Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">GDPR Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">GDPR Guidelines refer to regulations aimed at protecting personal data and privacy in the EU, ensuring AI systems comply with legal standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The GDPR Guidelines are European regulations established by the European Union aimed at safeguarding data privacy and security for individuals. These guidelines have a significant impact on how artificial intelligence (AI) systems manage and process user data. Specifically, the GDPR Guidelines govern the handling of personal data and privacy within the context of AI applications, influencing best practices and legal standards in data protection. The focus on individual privacy in data handling is not only a core aspect of the GDPR but also a critical element of initiatives such as the CoEvolution project, which seeks to align AI technology with these regulatory frameworks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54b95887f0a735a53175d3a901822dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f58584ea79a787e820a9f9468f6603f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9260f7f87786fb6b762b6bf5a25591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ae0f0567a0d81633f1194f5d9d67365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a9e31e2b7ee95a5a60fd9f2a49c2647</data>
