<node id="Charles Lefurgy">
  <data key="d0">Charles Lefurgy</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Charles Lefurgy is a researcher and author who has extensively contributed to the field of power management in computing environments. He has collaborated on various works focused on managing power consumption and performance, particularly utilizing reinforcement learning methodologies. Notably, Lefurgy co-authored a significant paper in 2007 that explores these concepts, further establishing his role in advancing techniques aimed at optimizing power and performance in computing systems. His work highlights his expertise in integrating reinforcement learning approaches to address power management challenges effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Charles Lefurgy is involved in research on the interplay between performance and energy efficiency in computing systems.</data>
