<node id="Secure Multiparty Computation (SMPC)">
  <data key="d0">Secure Multiparty Computation (SMPC)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Secure Multiparty Computation (SMPC) is a scheme used to protect data privacy in computational processes within AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Secure Multiparty Computation (SMPC) schemes are utilized in AI to secure data exchanges and prevent adversarial attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Secure Multiparty Computation is a cryptographic method that allows parties to jointly compute a function over their inputs while keeping those inputs private, applied in the CoEvolution project for secure model aggregation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1f13e4e9d2acd6290e2eddd212bdd3df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f8a78502e4359c56e2de032610b38aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b9d5508965f4ddd6b9dc8dab9cebb0f</data>
