  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Model Inversion Attacks are a type of security threat where an attacker reconstructs the input data utilized to train an AI model, posing privacy risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Model Inversion Attacks exploit knowledge of an AI model to reconstruct inputs or reveal private data, highlighting another form of adversarial threat against AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Model Inversion Attacks are specific threats where attackers could infer information about the training data from the model outputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6f799d77b58dcf9852f1c75b35188b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf0ef74c7d451fed43129ef79275910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f984a4687c34b201081d48b577fd5ba</data>
