  <data key="d6">29.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The CoEvolution Project is supported by IMT, which plays a significant role in its overall development and evaluation. IMT is actively involved in various research and development activities related to the CoEvolution Project. Their contributions include defining the project's architecture, highlighting their integral role in shaping its structure and objectives. However, a recent request by IMT to leave the CoEvolution Project suggests a change in their status, indicating their previous involvement in the project's beneficiary composition. Despite this request, the scope of IMT's contributions to the CoEvolution Project has been notable, reflecting their commitment during their participation.</data>
