<edge source="EU General Court" target="EU Court of Justice">
  <data key="d6">36.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The EU Court of Justice and the EU General Court are integral components of the judicial system of the European Union, each serving distinct roles within the framework of EU law. The EU General Court functions as the first tier for dispute resolution, handling initial cases and legal disputes. Decisions made by the EU General Court can be appealed to the EU Court of Justice, which serves as the highest authority in this judicial hierarchy. This relationship underscores their link in the legal process, with the EU Court of Justice overseeing appeals and ensuring the uniform interpretation of EU law. Together, they play a critical role in upholding legal standards and resolving disputes within the EU.</data>
  <data key="d8">EU law,judicial appeal,judicial hierarchy,judicial hierarchy",legal system</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-95e9aa7ab49a00972f3d46c56705b630&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9914231eecde0fb46ee3d4c21bb3e505&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f94199efc5d89e82849d9cfe93dfb68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e61a5cae6fe4c2cb8e2ff9868086dc8</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755425278</data>
</edge>
