</edge>
<edge source="CoEvolution" target="ISI">
  <data key="d6">421.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Institute for Scientific Information (ISI) plays a pivotal and multifaceted role in the CoEvolution project, serving as a vital research partner within the project consortium. ISI significantly contributes to the project's objectives, particularly in enhancing artificial intelligence (AI) security and trustworthiness. Its involvement includes the development of comprehensive technical specifications and architectural requirements that are essential for the robustness of networks employed in AI initiatives.

As a lead beneficiary in CoEvolution, ISI manages multiple deliverables related to technical aspects and security, notably leading Deliverable D5.1, which showcases its direct impact on the project's outcomes. In addition to this, ISI takes on a leadership role in scientific coordination, guiding technical discussions and reporting. It is actively engaged in various work packages, notably leading Work Package 1, where it focuses on providing strategic direction to maximize the overall impact of the project.

ISI addresses security vulnerabilities, particularly those related to side channel attacks, by ensuring compliance with legal and ethical standards in AI model deployments. The organization produces crucial security assurance reports that monitor and enhance these AI deployments, promoting secure and ethical practices within the AI landscape. It also facilitates knowledge exchange with other EU-funded projects, which strengthens the overall outcomes of CoEvolution.

In addition to its leadership and coordination responsibilities, ISI develops critical guidelines and provides technical support across various work packages to ensure effective reporting and resolution of technical issues. Through comprehensive efforts, including data collection and modeling to evaluate potential side channel leakage in AI models, ISI is integral to advancing the robustness of machine learning systems within the CoEvolution initiative.</data>
