<edge source="CoEvolution" target="TID">
  <data key="d6">449.0</data>
  <data key="d7">CoEvolution is an innovative collaborative initiative designed to develop privacy-preserving learning systems and decentralized solutions to address the challenges associated with distributed learning. It collaborates closely with TID, an essential organization that provides the technological infrastructure necessary for implementing CoEvolution's strategies effectively. TID's contributions are crucial, as it integrates advanced cybersecurity methodologies and artificial intelligence systems into the project, significantly enhancing CoEvolution's objectives.

Within the CoEvolution consortium, TID employs a peer-to-peer learning approach that emphasizes privacy and security among participants. The organization conducts structured training sessions to familiarize various stakeholders with the project’s outcomes, thereby increasing the overall effectiveness of CoEvolution. TID is also actively engaged in extensive research and development efforts aimed at creating secure learning environments, developing innovative security technologies, and implementing quality assurance management practices.

TID demonstrates a strong commitment to inclusivity by focusing on gender equality throughout the project's management and execution. To further support CoEvolution's overarching goals, TID is responsible for creating an Enablers repository, which includes tools and documentation produced during the project and serves as a vital resource for collaborative research. Additionally, TID is dedicated to developing scalable, privacy-preserving technologies and robust AI models that can withstand adversarial attacks.

Specifically, TID acts as the lead beneficiary for Work Package 4 (WP4), which concentrates on assessing and enhancing AI models. This role involves evaluating various project tasks, ensuring quality assurance, and conducting gender equality assessments within the project structure. TID also oversees the software repository that supports the implementation of tools developed under the CoEvolution project, ensuring adherence to European regulations regarding ethics and data protection.

Overall, TID's extensive involvement and innovative contributions are critical to the success of the CoEvolution project. Its efforts significantly enhance AI security, promote inclusivity and diversity, foster innovation, and strengthen collaborative research frameworks, establishing TID as a leading player within the consortium.</data>
