<edge source="CoEvolution" target="DIE">
  <data key="d6">212.0</data>
  <data key="d7">DIE contributes to the CoEvolution project as the lead beneficiary for security assurance documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;DIE is a key entity in the CoEvolution consortium, serving as both the lead beneficiary and consortium partner. Its significant contributions to the CoEvolution project are pivotal to the project's overall success, particularly in defining the roadmap and research objectives centered on AI model security. DIE plays a crucial role in addressing major challenges related to these objectives through extensive research and resource mobilization efforts.

One of DIE's primary responsibilities is deliverable D5.2, which outlines its involvement in the development of a security repository for the CoEvolution project. This encompasses ensuring security assurance and monitoring throughout the lifecycle of the project. Specifically, DIE leads the data requirements task, which is vital for effective lifecycle management of AI models. This task includes overseeing data collection and management, as well as establishing robust security assurance practices that contribute to the integrity of the project.

In addition to these core responsibilities, DIE is involved in creating a monitoring repository that equips the project with essential tools to maintain the integrity of its initiatives. Their efforts in security assessment and the development of monitoring engines enhance the project by continuously evaluating and testing its framework, ensuring compliance with necessary security standards.

DIE also promotes collaboration with other EU-funded initiatives, which broadens the project's scope and impact. Overall, DIE's multifaceted involvement in the CoEvolution project significantly fortifies its technical and security foundations, reflecting a strong commitment to advancing cybersecurity research in the context of artificial intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;DIE participates in the quality assurance task within the CoEvolution project, focusing on promoting gender equality and risk management.</data>
