<edge source="CoEvolution" target="AVI">
  <data key="d6">246.0</data>
  <data key="d7">AVI is a crucial partner organization within the CoEvolution consortium, significantly advancing cybersecurity technologies in the realm of artificial intelligence (AI). Through its extensive expertise, AVI plays an integral role in fostering ethical standards specifically related to vehicle perception technologies that enhance cyber-resilience.

In the CoEvolution project, AVI oversees important operations such as security testing against adversarial attacks, a critical component of ensuring the robustness of AI models developed under this initiative. As the Lead Beneficiary, AVI is responsible for the integration and evaluation of the CoEvolution framework, leading the development of adversarial attack security testing techniques. This leadership reflects AVI's commitment to ensuring the project achieves its essential milestones, including the management of the Minimum Viable Product (MVP) release.

AVI's contributions also extend to providing vital resources such as simulators and datasets, which actively support the project's research and development efforts. Additionally, AVI engages in intellectual property management, including participating in patent filings related to its innovations. This highlights AVI's commitment to responsible development and innovation within the AI sector.

Overall, AVI's comprehensive involvement in the CoEvolution project encompasses crucial areas like security testing, resource provision, innovation management, and validation processes. This deep engagement not only solidifies AVI's central role in reaching the objectives of the CoEvolution initiative but also enhances ethical practices in AI technology development. Furthermore, AVI's support extends to collaborating on tasks with PAN, underscoring the cooperative spirit that characterizes the project.&lt;SEP&gt;AVI is active in the CoEvolution project as the lead beneficiary for simulator development and MVP delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;AVI is involved as a lead beneficiary in the integration and evaluation of outcomes for the CoEvolution project.</data>
