<edge source="CoEvolution" target="UNICA">
  <data key="d6">251.0</data>
  <data key="d7">CoEvolution is an initiative dedicated to addressing the legal challenges associated with artificial intelligence (AI) technology. A pivotal organization within this consortium is UNICA, which plays a significant role by actively contributing extensive scientific and technical insights that are critical for the success of the project.

One of UNICA’s primary contributions is the SecML library, designed to enhance adversarial robustness in AI models, which integrates seamlessly into the CoEvolution framework. This library strengthens the security measures and overall resilience of AI implementations within the project. In addition to SecML, UNICA is focused on improving security testing practices that reinforce the robustness of AI systems.

UNICA’s involvement is comprehensive, as it not only aids in the development of adversarial attack mitigation tools, but also helps define the project scope of CoEvolution. The organization’s role encompasses the creation of open-source projects, which not only enhances the consortium's capabilities but also promotes collaborative progress among partners.

Moreover, UNICA actively participates in various work packages that focus on data security, context-awareness, and relevant research strategies, ensuring that advanced security measures are ingrained in AI technologies. Through the production of vital scientific reports and participation in research facilitation, UNICA drives essential deliverables for the CoEvolution project.

Overall, UNICA's multifaceted contributions and expertise make it an indispensable partner in the CoEvolution initiative, significantly enhancing the project's focus on AI research and cybersecurity.&lt;SEP&gt;CoEvolution is the project under which UNICA leads specific tasks related to data security and privacy."&lt;option&gt;project leadership, collaboration&lt;SEP&gt;UNICA plays a role in the CoEvolution project as the lead beneficiary for enablers development reports.</data>
