<edge source="CoEvolution" target="UPatras">
  <data key="d6">150.0</data>
  <data key="d7">CoEvolution is a collaborative initiative closely working with the University of Patras (UPatras), which plays a vital and multifaceted role in advancing the project. UPatras contributes its expertise to the H2020 HEIR project and significantly enhances the academic, research, and technological dimensions essential for the success of CoEvolution.

One of the primary responsibilities of UPatras is to lead the development of the minimum viable product (MVP) of an integrated framework, which is crucial for the project's development process. Additionally, UPatras is actively engaged in adversarial attack security testing to improve the robustness of the artificial intelligence models used within CoEvolution. The university also develops synthetic datasets to support various tasks, facilitating effective data utilization under the CoEvolution framework.

Furthermore, UPatras helps in the advancement of the ComDeX architecture, which focuses on enhancing the efficiency of context-aware Internet of Things (IoT) data exchanges. This effort is aligned with CoEvolution's goal of fostering context-awareness in its applications. The university is also involved in implementing strategies related to networked AI systems and enhancing cybersecurity measures, which contribute to the project's overall effectiveness.

Through its diverse contributions, UPatras participates in multiple work packages and deliverables, including deliverable D6.2, solidifying its active involvement in the project's goals. Overall, UPatras's contributions bolster the capabilities and achievements of the CoEvolution project significantly, reflecting its commitment to shaping the research efforts of the CoEvolution consortium.</data>
