<edge source="CoEvolution" target="AI MBOM">
  <data key="d6">327.0</data>
  <data key="d7">AI MBOM is a principal element within the CoEvolution concept, aimed at certifying the trust and security of artificial intelligence systems. As an integral part of the CoEvolution initiative, AI MBOM assists in tracking and ensuring the security of AI models throughout their lifecycle. It provides essential security-related data about the AI models involved in the ecosystem, enhancing transparency, accountability, and security.

Developed within the CoEvolution project, AI MBOM is designed to ensure that AI models are secure, robust, and trustworthy during their operational lifespan. It facilitates effective management of these AI models by offering a structured approach for risk assessment and compliance, allowing for continuous monitoring and improvement. This adaptability helps the models adhere to evolving security standards and promotes trust among stakeholders.

CoEvolution emphasizes the need to track all components of AI systems, conduct comprehensive security assessments, and integrate techniques that guarantee the robustness of these models. Furthermore, AI MBOM enables the exchange of information regarding AI security and the sharing of trusted models, fostering a reliable environment for working with AI systems.

In summary, the CoEvolution project plays a crucial role in developing and managing the AI MBOM framework, which is pivotal for managing AI models and ensuring their security and transparency. This framework significantly impacts the deployment and security of AI technologies, reinforcing trust and robustness in AI operations and integrations, while providing varying levels of access to users and ensuring secure handling. AI MBOM acts as a core component of CoEvolution, enhancing the security and robustness of AI models by documenting AI model structures and assessing their security metrics through a comprehensive risk and security assessment framework.</data>
