<edge source="CoEvolution" target="European Union">
  <data key="d6">120.0</data>
  <data key="d7">CoEvolution is a project dedicated to enhancing AI security frameworks that are currently regulated by the European Union's AI Act. The initiative focuses on addressing deficiencies in existing AI security measures, ensuring robust cybersecurity, and asserting digital sovereignty within technological advancements. CoEvolution aligns its security and risk assessment processes with the European Union's (EU) regulatory efforts related to artificial intelligence safety, which emphasizes ethical compliance throughout its activities.

The project receives vital support from the European Union, which not only serves as the granting authority but also provides essential funding through various grant schemes, facilitating the execution of CoEvolution's objectives. The goals of the project are closely aligned with those of the EU, especially in promoting cybersecurity and leveraging AI technologies to uphold digital sovereignty. Furthermore, CoEvolution engages in a collaborative effort with a range of EU-wide initiatives, reinforcing its commitment to operate within the regulatory frameworks established by the EU, particularly concerning trust and security assurance for AI applications.

In summary, CoEvolution exemplifies a synergistic relationship with the European Union, significantly influenced by its guidelines and regulations, to ensure that AI technologies are developed and deployed safely and ethically.</data>
  <data key="d8">European directives,collaboration,compliance,cybersecurity,cybersecurity initiative,digital sovereignty,ethical compliance,funding source,funding support,outreach,project backing,project compliance,project purpose,project support,regulation,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,regulatory impact,regulatory influence</data>
