<edge source="CoEvolution" target="Secure Multiparty Computation">
  <data key="d6">64.0</data>
  <data key="d7">CoEvolution is an initiative focused on evaluating Secure Multiparty Computation (SMPC) techniques as a strategic defense against potential adversarial attacks within artificial intelligence (AI) systems. The main goals of CoEvolution include ensuring model privacy and integrity, while also investigating how SMPC can enhance the security of AI model communications between clients and servers. The initiative explores various SMPC technologies to further improve the integrity and privacy of AI systems. By incorporating Secure Multiparty Computation, CoEvolution enables collaborative computations that do not compromise the privacy of input data, thereby assessing SMPC as a vital measure for maintaining the integrity of AI and preventing security breaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Secure Multiparty Computation is evaluated in CoEvolution as a means to prevent unauthorized access to AI models.</data>
  <data key="d8">AI security,access control,attack prevention,collaboration,collaborative security,computational privacy,data protection,data security,evaluation,integrity assurance,privacy measures,security evaluation,security measures,security method</data>
