<edge source="CoEvolution" target="EU AI Act">
  <data key="d6">308.0</data>
  <data key="d7">CoEvolution is an organization dedicated to the responsible development of artificial intelligence (AI) applications. It prioritizes safety, trustworthiness, and ethical standards in its practices. CoEvolution's mission closely aligns with the objectives and regulatory frameworks established by the EU AI Act, which is designed to ensure the safe and responsible use of AI technologies in response to identified risks.

To uphold the standards of the EU AI Act, CoEvolution integrates regulatory compliance into its AI framework by implementing a comprehensive compliance strategy that encompasses its operational and development processes. This strategy includes a robust risk analysis framework aimed at addressing safety and trust issues in AI applications, as well as enhancing the resilience and security of its AI systems.

CoEvolution emphasizes the importance of thorough documentation of AI model components and frameworks for risk assessment, showcasing its commitment to maintaining compliance with the stringent regulations set forth in the EU AI Act. The organization’s research objectives are in line with the ethical practices recommended by the Act, contributing positively to the evolving landscape of AI technologies.

Furthermore, CoEvolution’s approach includes a proposed security assessment framework and a decommissioning process that adheres to the regulations for managing high-risk AI applications. This ensures that its operations not only foster responsible AI practices but also reinforce its dedication to ethical standards in AI development.

Overall, CoEvolution plays a pivotal role in promoting compliance and the ethical use of AI technologies while striving to enhance safety and trustworthiness in AI applications, effectively complementing the EU AI Act.</data>
