<edge source="CoEvolution" target="UNIPI">
  <data key="d6">89.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The University of Pisa (UNIPI) plays a pivotal and multifaceted role in the CoEvolution project, focusing on the enhancement of AI model security through advanced incremental training technologies. As a leading participant, UNIPI significantly contributes to various activities and work packages within the project, driving research efforts related to AI technologies. It provides essential components and design knowledge for the AI Toolkit utilized in CoEvolution applications, reinforcing its importance in the project’s infrastructure.

In addition to its contributions to AI model development, UNIPI is instrumental in cybersecurity initiatives, ensuring that the project addresses critical safety concerns associated with AI systems. The university's ongoing projects related to incremental learning and security defenses are particularly crucial for advancing the overall objectives of CoEvolution.

Moreover, UNIPI supports the maintenance of open-source projects within the CoEvolution consortium, bringing in expertise for project maintenance and providing access to valuable open-source code. Through its active participation, UNIPI not only enriches the CoEvolution project with academic insights but also fosters collaborative research efforts, thereby solidifying its integral position in the initiative's continued success.&lt;SEP&gt;UNIPI plays a role in the CoEvolution consortium through its involvement in open-source initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;UNIPI's participation in various work packages indicates its contributions to the CoEvolution project.</data>
  <data key="d8">9,academic participation,collaboration,consortium contribution,consortium partnership,contribution,leadership,open-source maintenance,organizational effort,project contribution,project involvement,project support,project synergy,research collaboration,research contribution,research participation,resource sharing,technical support</data>
