<edge source="Horizon Europe" target="CoEvolution Consortium Agreement">
  <data key="d6">120.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The CoEvolution Consortium Agreement is a formal framework established in accordance with the regulations of Horizon Europe, a funding program aimed at supporting research and innovation projects across Europe. Specifically crafted for use within the Horizon Europe funding structure, the CoEvolution Consortium Agreement highlights the established connection between the CoEvolution Consortium and the Horizon Europe initiative. This agreement defines the collaborative methods and access rights for the entities involved, facilitating the sharing of results and cooperative efforts among participants. 

As part of a project proposal submitted to Horizon Europe for funding and support, the CoEvolution Consortium Agreement aims to improve research and innovation collaboration. It is tailored to detail cooperation among parties specific to a project funded by Horizon Europe, thereby ensuring that the collaborative projects adhere to the program’s standards and objectives. Furthermore, the agreement operates under the guidelines set forth by Horizon Europe, solidifying the collaborative terms for all participating entities involved in this initiative.</data>
  <data key="d8">EU initiatives,EU program,collaboration,funding,funding framework,funding program,project basis,project collaboration,project framework,project funding,project regulation,regulatory foundation,regulatory framework,research collaboration,research funding,research initiative,research program,specific project agreement</data>
