<edge source="General Assembly" target="Defaulting Party">
  <data key="d6">52.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Defaulting Party's breaches are addressed by the General Assembly, which decides on actions to remedy the situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The General Assembly holds the authority to declare a party as a Defaulting Party if that party breaches the obligations outlined in the Consortium Agreement. It is responsible for identifying such Defaulting Parties who fail to adhere to the terms of the agreement. Furthermore, the General Assembly has the power to terminate the participation of any Defaulting Party within the consortium as a consequence of this failure to comply with the agreed-upon obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;The General Assembly has the authority to decide on the termination of participation for a Defaulting Party.</data>
  <data key="d8">accountability,authority,compliance,decision-making,enforcement,governance,oversight</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-f27907e0f1cca34615e2743e211e3915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc042244536a2c477c732ec854a8e51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f737a86267a87605168fd1ae879e6180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d78b6916c07894b52e49fb0226ca1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-561ef15ef8c11dbe41ee0269571778b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ad85c72a1fdaf22b42cfab6d99532ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-924177c0e0f362a235f652bd1017e028</data>
