<edge source="Consortium Agreement" target="Grant Agreement">
  <data key="d6">43.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Consortium Agreement and the Grant Agreement are closely related documents that govern a collaborative project involving multiple partners. The Consortium Agreement is aligned with the Grant Agreement and serves as a formalization of the collaboration structure necessary for the project's execution. It establishes the collaborative framework under which the obligations and responsibilities of all partners are defined and managed.

The Grant Agreement, on the other hand, outlines the terms for funding and specifies the conditions under which the Consortium Agreement operates. It details the roles of the parties involved and provides the basis for enforcing the Consortium Agreement. Thus, both agreements work in tandem, with the Grant Agreement setting the financial and operational guidelines and the Consortium Agreement structuring the collaborative efforts among the partners.</data>
  <data key="d8">collaboration,contractual relations,contractual relationship,funding,legal framework,project execution,project governance,project obligations,terms of cooperation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-8c12a8ce9dbccebc341927add84979a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d70be6cc96049933abcbd5d9cfc8374&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a48cfc1f38ba5b30413053bbdefda5ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2804b4b4d78b4e8ad4bf46a4086bc654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8725d84f8b773d46e6200fdd9fab9de7</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755419453</data>
</edge>
