<edge source="Background" target="Access Rights">
  <data key="d6">33.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Access Rights are a framework established to regulate the distribution and utilization of Background information within a project. They are specifically defined in relation to the Background data and information that is essential for effectively exploiting the results of the project. Access Rights dictate how each Party can utilize the Background information supplied by other parties, thereby ensuring orderly use and collaboration. Furthermore, these rights extend to include permissions regarding Background materials that may be leveraged in conjunction with the project results for exploitation purposes.</data>
  <data key="d8">data rights,permission,permissions,prior knowledge,project guidelines,project implementation,utilization</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-496ff2c08e0ff26b59002ce18b9a5411&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77f4d0db61ea04c6dd99be408590bb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f27907e0f1cca34615e2743e211e3915&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bc736562ef02e369a2653a250fd668b</data>
