<edge source="AVL" target="PAN">
  <data key="d6">60.0</data>
  <data key="d7">AVL has replaced PAN in the CoEvolution project, marking a significant shift in project partnerships. Following PAN's decision not to participate, AVL assumed responsibilities previously held by PAN, leading to necessary adjustments in AVL's tasks to accommodate the duties that were left unfulfilled. This transition underscores AVL's direct involvement in project management and illustrates their adaptive approach to addressing project changes. AVL's engagement specifically aims to fill the gaps left by PAN, demonstrating a collaborative response to project needs and an effective accommodation of tasks within the consortium.&lt;SEP&gt;AVL is accommodating the tasks that PAN has left out, indicating a direct collaborative relationship in task management.</data>
  <data key="d8">6,change,collaboration,collaborative effort,consortium changes,partner replacement,partner transition,project collaboration,project management,project partnership,resource management,task accommodation,task reassignment</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-c1840a2aa861c08b15185d927867134a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827c0e1b05bc9eac5d2bbfb266ef6562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fb0f79a7142225a7d2dfaedc44c958&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f2e8aebdfb355f313ea068cac55423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3daedd8cfb8dad5cd7a0132b3057fb6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84670dae929f0474fd75c1904113c7d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad8c45296704b976d9974fb6ccbcc41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-672abb4b4d866c235db2385a6641554e</data>
