<edge source="AEGIS" target="SAP">
  <data key="d6">46.0</data>
  <data key="d7">References to SAP have been removed from project documents, which alters the context of AEGIS's project management.&lt;SEP&gt;The project dynamics between AEGIS and SAP have evolved, leading to the redistribution of responsibilities as part of a restructuring effort. SAP's previous roles are being reassigned to AEGIS and other partners, with AEGIS now taking over certain aspects of SAP's work in the management of project tasks and deliverables. Specifically, SAP has transferred 12 project managers (PMs) to AEGIS while also assigning additional PMs for targeted tasks. This transition signifies a clear distribution of responsibilities, with AEGIS assuming some of SAP’s duties in designated work packages.&lt;SEP&gt;The redistribution of work in the CoEvolution project indicates a functional relationship between SAP and AEGIS.</data>
  <data key="d8">collaboration,organizational collaboration,organizational restructuring,organizational shift,project adjustment,project management,project restructuring,resource allocation,resource distribution,stakeholder reduction,task redistribution,work redistribution</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-827c0e1b05bc9eac5d2bbfb266ef6562&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f2e8aebdfb355f313ea068cac55423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c3ab8cb1038a2d7402e7c20f7922fb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84670dae929f0474fd75c1904113c7d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad8c45296704b976d9974fb6ccbcc41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fd8590e514e02237067258b84c6af2</data>
