<edge source="AI Models" target="Adversarial Attacks">
  <data key="d6">39.0</data>
  <data key="d7">AI Models are increasingly vulnerable to Adversarial Attacks, which are designed to disrupt their functionality and integrity by injecting misleading data. These attacks exploit various vulnerabilities within AI models through methods such as data poisoning and model extraction. Given the significant risks posed by Adversarial Attacks, CoEvolution has developed techniques and guidelines aimed at mitigating these threats. The work of CoEvolution emphasizes the importance of safeguarding AI Models against the challenges presented by these attacks, ensuring their reliability and security in real-world applications.</data>
  <data key="d8">model security,model vulnerability,protection measures,security threat,security threats,threat awareness,vulnerability</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-42b64505cb57d831fa92eb10404f3632&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e396002be0503d0e0baac803477dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db75b2cab1362b7796ff2a8753c4245e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d294af5576309a3fad1a02ca2551b6e2</data>
