<edge source="Federated Learning (FL)" target="P4L">
  <data key="d6">33.0</data>
  <data key="d7">P4L is an innovative alternative approach to Federated Learning (FL) that aims to advance the existing paradigm by addressing its limitations. Unlike traditional Federated Learning, P4L does not depend on differential privacy measures or centralized systems. Instead, it emphasizes a decentralized learning architecture, allowing for collaborative learning without the need for a central server. Through these enhancements, P4L seeks to improve privacy and remove reliance on external systems, further fostering a robust collaborative framework in decentralized learning environments.</data>
  <data key="d8">9,alternative methodology,decentralization,decentralized learning,innovation,privacy improvement,privacy preservation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-fdb47fa58e505f36db27509e998c725c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7d7dd122ed2c0928bca9de4f77ffb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d7f2c53ed2b4b73ced4214f41c6193a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71006e55cf73aa373312d69b3b443261</data>
