  <data key="d11">1755419944</data>
</edge>
<edge source="P4L" target="Differential Privacy">
  <data key="d6">45.0</data>
  <data key="d7">"P4L provides an alternative to Differential Privacy, aiming to maintain data utility while preserving user privacy without centralized systems.")&lt;SEP&gt;P4L aims to address issues associated with existing methods, such as Differential Privacy, which often diminish the utility of data when shared during training. Specifically, P4L proposes a collaborative learning solution that operates independently of differential privacy approaches. Rather than relying on these common techniques for protecting data during the sharing of gradients, P4L presents an alternative strategy for privacy preservation, functioning without the constraints that typically come from Differential Privacy. This approach seeks to enhance the utility of shared data while still ensuring user data protection.&lt;SEP&gt;P4L seeks to function without relying on Differential Privacy, which often reduces the utility of shared data in collaborative learning."&lt;&lt;|"data privacy, collaborative learning</data>
  <data key="d8">7,alternative methods,data privacy techniques,data utility,method contrast,privacy enhancement,privacy focus,privacy preservation,privacy protection,system design,utility concerns</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-a460a143968d4ed5c18c7a4aba2f1a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5092e32b5e7f6b1dc6a316b8941ea4c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb47fa58e505f36db27509e998c725c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7d7dd122ed2c0928bca9de4f77ffb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-125a6d8c6730e236d423f077d38dc767&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71006e55cf73aa373312d69b3b443261</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755425989</data>
</edge>
<edge source="P4L" target="Partial Homomorphic Encryption (HE)">
  <data key="d6">26.0</data>
  <data key="d7">P4L aims to utilize Partial Homomorphic Encryption during training to mitigate information leakage in shared gradients.&lt;SEP&gt;P4L utilizes Partial Homomorphic Encryption to secure shared gradients, ensuring confidentiality in collaborative learning systems.&lt;SEP&gt;P4L incorporates Partial Homomorphic Encryption to maintain confidentiality during the sharing of model gradients.</data>
  <data key="d8">data privacy,data protection,data security,encryption use,security,security method</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-c6e06c3c78a2faf8db92a10b50f161ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a460a143968d4ed5c18c7a4aba2f1a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdb47fa58e505f36db27509e998c725c</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755424361</data>
</edge>
<edge source="P4L" target="Asynchronous Decentralized Collaborative Learning">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">P4L facilitates Asynchronous Decentralized Collaborative Learning, enabling users to engage without relying on a centralized server.</data>
  <data key="d8">collaboration,decentralized learning processes</data>
