<edge source="RAGRE" target="GDPR">
  <data key="d6">54.0</data>
  <data key="d7">RAGRE is an organization that places significant emphasis on compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) across its operations, particularly in the assessment and management of risks associated with artificial intelligence (AI) models. RAGRE systematically integrates GDPR guidelines into its risk evaluation processes, ensuring that data privacy regulations are upheld throughout the development and implementation of AI technologies. By aligning its risk assessments with GDPR, RAGRE effectively manages risks related to data privacy, safeguarding personal data and maintaining regulatory adherence. The organization prioritizes the incorporation of GDPR compliance in all its risk assessments, reinforcing its commitment to data privacy and protection during AI deployment.</data>
  <data key="d8">compliance,data privacy,data protection,legal compliance,legislation,regulatory compliance,risk assessment</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-3d31a9f46c18f75b8bffad97afd44ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c366ab8df2f44a9f385a6868c2d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f7c6a9a08e9c022ee9a774571a1ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32c9082aac6fd2a45950240834514168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f735046fbbdc14f326a8f041cac6de9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755426032</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAGRE" target="Digital Services Act (DSA)">
  <data key="d6">33.0</data>
  <data key="d7">RAGRE aligns its risk evaluation framework with the principles outlined in the Digital Services Act (DSA) to ensure the responsible usage of artificial intelligence (AI). In this context, RAGRE considers the implications of the DSA as it assesses the risks associated with AI deployment. Furthermore, the organization evaluates these risks as part of its comprehensive risk management practices, taking into account the DSA requirements in its assessments for ethical AI deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;RAGRE evaluates the implications of the Digital Services Act on AI model assessments and compliance strategies.</data>
  <data key="d8">ethical considerations,ethical standards,legal compliance,legislation impact,regulatory alignment,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,risk assessment,risk evaluation,risk management</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-3d31a9f46c18f75b8bffad97afd44ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32c9082aac6fd2a45950240834514168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f7c6a9a08e9c022ee9a774571a1ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755426033</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAGRE" target="EU AI Act">
  <data key="d6">82.0</data>
  <data key="d7">RAGRE is an organization that focuses on aligning its risk assessments with the EU AI Act to ensure compliance with emerging legislation related to artificial intelligence technologies. It is dedicated to integrating the requirements of the EU AI Act into its evaluation processes, reflecting a commitment to both regulatory adherence and ethical considerations. RAGRE actively evaluates the risks associated with AI models in light of the proposed regulations of the EU AI Act, promoting ethical practices within the field of artificial intelligence.

To enhance this alignment and support compliance efforts, RAGRE has established a regulatory sandbox specifically for AI models under assessment. This sandbox provides a controlled environment for testing AI technologies, allowing for comprehensive evaluations while ensuring they meet the necessary regulations and standards. Through these initiatives, RAGRE demonstrates its proactive approach to navigating the evolving regulatory landscape surrounding AI technologies, underscoring its commitment to responsible and ethical AI development.</data>
  <data key="d8">AI ethics,AI regulation,assessment framework,ethical AI,ethical assessment,future compliance,legal framework,legislation compliance,legislative alignment,regulatory alignment,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,risk assessment</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b73d4bb0dd8d885f8eae5c8842c1ea98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d31a9f46c18f75b8bffad97afd44ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c366ab8df2f44a9f385a6868c2d6be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32c9082aac6fd2a45950240834514168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5f7c6a9a08e9c022ee9a774571a1ae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f735046fbbdc14f326a8f041cac6de9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755426030</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAGRE" target="STR Testing/Assessment Engine">
  <data key="d6">43.0</data>
  <data key="d7">RAGRE employs the STR Testing/Assessment Engine as a critical component for conducting security testing on AI models. This engine works as an extension of RAGRE, focused on implementing adversarial attack testing. It draws upon risk evaluations performed by RAGRE to enhance its security assessments, thereby ensuring a comprehensive approach to evaluating the security of AI models. Overall, the STR Testing/Assessment Engine functions within the framework established by RAGRE to improve the robustness of security testing protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;The STR Testing/Assessment Engine provides security testing results that serve as evidence for RAGRE's assessments.</data>
  <data key="d8">adversarial testing,evidence,extended functionality,functional collaboration,organizational integration,risk evaluation,security enhancement,security testing,security validation,testing process</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b73d4bb0dd8d885f8eae5c8842c1ea98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2a45c222140df04434355f127ac357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7cd78f3c47313f00197d5ea64555dcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755424381</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAGRE" target="Technical Evaluation Engine">
  <data key="d6">43.0</data>
  <data key="d7">RAGRE collaborates with the Technical Evaluation Engine to ensure that AI models meet regulatory and industry standards throughout the risk assessment process. The Technical Evaluation Engine is an integral part of the RAGRE system, utilized after RAGRE conducts risk assessments to confirm compliance with established standards. It provides rigorous evaluations that align AI models with regulatory requirements, supporting RAGRE's mission to evaluate AI models against identified risks according to those standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The RAGRE utilizes the results from the Technical Evaluation Engine to assess AI models against regulatory standards and risks.</data>
  <data key="d8">collaboration,compliance,evaluation,evaluation process,organizational function,regulatory compliance,risk evaluation</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-b73d4bb0dd8d885f8eae5c8842c1ea98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2a45c222140df04434355f127ac357&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b47fa4d5e8d983c7d35feee9e94172d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58c7cbb33ab30b7a655c9e6abee10258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1b1bd730a128c6aa8545dadc45ad37</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1755425118</data>
</edge>
