<edge source="granting authority" target="beneficiary">
  <data key="d6">35.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The granting authority plays a crucial role in overseeing the financial management and compliance of beneficiaries who receive grants. It has the authority to approve or reject expenses submitted by beneficiaries, ensuring that they comply with the established terms of the grant. Additionally, the granting authority is responsible for managing the funds allocated to beneficiaries, which includes setting the terms for both payment and recovery. Through these actions, the granting authority maintains a relationship with beneficiaries by not only providing grants but also ensuring adherence to the agreed-upon terms and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d8">compliance oversight,financial responsibility,financing,fund management,funding relationship,grant management,oversight</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-153d0d25b1dc6cfa0bcf7a7947b40d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a078d51839f156c28b044d78b32cd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d24cc4a2a88c7af17c3b59914ddb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1e6845be0998259ad41a50c2e648ae7</data>
